{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:22:58.224Z","ordinal":35027,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5ba939de-f1c2-489d-b805-1e535e020493","process_id":"96707","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage|acceptance.json|fake provider|NEXUS_EVAL' eval cli scripts docs/v1.1.0 | head -n 120; sed -n '1,240p' eval/package_runtime.test.mjs; sed -n '18,34p' eval/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage|acceptance.json|fake provider|NEXUS_EVAL' eval cli scripts docs/v1.1.0","query":"versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage|acceptance.json|fake provider|NEXUS_EVAL","path":"eval"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' eval/package_runtime.test.mjs","name":"package_runtime.test.mjs","path":"eval/package_runtime.test.mjs"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '18,34p' eval/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"eval/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:78:- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:14:- **AC5:** Run the exact candidate CLI against a local fake provider that captures the actual request after prompt construction; record one candidate invocation and validator/scorer result for each of the six manifest-declared benchmark task IDs, with zero skipped or missing tasks. Pin the candidate SHA, dataset version/split, and the SHA-256 recomputed from the final integrated `core-v1/manifest.json`; do not reuse the prior branch's `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43` as current evidence. Test/evidence: `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. This establishes execution coverage and request isolation, not model quality.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:16:**Out of scope:** Modifying oracle semantics, held-out corpus data or custody; changing evaluator scoring; packaging the runtime; live inference against a real model/provider. AC5 uses the actual candidate CLI and prompt path with a local deterministic fake provider; the fake provider captures the request and returns a fixture response so the evaluator can score every declared benchmark task.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:20:**Files claimed/current ownership:** The plan file and `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` are claimed by root on `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. The WP-1103 umbrella claim covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`. Runner claims on the same branch cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and `eval/dataset.test.mjs`; that `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim spans chunks 1 and 2 sequentially. The G1.1-2 evidence is claimed at `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`; write it only after the exact candidate CLI run completes and the final manifest hash is recomputed. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:26:3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:35:**Risk / unknown:** The current runner merges example and oracle fields into an evaluator-side task record before launching the candidate. The exact prompt/provider request and candidate filesystem/mount boundary must be observed without a live model; the fake provider/request capture must establish the actual CLI prompt path, and filesystem checks must establish access denial rather than mere omission from the staged copy. The benchmark evidence must identify the exact candidate SHA, dataset version, split, manifest SHA-256, denominator and each task invocation/result.\ncli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:14:  const workspaceRoot = process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT;\ncli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:16:  const runtimeRoot = process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT;\ncli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:18:  const runAs = process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUN_AS ?? \"nobody\";\neval/runner_api.mjs:31:    if (task.t4Fixture) env.NEXUS_EVAL_TOOL_RECEIPTS = \"1\";\neval/runner_api.mjs:154:    fs.writeFileSync(apiKeyFile, `NEXUS_EVAL_API_KEY=REDACTED, { encoding: \"utf8\", mode: 0o600, flag: \"wx\" });\neval/runner_api.mjs:156:    result.apiKey = REDACTED file: apiKeyFile, var: \"NEXUS_EVAL_API_KEY\" };\neval/dataset.test.mjs:216:    assert.deepEqual(observed.config.apiKey, { file: path.join(path.dirname(observed.configPath), \"api-key.env\"), var: \"NEXUS_EVAL_API_KEY\" });\neval/dataset.test.mjs:219:    assert.equal(observed.credential, \"NEXUS_EVAL_API_KEY=REDACTED;\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1070:  const workspaceRoot = process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT ?? \"/dev/shm\";\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1090:  if (process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT) assert.equal(isolation, null, \"the dedicated test tmpfs and kernel resource contract must pass preflight\");\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1092:  if (process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT) {\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1135:  const workspaceRoot = process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT ?? \"/dev/shm\";\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1157:    if (process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT) {\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1211:  const workspaceRoot = process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT ?? \"/dev/shm\";\ncli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1261:    const workspaceRoot = process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT ?? profile.workspaceRoot;\ncli/test/check_requirements.test.ts:54:  const recordPath = path.join(supportRoot, \"rc-acceptance.json\");\ncli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts:18:  'echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"',\ncli/test/release_workflow_parity.test.ts:19:  'echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT=$runtime_root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"',\ncli/src/core/app.ts:177:    if (process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TOOL_RECEIPTS === \"1\") this.agent.clearEvaluationToolReceipts();\ncli/src/core/app.ts:317:      ...(process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TOOL_RECEIPTS === \"1\"\ncli/src/agent.ts:4964:    const workspaceAvailableBeforeBytes = toolName === \"run_command\" && process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TOOL_RECEIPTS === \"1\"\ncli/src/agent.ts:4980:    if (toolName === \"run_command\" && actor === \"agent\" && process.env.NEXUS_EVAL_TOOL_RECEIPTS === \"1\") {\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport http from \"node:http\";\nimport { spawn, spawnSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\nimport { stageEvaluatorRuntime, EVAL_RUNTIME_FILES } from \"../scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs\";\n\nconst expectedRuntimeFiles = [\n  \"eval/run.mjs\", \"eval/validate.mjs\", \"eval/t4_fixtures.mjs\", \"eval/isolate.mjs\",\n  \"eval/hide_oracle.cjs\", \"eval/hide_oracle.py\", \"eval/unlink_then_exec.sh\",\n  \"eval/agent_sandbox.mjs\", \"eval/model_proxy.mjs\", \"eval/score.mjs\", \"eval/dataset.mjs\",\n  \"eval/runner_integrity.mjs\", \"eval/runner_api.mjs\", \"eval/oracle.mjs\", \"eval/infra.mjs\",\n  \"eval/workspace.mjs\", \"eval/resources.mjs\", \"eval/cgroup_supervisor.mjs\", \"eval/t3.mjs\",\n  \"eval/hardened_check.mjs\", \"eval/toolchain-versions.json\", \"eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs\",\n];\n\ntest(\"evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files\", () => {\n  assert.deepEqual(EVAL_RUNTIME_FILES, expectedRuntimeFiles);\n  const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-runtime-package-\"));\n  const source = path.join(root, \"source\");\n  const packageRoot = path.join(root, \"package\");\n  try {\n    for (const file of expectedRuntimeFiles) {\n      const sourceFile = path.join(source, file);\n      fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(sourceFile), { recursive: true });\n      fs.writeFileSync(sourceFile, `runtime:${file}\\n`);\n    }\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(source, \"eval\", \"datasets\", \"core-v1\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(source, \"eval\", \"datasets\", \"core-v1\", \"oracles.jsonl\"), \"secret oracle\\n\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(source, \"eval\", \"tasks\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(source, \"eval\", \"tasks\", \"held-out.json\"), \"held-out\\n\");\n\n    stageEvaluatorRuntime(source, packageRoot);\n\n    for (const file of expectedRuntimeFiles) {\n      assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(packageRoot, file), \"utf8\"), `runtime:${file}\\n`, file);\n    }\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(packageRoot, \"eval\", \"datasets\")), false);\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(packageRoot, \"eval\", \"tasks\")), false);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"evaluator runtime staging fails when an allowlisted module is missing\", () => {\n  const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-eval-runtime-missing-\"));\n  try {\n    assert.throws(() => stageEvaluatorRuntime(root, path.join(root, \"package\")), /required evaluator runtime module is missing/);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout\", { skip: process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT ? false : \"set NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT to a freshly built package\" }, async () => {\n  const packageRoot = fs.realpathSync(process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT);\n  const sourceRoot = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\n  assert.equal(packageRoot === sourceRoot || packageRoot.startsWith(`${sourceRoot}${path.sep}`), false, \"package must be staged outside the source checkout\");\n  const outside = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-installed-eval-smoke-\"));\n  const dataset = path.join(outside, \"dataset\");\n  const outputDir = path.join(outside, \"score.json.artifacts\");\n  fs.mkdirSync(dataset);\n  try {\n    const examples = \"\";\n    const oracles = \"\";\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \"examples.jsonl\"), examples);\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \"oracles.jsonl\"), oracles);\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dataset, \"manifest.json\"), `${JSON.stringify({\n      schemaVersion: 1,\n      name: \"empty-package-smoke\",\n      version: \"1.0.0\",\n      domains: [],\n      splits: { regression: { count: 0 }, benchmark: { count: 0 } },\n      files: {\n        \"examples.jsonl\": createHash(\"sha256\").update(examples).digest(\"hex\"),\n        \"oracles.jsonl\": createHash(\"sha256\").update(oracles).digest(\"hex\"),\n      },\n      tasks: {},\n    }, null, 2)}\\n`);\n\n    const launcher = path.join(packageRoot, \"bin\", \"nexus\");\n    const help = spawnSync(launcher, [\"eval\", \"--help\"], {\n      cwd: outside,\n      encoding: \"utf8\",\n      env: { PATH: process.env.PATH ?? \"/usr/bin:/bin\", HOME: outside, NEXUS_HOME: packageRoot },\n      timeout: 30_000,\n    });\n    assert.equal(help.status, 0, `${help.stdout}${help.stderr}`);\n    assert.match(help.stdout, /--dataset <path>/);\n    assert.match(help.stdout, /--split <name>/);\n\n    const evalRun = spawnSync(launcher, [\n      \"eval\", \"--dataset\", dataset, \"--split\", \"benchmark\", \"--runs\", \"1\", \"--output\", path.join(outside, \"score.json\"),\n    ], {\n      cwd: outside,\n      encoding: \"utf8\",\n      env: {\n        PATH: process.env.PATH ?? \"/usr/bin:/bin\",\n        HOME: outside,\n        NEXUS_HOME: packageRoot,\n        LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT: \"http://127.0.0.1:1/v1\",\n        LOCAL_LLM_MODEL: \"package-smoke\",\n      },\n      timeout: 30_000,\n    });\n    assert.equal(evalRun.status, 0, `${evalRun.stdout}${evalRun.stderr}`);\n    const score = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(outside, \"score.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    assert.equal(score.score.totals.runs, 0);\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(outputDir, \"results.jsonl\")), true);\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(outputDir, \"score.json\")), true);\n    assert.equal(fs.statSync(path.join(outside, \"score.json\")).mode & 0o777, 0o600);\n    assert.equal(fs.statSync(path.join(outputDir, \"score.json\")).mode & 0o777, 0o600);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(outside, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"installed package launches a non-empty candidate without mounting evaluator code\", { timeout: 120_000, skip: process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT ? false : \"set NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT to a freshly built package\" }, async () => {\n  const packageRoot = fs.realpathSync(process.env.NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT);\n  const sourceRoot = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"..\");\n  assert.equal(packageRoot === sourceRoot || packageRoot.startsWith(`${sourceRoot}${path.sep}`), false, \"package must be staged outside the source checkout\");\n  const outside = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"nexus-installed-eval-candidate-\"));\n  const dataset = path.join(outside, \"dataset\");\n  fs.cpSync(path.join(sourceRoot, \"eval\", \"datasets\", \"core-v1\"), dataset, { recursive: true });\n  const requests = [];\n  const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {\n    if (req.method === \"GET\" && req.url?.endsWith(\"/models\")) {\n      res.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" });\n      res.end(JSON.stringify({ data: [{ id: \"package-smoke\" }] }));\n      return;\n    }\n    let raw = \"\";\n    req.on(\"data\", (chunk) => { raw += chunk; });\n    req.on(\"end\", () => {\n      const body = JSON.parse(raw);\n      requests.push(body);\n      res.writeHead(200, { \"content-type\": \"text/event-stream\" });\n      const frame = (value) => `data: ${JSON.stringify(value)}\\n\\n`;\n      if (requests.length === 1) {\n        res.end(frame({ choices: [{ index: 0, delta: { tool_calls: [{ index: 0, id: \"write-math\", type: \"function\", function: { name: \"write_file\", arguments: JSON.stringify({ path: \"math.js\", content: \"exports.add = (a, b) => a + b;\\n\" }) } }] } }] }) + frame({ choices: [{ index: 0, delta: {}, finish_reason: \"tool_calls\" }] }) + \"data: [DONE]\\n\\n\");\n      } else {\n        res.end(frame({ choices: [{ index: 0, delta: { content: \"Implemented math.js.\" } }] }) + frame({ choices: [{ index: 0, delta: {}, finish_reason: \"stop\" }] }) + \"data: [DONE]\\n\\n\");\n      }\n    });\n  });\n  await new Promise((resolve) => server.listen(0, \"127.0.0.1\", resolve));\n  const address = server.address();\n  assert.ok(address && typeof address === \"object\");\n  const launcher = path.join(packageRoot, \"bin\", \"nexus\");\n  const child = spawn(launcher, [\"eval\", \"--dataset\", dataset, \"--split\", \"regression\", \"--runs\", \"1\", \"--max-steps\", \"3\", \"--output\", path.join(outside, \"score.json\")], {\n    cwd: outside,\n    env: { PATH: process.env.PATH ?? \"/usr/bin:/bin\", HOME: outside, NEXUS_HOME: packageRoot, LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT: `http://127.0.0.1:${address.port}/v1`, LOCAL_LLM_MODEL: \"package-smoke\" },\n    stdio: [\"ignore\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"],\n  });\n  let stdout = \"\";\n  let stderr = \"\";\n  child.stdout.setEncoding(\"utf8\").on(\"data\", (chunk) => { stdout += chunk; });\n  child.stderr.setEncoding(\"utf8\").on(\"data\", (chunk) => { stderr += chunk; });\n  let timer;\n  try {\n    const status = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      timer = setTimeout(() => child.kill(\"SIGTERM\"), 100_000);\n      child.once(\"error\", reject);\n      child.once(\"close\", resolve);\n    });\n    clearTimeout(timer);\n    assert.equal(status, 0, `${stdout}${stderr}`);\n    assert.ok(requests.length >= 1, `installed candidate must reach the deterministic provider; stdout=${stdout}\\nstderr=${stderr}`);\n    assert.match(JSON.stringify(requests[0].messages), /Add math\\.js exporting add/);\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(outside, \"score.json.artifacts\", \"results.jsonl\")), true);\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(outside, \"score.json.artifacts\", \"score.json\")), true);\n    const artifactScore = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(outside, \"score.json.artifacts\", \"score.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    assert.equal(artifactScore.totals.crashed, 0, JSON.stringify(artifactScore));\n    assert.equal(artifactScore.rows.find((row) => row.task === \"selftest-add\")?.correct, 1, JSON.stringify(artifactScore));\n  } finally {\n    clearTimeout(timer);\n    if (child.exitCode === null) child.kill(\"SIGKILL\");\n    await new Promise((resolve) => server.close(resolve));\n    fs.rmSync(outside, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\n```bash\nnexus eval --dataset /path/to/core-v1 --split benchmark --runs 1 \\\n  --isolated-home --output ./results/benchmark.json\n```\n\nThe dataset path must be a versioned dataset directory. The installed command loads its runner from the package named by\n`NEXUS_HOME`; it does not fall back to evaluator code in a development checkout. The score file is created with\nowner-only permissions, and per-task run artifacts are written beside it under `<output>.artifacts`. The legacy\n`nexus eval <dataset-file> --limit N` form remains available for file-based benchmark datasets. `--limit` is not\nsupported for versioned dataset directories; select `--split` or provide a dataset containing the desired task set.\n\nEach run uses a frozen copy of the task tree, a fresh workspace and `HOME`, and a unique output directory. The agent\nreceives only its workspace, isolated home, selected read-only runtime files, and a run-scoped token for a local proxy;\nthe real gateway credential stays in the harness process. The candidate runs in Bubblewrap user, PID and network\nnamespaces, with nested user namespaces disabled. Legacy development tasks may still use `hidden: { dir, into, command }`;\nthose commands execute against the candidate workspace after the agent exits and are **not safe for qualification**, because\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":155988688}},"started_at_ms":1793607777065,"completed_at_ms":1793607778221}}
