{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:42:01.647Z","ordinal":35702,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a19b6c-322e-7640-b50d-5ac85569f301","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**REQUEST_CHANGES** for the acceptance test’s oracle-leak check.\n\nThe six-task record matches the dataset IDs, and I independently verified the archive, launcher, CLI bundle, core binary, and manifest hashes. However, [package_runtime.test.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/eval/package_runtime.test.mjs:130) only rejects `\"/hidden/\"`; the current oracle commands use relative paths such as `hidden/csv.hidden.test.js`, so this check would miss their disclosure. Check for `hidden/` or compare captured requests against serialized oracle data.\n\nAlso, [package_runtime.test.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/eval/package_runtime.test.mjs:161) overwrites an existing acceptance artifact. Use exclusive creation or candidate-specific evidence paths to preserve prior evidence.\n\nI made no edits and ran no tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","create_time":1793608921.6468577,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1538}}
