{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:43:10.396Z","ordinal":35738,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016ae84d1916d881a389d6a3add07290b3","status":"completed","call_id":"call_d2bddcac2bf24c99984c5393573e25c0","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\\n-- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent, while reporting no other source-level correctness/security blocker. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending with the evidence artifact attached.\\n+- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in candidate-specific `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json`. The earlier generic `acceptance.json` is retained unchanged as superseded evidence; the test writes candidate evidence exclusively and rejects relative `hidden/...` command paths as well as full hidden validator commands in captured requests. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\\n+- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","create_time":1793608985.0906208}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:43:10.428Z","ordinal":35739,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-05681a15-7e6c-44af-b89d-f8961a1820a7","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -70,4 +70,4 @@\n - **AC5 red/green:** The first strengthened run failed because the mock returned JSON while the client requested SSE (`INFERENCE_FAILED: stream_incomplete`). After switching to the retrieved SSE contract and setting `--workspace` to an isolated empty directory (so evaluator discovery cannot run this repository's test suite), `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` passed 7/7; the non-empty `--limit 1` case confirmed exactly one completion request containing the first prompt and not the second.\n-- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\n-- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent, while reporting no other source-level correctness/security blocker. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending with the evidence artifact attached.\n+- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in candidate-specific `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json`. The earlier generic `acceptance.json` is retained unchanged as superseded evidence; the test writes candidate evidence exclusively and rejects relative `hidden/...` command paths as well as full hidden validator commands in captured requests. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\n+- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793608990427,"completed_at_ms":1793608990428}}
