{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:26:02.696Z","ordinal":36748,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19b94-7ec8-79e3-a46e-e392de9e63b2","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...784 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-02 9:26am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (19,102t read) | 97,218t work | 80% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\nS2059 WP-1104 Full Suite Gate Monitoring — Fourth Suite Run Active, Work State Updated to GREEN Phase (Nov 2, 7:40 AM)\nS2061 WP-1104 Full Suite Gate Monitoring — Fourth Suite Run at ~19.5 Minutes, T3 Evaluator Tests Passed (Nov 2, 7:52 AM)\n27142 8:22a ○ core-v1 Dataset Manifest: 7 Tasks, 1 Regression + 6 Benchmark Split\n27143 \" ○ eval/package_runtime.test.mjs Non-Empty Candidate Test Uses Async Spawn with In-Process Fake Provider\n27144 8:23a ⚖ COORDINATOR_RULING: WP-1104 AC4/AC5 Mock-Only Acceptance Does Not Consume GATEWAY Claim\n27145 8:24a ○ core-v1 Dataset Full Task Inventory: Examples and Oracles Confirmed\n27146 \" ○ core-v1 Benchmark Task Source Files Contain Intentional Bugs for Candidate to Fix\n27147 \" ○ G1.1-2 Acceptance Evidence File Does Not Yet Exist\n27148 \" ○ stageEvaluatorRuntime Excludes eval/datasets and eval/tasks from Package — Oracle Isolation Enforced\n27149 8:25a ○ Two Built v1.1.2-rc.1 Package Tarballs Available in Worktrees\n27150 \" ○ WP-1104 Integration Branch: Two Recent Commits Adding Versioned Runner API\n27151 \" ○ Package Smoke-Final Extracted Directory Lacks Compiled CLI — Package May Need Re-extraction\n27152 \" ○ Extracted Package Structure Confirmed: eval_cli.js Not in lib/cli Root — Compiled JS in dist/\n27153 \" ○ Suite Run 4 Log Confirms Dataset Tests Passed and Candidate Actually Ran Against selftest-add\n27154 8:26a ◆ AC4/AC5 Evidence Validator Test Added to package_runtime.test.mjs\n27155 \" ● AC4/AC5 Evidence Validator Test RED Confirmed — Fails When Evidence File Missing\n27156 8:27a ○ eval_cli.ts runVersionedEvalCommand Passes sandboxRuntimePaths Mounting Only CLI and Core Closures\n27157 \" ○ package-linux.sh Requires Approved Rust 1.95 Bookworm Builder or NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1\n27158 8:28a ◆ AC4/AC5 Full Benchmark Evidence Test Implemented in package_runtime.test.mjs\n27159 \" ↻ AC4/AC5 Evidence Test Updated: Self-Extracts Package Archive Instead of Requiring Pre-Extracted NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT\n27160 \" ● Duplicate Variable Declaration Bug in package_runtime.test.mjs — manifestBytes Declared Twice\n27161 8:29a ○ AC4/AC5 Evidence Test Fails: run.mjs Exits with Code 1 When nexus CLI Invoked from Extracted Package\n27162 8:32a ◆ Fresh v1.1.2-rc.1 Package Built from Integration Branch with Docker Bookworm Builder\n27163 \" ○ Fresh Package Still Fails: run.mjs Exits Code 1 — Root Cause Not Yet Identified\n27164 \" ○ runner_api.mjs Spawns run.mjs with stdio: \"ignore\" — run.mjs Error Output Is Silently Discarded\n27165 8:33a ● Diagnostic Retention Added to Evidence Test: Failed Run Copies Outside Dir to /tmp for Inspection\n27166 \" ○ Diagnostic Dump Reveals Package Missing lib/cli/dist/ — Compiled CLI JS Absent from Package\n27167 8:34a ○ Installed nexus CLI Works — VERSION is v1.1.2-rc.1, eval --help Exposes All Versioned Dataset Options\n27168 \" ○ run.mjs Failure Root Cause: \"protected candidate runtime root is forbidden\" — Package Extracted into /tmp Violates Isolation Check\n27169 \" ○ run.mjs Failure: /tmp Extraction Path Triggers FORBIDDEN_RUNTIME_ROOTS Check\n27170 \" ○ sandboxRuntimeRoots Constraint: Package Must Reside Under a Pre-Approved Root Path\n27171 \" ○ FORBIDDEN_RUNTIME_ROOTS Explicitly Includes /tmp — Package Extraction Location Must Avoid All Listed Paths\n27172 8:35a ● AC4/AC5 Evidence Test Fixed: Package Now Extracted to NEXUS_PACKAGE_INSTALL_ROOT Instead of /tmp\n27173 \" ◆ AC4/AC5 Evidence Test Running Live — Package Installed to /nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-ac4-package/install\n27174 8:36a ○ AC4/AC5 Evidence Test Failed Again — Failure Dump Present at /tmp/nexus-ac4-candidate-failure-900948\n27175 8:37a ○ AC4/AC5 Evidence Test New Failure: \"captured candidate request is missing t2-bugfix-csv\"\n27176 \" ✓ Diagnostic Improvements Added to AC4/AC5 Evidence Test for Missing-Task Failures\n27177 8:38a ○ t2-bugfix-csv Objective Text Mismatch — Candidate Received Task But Test Can't Find It by Objective String\n27178 \" ● Evidence Test Request-Matching Fixed: Search Message Content Strings Not JSON-Stringified Message Arrays\n27179 \" ◆ AC4/AC5 Evidence Test GREEN — Acceptance Evidence Written to docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json\n27180 \" ○ AC4/AC5 Evidence File Contents: All 6 Tasks Run, 0 Correct — Loopback Fake Provider Expected\n27181 8:39a ◆ Evidence File Expanded: launcherSha256, cliBundleSha256, coreBinarySha256 Added to Candidate Provenance\n27182 8:40a ○ Final acceptance.json Has Four Component Digests — git diff --check Clean, package_runtime.test.mjs Syntax Valid\n27183 \" ○ Integration Branch Ready to Commit — 11 Changed/New Files, Evidence File at Mode 600\n27189 8:41a ◆ Full package_runtime.test.mjs Suite: 5/5 Pass — All Tests Green Including Package Smoke and Non-Empty Candidate\n27190 8:42a ◆ Evidence File Hardened: Candidate-Specific Filename, Immutability Guard, and Oracle Leak Checks Added\n27191 8:43a ◆ Hardened Evidence Test Green — Candidate-Specific Filename acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json Written Successfully\n27193 \" ○ Suite Snapshot Sync Has Path Bug — eval_cli.ts and Other Files Copied to Wrong Directories\n27194 \" ○ Snapshot Cleanup rm Failed — $snapshot Variable Not Set in Suite-Snapshot Shell Context\n27195 8:45a ✓ Work State Updated: review_delta APPROVED WP-1103/1104 Source and Six-Task Evidence After Corrections\n27196 8:50a ○ Suite Entered New Test Section: /compact Operator Tests Now Running at ~6 Minutes Elapsed\n27197 8:51a ○ Third Evidence File acceptance-b385cd533f9e-suite.json Written — Suite Run Also Executed Acceptance Test\n\nAccess 97k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","create_time":1793611562.696266,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:26:04.001Z","ordinal":36749,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b3e-e325-7090-bf1f-c31aa606240e","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016ae8572b6cec81a38951cab5fbf5b4c7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’ll resume from the active full-suite run, verify its result and claim ownership, then continue the v1.1.2 roadmap with the other agents while keeping the already-approved WP-1103/1104 work isolated from the shared dirty checkout."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793611563445,"completed_at_ms":1793611564001}}
