{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T09:35:40.603Z","ordinal":37050,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a19b9d-503b-7911-a74d-bc95b8b90c0a","author":"/root/v112_release_publication_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/v112_release_publication_audit\nPayload:\n**v1.1.2 is not tagged or published.** GitHub lists v1.1.1 as latest, `gh release view v1.1.2` returns “release not found,” and neither local Git nor `origin` has a `v1.1.2*` tag.\n\nThe release scope is inconsistent with the requested roadmap. The integration worktree’s [v1.1.2 release notes](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md) define a one-fix patch that inherits v1.1.1 qualification. The [v1.1.0 roadmap](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md) defines WP-1101 through WP-1108 and five release gates; its README explicitly says those roadmap packages are not implemented in the described release. Branch CI successes do not qualify an integrated exact head, and the current WP-1103/1104 package was built from a dirty candidate, so it is not exact-commit release evidence.\n\nI sent the audit and recommended next steps to the parent agent. No tags, releases, or files were changed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b9b-782b-7be2-9caf-38c53b688eab","create_time":1793612140.6033313,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1568}}
