{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:02:07.072Z","ordinal":37773,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cfd5c4cd-1d43-44db-818c-c8bd42f682c9","process_id":"20955","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'pending|APPROVED|suite|AC4|GREEN|Gate|release-scope' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'pending|APPROVED|suite|AC4|GREEN|Gate|release-scope' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md","query":"pending|APPROVED|suite|AC4|GREEN|Gate|release-scope","path":"WP-1104-PLAN.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"5:**User story:** As a Nexus operator, I need to run a versioned evaluation dataset through the installed Nexus executable and receive a structured score file, so that I can compare candidate builds reproducibly without depending on the source checkout.\n12:- **AC4:** An exact installed candidate run executes the six unique public benchmark tasks with no skips or missing tasks and records the binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA. Test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`.\n56:- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"run.mjs creates results.jsonl output directory before appending task records\"; no relevant hit because the indexed prefix contains `cli/src` only. The failing outside-checkout test showed that an empty versioned split invokes the scorer with no `results.jsonl`; the fix initializes the new results file before appending records, following the existing file/append flow in `eval/run.mjs`.\n63:- **GREEN:** `npm run build` passed; the initial `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` run passed 7/7 with the original empty-dataset legacy case. That test was later strengthened because the initial case did not prove truncation.\n66:- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\n67:- **Peer review:** Independent code review returned `APPROVED_WITH_COMMENTS` for AC2. Reviewer confirmed the installed CLI/runner/scorer path and the empty-split file fix; the comment is blocking AC4 evidence, which remains outstanding.\n69:- **AC5 test review:** An independent read-only review confirmed the non-empty two-task fixture and `--limit 1` assertions exercise real truncation and first-task-only prompting. The reviewer caught that `spawnSync` would block the in-process mock server; the test now uses async `spawn`, which the reviewer confirmed resolves that deadlock. Runtime verification remains pending the shared test lane.\n70:- **AC5 red/green:** The first strengthened run failed because the mock returned JSON while the client requested SSE (`INFERENCE_FAILED: stream_incomplete`). After switching to the retrieved SSE contract and setting `--workspace` to an isolated empty directory (so evaluator discovery cannot run this repository's test suite), `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_cli.test.ts` passed 7/7; the non-empty `--limit 1` case confirmed exactly one completion request containing the first prompt and not the second.\n72:- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\n74:## Gate attempt notes\n76:- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reconciled to the full roadmap before any v1.1.2 publication; this WP slice does not change the release notes or release branch.\n77:- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\n79:- A first `npm test` run on `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot` was diagnostic only: the snapshot had no `cli/dist/index.js` or Rust core binaries, and `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` was unset so the actual package smoke was skipped. Its test runner reported 1,981 tests (1,739 pass, 222 fail) and then remained in `turn_semantics.test.ts` with repeated provider-recovery retries; that process was interrupted after about 40 minutes. This is not accepted full-suite evidence.\n81:- A separate focused test process in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr398-review` remains active. The next full-suite attempt must wait for it to finish, then set `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` to the freshly extracted development package so the actual outside-checkout runtime test runs instead of skipping.\n82:- After peer review identified that the former empty-dataset `--limit 0` case did not prove truncation, the legacy compatibility test was strengthened to a non-empty two-task fixture and async local OpenAI-compatible mock. The first mock response format caused an expected transport failure; the second run timed out because the evaluator used the repository as its workspace and discovered the repository test command. Both causes were corrected. Current targeted TypeScript no-emit and `git diff --check` pass, and the updated focused suite passes 7/7.\n83:- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":881370826}},"started_at_ms":1793613726188,"completed_at_ms":1793613727070}}
