rsion, split, manifest SHA-256, denominator and each task invocation/result.\n\n**Coordination:** The original plan was independently approved by `review_delta` and `release_gate_audit`. The previous runner claim was older than 24 hours, its clean branch was still `c548e53e`, the host had rebooted since the claim, and no process had its worktree as cwd; `.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log` records the stale-claim break at 2026-11-01T21:56Z. Old dataset and runner branches are preserved as read-only reference. Fresh claims now point to `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. Re-review this updated plan before coding. The previous SUITE claim was released after host reboot interrupted its run; claim SUITE before the next suite.\n14:- **AC5:** Run the exact candidate CLI against a local fake provider that captures the actual request after prompt construction; record one candidate invocation and validator/scorer result for each of the six manifest-declared benchmark task IDs, with zero skipped or missing tasks. Pin the candidate SHA, dataset version/split, and the SHA-256 recomputed from the final integrated `core-v1/manifest.json`; do not reuse the prior branch's `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43` as current evidence. Test/evidence: `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. This establishes execution coverage and request isolation, not model quality.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","create_time":1793614135.6121027}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
