{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:11:43.078Z","ordinal":38213,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a19bbe-4f66-7120-9c93-23cf198dd450","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**REQUEST_CHANGES before closing WP-1103.** AC1, AC3, AC3a, AC4, and AC5 have evidence at `2a94f62e`; AC2 is not fully established against its exact wording.\n\n- **AC1 — proven:** [eval_dataset.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts:27) captures the actual provider request and checks injected oracle sentinels are absent. [dataset.test.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/eval/dataset.test.mjs:122) checks the production payload builder’s argv, environment, and serialized stdin.\n- **AC2 — partial:** the dataset integration test checks that `hidden/math.hidden.test.js` is absent from the staged workspace and unreadable by its relative path ([eval_dataset.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts:84)). General Bubblewrap tests probe external canaries and protected paths ([eval_integrity.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:915), [line 1243](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1243)), but I found no dataset-specific probe of the absolute dataset task/validator paths or the exact mount list for that run. The tests support the boundary, but do not directly demonstrate the full dataset-specific mount-view criterion.\n- **AC3 and AC3a — proven:** split/ID selection and oracle/task-tree tampering regressions are in [dataset.test.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/eval/dataset.test.mjs:24).\n- **AC4 — proven:** the actual candidate exits before the evaluator records `hiddenPass: true` for the synthetic fixture ([eval_dataset.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts:90)).\n- **AC5 — proven for execution and request capture:** the installed package runs all six benchmark IDs with six captured requests and no missing or skipped tasks. The evidence binds the package components and recomputed manifest hash. The false hidden-test scores are correctly described as fixture/provider behavior, not model-quality evidence.\n\n**Claim state:** `WP-1103` and `WP-1103_RUNNER_API` still point to the existing `v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` worktree at `af26ade`. Most file claims point to the integration worktree at `2a94f62e`. The evidence claim still names generic `acceptance.json` on the old worktree; the candidate-specific evidence files are not named by that claim. Reconcile or release these claims before closing. I did not inspect held-out payloads, edit files, or run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","create_time":1793614303.0785172,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1606}}
