{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:16:39.943Z","ordinal":38409,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016ae86303907081a3b3279ecb554953f9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_2b365560e670455da709ea669cea03da","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\\n@@\\n **Coordination:** The original plan was independently approved by `review_delta` and `release_gate_audit`. The previous runner claim was older than 24 hours, its clean branch was still `c548e53e`, the host had rebooted since the claim, and no process had its worktree as cwd; `.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log` records the stale-claim break at 2026-11-01T21:56Z. Old dataset and runner branches are preserved as read-only reference. Fresh claims now point to `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. Re-review this updated plan before coding. The previous SUITE claim was released after host reboot interrupted its run; claim SUITE before the next suite.\\n+\\n+## AC2 plan addendum — actual candidate mount view\\n+\\n+**Spec refinement:** AC2 requires evidence from the running dataset candidate's filesystem view, in addition to proving that the staged fixture workspace omits hidden files. The test must show that the candidate can see its declared `/workspace` mount, that the evaluator's dataset staging root is not mounted there, and that the absolute hidden validator path is unreadable.\\n+\\n+**Chunk:** Extend the existing `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` subtest in `cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts`. Use the local fake provider to ask the real candidate to execute a read-only `run_command` probe. Capture the command's stdout and assert all three mount/path outcomes, while retaining the existing relative-path and sentinel assertions. No production sandbox change is planned unless the probe exposes a real leak.\\n+\\n+**Reference retrieval:** XERJ `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:183` (`probeBwrapSandbox`) demonstrates probing a real Bubblewrap process against an outside canary; `nexus-cli/tools.ts:1523` locates the production `run_command` wrapper, and `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:219` provides the `wrapSandboxedCommand` signature. `eval/isolate.mjs` is outside the indexed CLI source; local source inspection at `agentSandboxArgv` confirmed the evaluator mounts `/tmp` as tmpfs and binds the candidate workspace at `/workspace`.\\n+\\n+**Observed TDD:** The first focused run failed because the assertion matched the literal readable branch in the captured command rather than its stdout. The test was corrected to parse the `run_command` result. The focused dataset test then passed 3/3, with workspace mount present, dataset root mount absent, and the absolute validator path unreadable. This change adds dataset-specific acceptance evidence; it does not change production sandbox code.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","create_time":1793614595.5654218}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T10:16:39.987Z","ordinal":38410,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19b9f-f23a-70e0-bbf9-0adf509bb26d","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-364773fe-2636-45a2-88e6-21f6f5e37071","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -37 +37,11 @@\n **Coordination:** The original plan was independently approved by `review_delta` and `release_gate_audit`. The previous runner claim was older than 24 hours, its clean branch was still `c548e53e`, the host had rebooted since the claim, and no process had its worktree as cwd; `.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log` records the stale-claim break at 2026-11-01T21:56Z. Old dataset and runner branches are preserved as read-only reference. Fresh claims now point to `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. Re-review this updated plan before coding. The previous SUITE claim was released after host reboot interrupted its run; claim SUITE before the next suite.\n+\n+## AC2 plan addendum — actual candidate mount view\n+\n+**Spec refinement:** AC2 requires evidence from the running dataset candidate's filesystem view, in addition to proving that the staged fixture workspace omits hidden files. The test must show that the candidate can see its declared `/workspace` mount, that the evaluator's dataset staging root is not mounted there, and that the absolute hidden validator path is unreadable.\n+\n+**Chunk:** Extend the existing `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` subtest in `cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts`. Use the local fake provider to ask the real candidate to execute a read-only `run_command` probe. Capture the command's stdout and assert all three mount/path outcomes, while retaining the existing relative-path and sentinel assertions. No production sandbox change is planned unless the probe exposes a real leak.\n+\n+**Reference retrieval:** XERJ `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:183` (`probeBwrapSandbox`) demonstrates probing a real Bubblewrap process against an outside canary; `nexus-cli/tools.ts:1523` locates the production `run_command` wrapper, and `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:219` provides the `wrapSandboxedCommand` signature. `eval/isolate.mjs` is outside the indexed CLI source; local source inspection at `agentSandboxArgv` confirmed the evaluator mounts `/tmp` as tmpfs and binds the candidate workspace at `/workspace`.\n+\n+**Observed TDD:** The first focused run failed because the assertion matched the literal readable branch in the captured command rather than its stdout. The test was corrected to parse the `run_command` result. The focused dataset test then passed 3/3, with workspace mount present, dataset root mount absent, and the absolute validator path unreadable. This change adds dataset-specific acceptance evidence; it does not change production sandbox code.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793614599985,"completed_at_ms":1793614599987}}
