{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:01:13.984Z","ordinal":41014,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016ae87b8915ac81a3a91d7ee74e21bb80","status":"completed","call_id":"call_452cccaea9e849ee8733f1273865129e","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,130p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -type f | head -n 12; find .git -maxdepth 2 -iname '*claim*' -type f | head -n 20; rg -n \\\"nexus-claims|claim.*release|release.*claim|owner.json\\\" scripts docs .github\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:2400});text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","create_time":1793620873.0859635}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:01:14.073Z","ordinal":41015,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016ae87b87660c81a39429361c5df737cc","usage":{"input_tokens":174795,"cached_input_tokens":173696,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":277,"reasoning_output_tokens":134,"total_tokens":175072},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":850984,"cached_input_tokens":839808,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2120,"reasoning_output_tokens":1237,"total_tokens":853104},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":789621578,"cached_input_tokens":782925440,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1635402,"reasoning_output_tokens":827659,"total_tokens":791256980}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:01:16.898Z","ordinal":41016,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8a644d3e-4fdd-4a1c-be96-5de21d0103e8","process_id":"88017","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,130p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -type f | head -n 12; find .git -maxdepth 2 -iname '*claim*' -type f | head -n 20; rg -n \"nexus-claims|claim.*release|release.*claim|owner.json\" scripts docs .github"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,130p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md","name":"CONCURRENCY.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -type f","path":"nexus-claims"},{"type":"search","cmd":"find .git -maxdepth 2 -iname '*claim*' -type f","query":"*claim*","path":".git"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'nexus-claims|claim.*release|release.*claim|owner.json' scripts docs .github","query":"nexus-claims|claim.*release|release.*claim|owner.json","path":"scripts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\nThese files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n\n| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n| `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts` | 01, 02 | **PLAN-01 PR-1a (effect classes) lands first.** PLAN-02 PR-2c adds schema fields afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\n| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\n| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n| `package.json`, `cli/package.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, lockfiles | 01, 06, 07, 08 | **Only one agent at a time.** Version fields are written only by `scripts/sync-version.mjs`. Dependency changes are separate commits that touch only the lockfile and manifest. |\n| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\n\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\n\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\n\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n\n## 6. Coordination records\n\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n|---|---|\n| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\n| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\n| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\n| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\n| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n\n## 8. Independence constraints\n\n- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\n- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\n- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_eval_datasets_core-v1_tasks_t2-bugfix-csv_task.json/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_eval_datasets_core-v1_manifest.json/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_eval_cli.ts.released-20261102T100651Z/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_experiments_cloudflare-artifacts-vertical-slice_trusted-broker-bundle_package.json/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc.11_providers_openrouter_live_task_20261030.md/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_eval_datasets_core-v1_tasks_t2-bugfix-duration_repo_tests_test_durations.py/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_core_git_hook_guard.ts/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/V1_HELDOUT_CORPUS_CUSTODY_20261028/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_eval_datasets_core-v1_tasks_t2-feature-slugify_repo_package.json/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_eval_datasets_core-v1_tasks_t2-bugfix-duration_repo_durations.py/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_test_team.test.ts/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_cli_src_session_export.ts/owner.json.handoff-20261020T113105Z\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.lock\n.git/nexus-claims/.claims.lock\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log.lock\n.git/nexus-claims-ownership.lock\n.git/nexus-claims.log\n.git/nexus-claims.log.lock\ndocs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md:119:When a recovery or upgrade observes a stale lock (dead holder PID), exactly one process may unlink and replace it. Serialization uses a permanent kernel-owned guard file `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.upgrade.lock.guard` (never unlinked or replaced; accepted only as a regular file owned by the running user with no group/other permission bits): the reclaimer holds an advisory `flock` on the file's open file description for the whole reclaim section, acquired through `/usr/bin/flock` (util-linux; Linux runtime prerequisite) with exit status 75 distinguishing contention. The kernel drops the lock when the last referring descriptor closes, so a reclaimer killed by SIGKILL or power loss releases automatically instead of wedging later upgrades. If the flock utility or filesystem is unavailable, acquisition fails closed with a manual-intervention error rather than proceeding unserialized.\ndocs/CLOUDFLARE_CONTEST_CRITICAL_PATH_ASSESSMENT.md:44:| `CTX-001` | Prompt context lacks demonstrated per-item source provenance and classification; reconstruction of why an agent acted may be incomplete. | Phase 2 §12; final matrix row `CTX-001`; `cli/src/agent.ts:1205` builds a combined prompt from project rules, skills, knowledge, few-shots, task/history and tool schemas. | Issue #12 closure blocker; contest `DEMO_RELIABILITY_RISK`. Remains open. | Demo must pin runner version/config and task/baseline, use clean controlled repositories and keep the prompt short; do not claim complete prompt-item provenance. This bounds variability but does not satisfy the requirement. | Before claiming full prompt causality/provenance, adding arbitrary retrieved context, or general release. |\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP_REVIEW_20261031.md:29:- **Claim:** `RC14_RELEASE_PARITY_DOCS`\ndocs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP_REVIEW_20261031.md:67:- Claims directory shows: RC14_E2_NODE_FLOOR_EVIDENCE, RC14_RELEASE_PARITY_DOCS\ndocs/REPOSITORY_QUALITY.md:27:Mandatory SHA policy remains off while the default branch still contains mutable references. This PR's pins must reach main before enabling it. Release-environment restrictions and release-asset immutability are not claimed applied; they require a coordinated lifecycle check with the publisher. Required CI and review of this PR remain pending independently of the applied settings. CodeQL and Dependabot configuration checks on the original PR head passed; that is not full product qualification.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:168:The standalone qualification follows [DEC-16](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-16-standalone-qualification-under-a-gateway-only-environment). Nexus runs in a clean environment without gateway credentials or gateway-specific configuration and sends requests through a local stripping proxy. The proxy removes gateway-only model, tokenization, response-header, and admission information before Nexus sees it. Qualification also requires the specified server-kind conformance checks. This release candidate has not completed the standalone matrix, so no standalone server-kind qualification is claimed.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:179:- **Manual real-terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** No manual five-terminal by three-size runs or per-cell evidence are claimed. The automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory release gates and must pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:- **Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `998d34e04a56726d9e2403e4ac6c2491042ab4f5`, the merge commit for PR #358. CodeQL run [41170399717](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41170399717) passed on that exact SHA. Main CI run [41170399731](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41170399731) is still in progress; no full-main CI pass is claimed yet. Earlier run [41164168577](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41164168577) passed on its exact prior SHA `de5e30baca788ee103437ddd984a4df567f90981` only. These results do not qualify the installed RC14 artifact or establish overall release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:11:- **RC14 artifact and integrated evidence:** The latest public release is prerelease `v1.0.0-rc.14`, built from `16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99`; its Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `52d1c855158c63dbc7cac2e9d87e2f64b1feffb193de97660e92276a2bd46eb7`. Stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Exact-RC two-runner reproducibility run [41038503854](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/41038503854) passed, including comparison of both runner builds and selected package/SBOM artifacts against the published RC14 archive; its downloaded evidence binds `REQ-REL-114`/`ACC-SUP-08` to this RC14 source and digest. The ledger row still needs reconciliation with that packet, and this result does not qualify any later candidate. RC14 artifact/provenance, cross-runner, power-loss, corrected power-loss linkage, and E2 node-floor/root evidence are integrated through PRs #344, #345, #347, #348 and #349. PR #354 integrated the 43 checksum-bound RC14 logs and narrow ignore allowlist. PR #352 integrated the bounded OpenRouter live-task and provider-verification packet plus the experimental ChatGPT repeat verification after independent ACCEPT, all 15 packet checksums, a 3/3 offline-fixture rerun, and passing exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks; its Entire gate is `NEUTRAL` and the associated trail is closed. PR #358 merged the exact-installed-RC scripted-PTY packet at `bb48dc93` into current main as `998d34e0`. Its evidence review remains `CHANGES_REQUIRED`: it identified missing `TERM=dumb` and 40×14 automated accessibility coverage and truncated 40-column hints. A focused product fix is being handled on a separate claimed branch; neither that fix nor independent §5.2 acceptance is established by this merge. These scoped results do not establish overall RC acceptance, and they do not qualify later source revisions merely because those revisions are descended from RC14.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:14:- **Disposition and remaining gates:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. PR #356 (readiness and release-note disclosures) and PR #357 (RC14 lifecycle evidence correction) remain open against the prior base and are being rebased onto `998d34e0`; prior exact-head checks and review results do not qualify rebased heads. PR #358 is merged, but its unresolved automated accessibility finding leaves §5.2 unaccepted; the focused fix remains on a separate claimed branch. Installed-RC qualification, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, held-out T2/T3/T4 custody and qualification, the final exact-RC evidence gate, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The release-note disclosures must be refreshed from accepted exact-RC evidence before stable publication. No local server kind is listed as qualified before its required standalone evidence passes. Current main is not the RC14 source commit; any candidate containing later source changes needs its own exact-artifact qualification rather than inheriting RC14 evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:39:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:65:**Release PRs:** PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is merged at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`, included in current main. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is based on `145d464` at exact head `49a2af0c1d556912d12b834aa7f2022ef63b528c`; its latest follow-up scopes checkout to the nested workspace and extends the regression to preserve both staged and unstaged sibling state. The prior nested-index delta at `662d084` was independently ACCEPTed (SHA-256 `61f4e40bc135152ffa003c82bdc31fc15703542b5bd9ba3b67f7b6b1edae1cb2`), and the checkout-scope delta was independently ACCEPTed by `review_pr302` (SHA-256 `26ce020bdc1f6865e194f02e45c6889eaa32415cc786a457fbcfae1ddaa78605`, tests not run). PR #302 CodeQL and JS/TS checks pass; Node 22/24 CI and Entire are running. TypeScript `--noEmit` and `git diff --check` passed on the prior delta; no local suite was run under the active SUITE claim.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**Requirements and qualification:** Current-main CI's requirements checker passes; the most recent explicit `--enforce` result was on PR #302 head `c3901774` before the nested-workspace-only follow-up: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to installed-RC qualification. RC10 has scope-limited exact-artifact evidence: OpenRouter pinned-model verification and one synthetic live task passed, and the cross-runner workflow passed for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against published RC10 (run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805)). A later checkpoint correction incorrectly claimed this workflow failed because of an npm-version mismatch. That correction is superseded: GitHub records run `40564959805` and its `compare` job as completed successfully; the current checkpoint above reports that final result. This historical correction is retained here to preserve the audit trail. These results apply only to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; they do not qualify a successor candidate or establish full release acceptance. The newly pushed #302 head must complete exact checks before its requirements evidence is refreshed. Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. GitHub installer is the selected distribution target; npm publication is inapplicable.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:151:**RC10 reproducibility scope:** PR [#281](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/281) recorded the successful exact-tag run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805); PR [#282](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/282) clarified that the comparison established byte identity for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against the published RC10. It does not claim byte identity for every build output. This evidence is bound to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; any successor source needs its own exact-tag reproducibility run.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:171:**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Exact cross-runner reproducibility passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca`; a successor candidate from current main still requires its own reproducibility run. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; no cell result or screenshot is recorded. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:183:**Other release-path PRs:** PR [#276](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/276) records a synthetic-only qualification-host preflight (10/10) bound to `ceabfcc`; its Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass, while Linux CI remains in progress. Its evidence does not establish custodian access, held-out qualification, or acceptance. PR [#277](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/277) addresses configured Git-hook execution during checkpoint and retention operations. Its exact diff received conflicting review dispositions: a GitHub review comment requested changes for a hook-discovery race and retention error accounting, while a separate read-only review returned ACCEPT. The findings remain unresolved pending the claimed implementation owner's response; no acceptance or merge is claimed. Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks pass; Linux CI remains in progress.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:364:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `bbafae868939084ccd49f21621695dff6b05f752`, incorporating PR #249 (`8e562b0f3406e94003806746cb69a5258f72a59f`) and PR #250. PR #249 merged at 05:57 UTC and PR #250 merged at 06:20 UTC. On this exact source, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification), and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` confirms all components are `1.0.0-rc.8`. CodeQL run [40279197561](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197561) passed. Exact-main CI [40279197785](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40279197785) is still running; its Node 22 and Node 24 jobs passed Rust tests and release builds and were running the CLI test suite at 06:24 UTC. The current checkpoint does not claim full CI success.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:387:**Checkpoint index-lock defect:** PR [#243](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/243) merged as `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, an ancestor of current `main`. It adds actionable diagnosis and a final lock recheck when checkpoint creation encounters a Git index lock. Its required checks passed and an independent review accepted the exact diff. This is source remediation on current `main`; RC6 and RC7 artifacts predate it. The next installed RC still needs to be exercised against the reported startup failure before claiming a released fix.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:401:**Checkpoint index-lock defect:** PR [#243](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/243) merged as `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, an ancestor of current `main`. It adds actionable diagnosis and a final lock recheck when checkpoint creation encounters a Git index lock. Its required checks passed and an independent review accepted the exact diff. This is source remediation on current `main`; RC6 and RC7 artifacts predate it. The next installed RC still needs to be exercised against the reported startup failure before claiming a released fix.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:415:**Checkpoint index-lock defect:** PR [#243](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/243) merged at 00:16 UTC as `0542312a0364b03cec5b66b6cb8234b210805cd2`, which is an ancestor of current `main`. Its focused change adds actionable diagnosis and a final lock recheck when checkpoint creation encounters a Git index lock; its tests and required PR checks passed, with independent review ACCEPT recorded for the exact diff. This is source-level remediation on current `main`, not behavior in the older RC6 or RC7 artifacts. The installed next RC must still be exercised against the reported startup failure before claiming the issue fixed in a release. The `FILE_cli_src_checkpoint.ts` claim has been released after verifying merge, checks and a clean worktree.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:443:**Disposition:** Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is not accepted and no stable release is claimed. The next release candidate must include the merged checkpoint fix, pass exact-source CI and qualification gates, and be installed and identified before product qualification. Remaining gates include independent held-out custody and T2, provider/standalone behavior, T3/T4, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance. Publication authorization remains granted once every required gate passes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:449:**Release state:** GitHub lists `v1.0.0-rc.6` as the latest published prerelease. Signed tag `v1.0.0-rc.7` (tag object `d1f79e58a27c0f79f1663f662a153ae4ec5a7824`) now points to source `431cb194931f09eaaffdb6880dc464c1d7b5e2a1`; Release workflow [40246054889](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40246054889) is in progress. GitHub has not published an RC7 release or assets yet. RC6 is not an accepted RC, and no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:471:**Release disposition and next actions:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is published but unaccepted; no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Exact-main CI and CodeQL now pass on `1f3c655`; the pinned-builder documentation claim still needs a safe owner handoff and reconciliation. Continue the installed-candidate qualification lanes, resolve held-out corpus compatibility with the independent custodian, and prepare a new versioned RC only through the accepted process after its prerequisites pass. Exact-RC qualification, independent acceptance, and final publication remain gated by their evidence. Publication authorization remains granted and gated.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:483:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC3 is a published candidate, not an accepted RC. No stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. The installed command now uses RC3; RC1 remains available by its versioned path. The next critical dependency is accepted held-out custody and runner compatibility; other exact-RC gates can proceed independently where their required providers and environments are available.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:495:**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed. Next source action is to finish exact post-merge CI on `1b9791f`; after it passes, proceed through the accepted RC3 workflow and exact-artifact qualification. Held-out qualification remains dependent on the independent custodian and cannot start before custody and runner compatibility are accepted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:511:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:525:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:539:`origin/main` is now `dceac980b3d77c99a26bb9ddedb61c443168952a`, after PR #142 merged as `08861feb2c6a164a89f4c0573e1c7793c9f938e5` and PR #143 merged as `dceac980b3d77c99a26bb9ddedb61c443168952a`. PR #143 corrects the Node 20 EOL date in the RC1 release note; independent review accepted its exact net diff, and exact-head CI `39769489238` plus CodeQL `39769489243` passed on PR head `5e1f221e920bf6738fb3d62296199f34c8db53a0` against base `08861fe`. Post-merge CI `39773603423` and CodeQL `39773603376` are running on exact `main@dceac980`; no post-merge conclusion is claimed yet. Contest work is over and no contest freeze applies. Campaign status remains `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. RC1 remains an older artifact, and no stable v1.0.0 release is asserted.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:618:- **PR state:** PRs #9, #13, #15, #16, and #44 are integrated. PR #9's stale readiness changes were merged earlier and are retained in history. PR #33 remains open at `0ca77e5ee64f80db02e2b16178c5be551ce5de0c`, based on now-stale `faf9580`; its exact CI run `39141771002` passed all five jobs, including 1,243 CLI tests with zero failures, resource enforcement fixtures, staged Git-history/external-store canaries, security gates, deterministic package/SBOM comparison, and installer/package smoke. Independent review found a release-critical gap: preflight does not compare protected corpus paths with the evaluator's unconditional system mounts such as `/usr/local/lib`. The reviewer requested refusal of protected paths beneath every mounted host path and regression coverage. The evaluator claim remains active; no transfer or remediation checkpoint has been reported. Do not run held-out qualification. PR #33 must incorporate `4bce876`, fix this finding, pass exact-head checks, and receive independent re-review.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:634:- **T3 and terminal lanes:** PR #27 T3 harness head `12edf74` has independent code review ACCEPT. Its CI run [39119197191](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39119197191) has the contest-contract and Node 20/22/24 jobs successful; `linux-x86_64` remains in progress. The custodian recorded an 8/8-task T3 corpus seal at 10:43:02 UTC, with corrected private manifest digest `dcbd794ed2998423787fdead4957b38b0c4a8a641855d87304d065d01c3fae37` at 10:43:22 UTC, and released both authoring claims. This is sealed, custodian-validated corpus evidence; no T3 qualification run has occurred. PR #24's real-terminal procedure is integrated, but all required five environments × three sizes still require the exact installed RC and genuine operator evidence; no matrix cell is claimed complete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:758:- **Campaign:** `NEXUS_V1_RC_QUALIFICATION_ACTIVE`. **Acceptance:** `IN_PROGRESS`. RC5 is a public prerelease; neither an accepted RC nor stable v1.0.0 is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:797:- **Checkpoint restore PR #302:** The remote PR head remains `934ed912b8e187c5c418709e472a6313bb4169a8`; its exact run [40729450236](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40729450236) failed the Node 22 and Node 24 suites on the tracked-deletion/symlink-parent checkpoint creation case, with Linux skipped. A separate local candidate has been rebased onto `8580c82` at `87b560c7e581fa71cce270474ba40766f372fb04`; the cumulative change is limited to `checkpoint.ts` and its two restore tests. Independent full-diff review and the authorized full-suite owner’s safe-boundary release are pending. The candidate has not been pushed, and no test result is claimed for it.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:799:- **Qualification and release:** At this historical checkpoint, Acceptance was `IN_PROGRESS`; installed-RC evidence was tied to RC10. DEC-20 later waived the manual real-terminal matrix for v1.0.0, superseding the earlier 0/15 required-cell disposition; no cells are claimed as passed. Held-out custody and evaluator compatibility were unresolved; no protected payload was accessed or run. Current exact-RC provider, standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent acceptance were not established. Stable `v1.0.0` was unpublished. Publication authorization remains granted but gated by acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:55:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:94:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:95:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:126:| HIST-01 | S2 | Extensions/MCP, release gating | docs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:7,112-121; cli/src/plugins.ts:150-200 | DOC-CLAIM+SOURCE: Issue #12 remains OPEN; CTX-001, CTX-002, EXT-004 never closed in any later doc. EXT-004 still unmet at HEAD: `executeToolPipeline` pre/post middleware can rewrite args/results with no before/after audit record | Plugins can silently alter what tools did; prompt provenance not reconstructable | Either implement or record an explicit operator waiver/supersession before v1; do not ship v1 with silently-open normative blockers |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:131:| HIST-06 | S3 | Install/positioning docs | docs/USER_MANUAL.md:3,14,19; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:24-25,43; quickstart.md:21-23 | SOURCE/DOC: manual claims \"direct parity with OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude Code\"; `harness repl` (installed binary is `nexus`); `nexus --approve` vs quickstart `nexus repl --approve`; ARCHITECTURE names homelab hardware/port 18010 and calls `repl.ts` the TUI; quickstart \"install another specific version\" example is identical to the pinned command; MCP_GUIDE link is `file:///home/mike/...` | New users get wrong commands and inflated expectations | Reconcile docs to shipped binary (RELEASE-REQUIRED) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:133:| HIST-08 | S2 | Standalone local inference | reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md \"Not done\"; docs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:33 | DOC-CLAIM: all live evidence is homelab gateway (llama.cpp behind aihost). No live run on plain LM Studio/vLLM/llama.cpp/Ollama although quickstart's first-run path is LM Studio | Primary documented setup unqualified | v1 must include live standalone qualification on ≥2 servers |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:194:| REQ-DX-V1-01 | Docs match shipped behaviour: no parity claim, correct commands, no worker-sandbox claim unless wired, no homelab hardware in ARCHITECTURE | HIST-03/06 | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Doc-command smoke: every command in README/quickstart/USER_MANUAL runs `--help` OK on package |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/B_providers.md:111:| PRV-R10 | Docs match behaviour: remove homelab ids, fix catalog-cache and redaction claims, document custom CA and LAN/Tailscale locality setting. | docs | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Doc review checklist against PRV-11/17/18. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:55:| VER-04 | S2 | Configured-verifier VERIFIED claims; discovered-verifier coverage | tester.ts:356-360 | RUNTIME (tester_probe). `isVerifierDeliverableBound` matches basenames by substring against the command and the output. If `src/a.ts` changed and the output mentions `src/data.ts`, the run counts as bound. If `README.md` changed and the output says \"see README.md\", it counts as bound. Any changed file under `test/` binds the whole change. With a configured verifier, bound means VERIFIED (agent.ts:5124-5146, no independence check). | VERIFIED can rest on a filename coincidence instead of coverage. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: match whole path tokens (boundary-delimited relative paths). Drop basename matching or require a path separator before it. Require a test-path change to be accompanied by executed tests from that file. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:58:| VER-07 | S2 | `nexus eval` benchmark scores | evaluator.ts:128, 155-166, 173-190, 213 | SOURCE. (a) `git checkout base_commit` runs in the operator's workspace before the worktree exists, and failure is ignored. (b) The patch is `git diff HEAD~1..HEAD`, the last commit and not the agent's change, so `hasCodeChanges` is true for almost any repo with history. (c) A `test_patch` apply failure is swallowed and grading continues on the existing suite. (d) `fail_to_pass`/`pass_to_pass` are ignored and the whole suite runs via detectTestCommand (`npm test` fallback). (e) `testRes.command === \"none\"` is unreachable. Net effect: an agent that does nothing on a repo whose tests pass scores RESOLVED. evaluator.test.ts never calls `evaluateInstance`. ISSUE12 matrices mark EXEC-011 \"DEMONSTRATED\". | Any published `nexus eval` pass rate is invalid. The workspace HEAD may be detached unexpectedly. | BLOCKER for any benchmark claim; otherwise RELEASE-REQUIRED: remove the command or label it experimental, or fix it (diff vs base in the worktree, fail on test_patch error, run FAIL_TO_PASS/PASS_TO_PASS ids, never touch the operator checkout). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:59:| VER-08 | S2 | `--tdd` / `/tdd` | synthesizer.ts:239-326; agent.ts:5236-5255 | SOURCE + INFERENCE. `runAutonomousTdd` never calls `verifyRedPhase` or `verifyGreenPhase`, ignores every `agent.run` result, and contains dead code (266-272). Success is only a full-suite exit 0, with no check that tests executed. Each `agent.run` calls `resetConversation()` (AGT-01), so GREEN starts with no memory of the RED test. The RED prompt asks the model to call `task_completed` with a deliberately failing test, but the completion oracle runs the discovered verifier, which fails → completion refused (INFERENCE). The success summary claims \"RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR verified\". | The TDD mode advertises a protocol it does not enforce. RED turns likely end in NOT_ESTABLISHED or stagnation. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enforce the phases (run the repro target and require fail, then pass), carry the conversation between phases, exempt the RED phase from the completion oracle; or mark the mode experimental. Add an e2e test with a mock model. |\ndocs/ISSUE12_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_ASSESSMENT.md:127:| `F-WP11-OBS-01`: secret scanning primarily covers tracked/staged files. | `ACCEPTED_BOUNDED_LIMITATION` | Does not contradict the bounded commit/release scan claims already accepted; retain the scanner boundary precisely. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:66:| DOC-01 | S3 | docs accuracy | docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:55-58 | DOC-CLAIM vs RUNTIME. \"requests targeting /etc/shadow, ~/.ssh are rejected\" is true only for file tools (`run_command cat ~/.ssh/...` runs, and is allowed even in read-only). The \"Dangerous Command Filter\" is presented as prevention. Audit \"permanently recorded\" has no rotation. WP05 DISC-003 \"never contain unredacted secrets\" rests on a pattern classifier: non-pattern data in a fetch_web URL is not covered (INFERENCE). | Overstated guarantees. | RELEASE-REQUIRED doc correction. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:21:| upstream/node-v24.21.0/{pubring.kbx, SHASUMS256.txt, .sig} (vendored) | sha256 compared with README claim; `gpgv` signature check run locally against the vendored keyring. Keyring provenance (nodejs/release-keys commit) not independently re-fetched. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:92:| EVL-001 | S1 (v1 task-quality claim) | Qualification evidence | eval/README.md:42,47-58; docs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md:62-63 | DOC-CLAIM + SOURCE. The only scored evidence is 6 in-repo T2 fixture tasks. RESULT.md itself says \"These six tasks were used to find and fix the issues … it does not qualify Nexus. Qualification needs a fresh task set.\" Missing: held-out tasks, the T3 long-task set, the T4 fault injector, the T3 fact-sheet scorer, and runs on the release candidate. The measured builds are 76f4081, ed17e99 and 4fcbe68-dirty; their rebased equivalents (fe576f1, d116e99, 0090f9c) are on main, but db1ca55 itself was never evaluated. | No basis for a v1 claim about task quality. The pilot verdict was \"NOT QUALIFIED (false VERIFIED=2)\". The rerun had 0 false VERIFIED, but on tuned tasks. | A v1 protocol is in §7. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:176:| EVL-R1 | **Held-out set:** at least 40 T2 tasks (proposal). At least 50% from external repos at pinned commits (JS/TS, Python, Rust, Go). The held-out half is authored by someone other than the Nexus developer and kept outside the repo (encrypted or private) until the freeze. The 6 pilot tasks plus the routing engx T01-T12 count as a *development* set only. | workflow | BLOCKER for any v1 quality claim | The manifest lists task sha256s committed *before* the release-candidate (RC) freeze. Tasks are revealed after scoring. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:20:The source tests cover the applicable source acceptance criteria. They do not claim installed-RC qualification, held-out qualification, cross-runner qualification, or human terminal acceptance. Those release gates remain pending.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-DISCOVERED-VERIFIER-BASELINE-20261026/node22-focused-run.md:8:- Shared `SUITE` claim was held for the run and released after exit 0.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_SESSION_POWER_RECOVERY/README.md:17:All runs use isolated HOME/XDG and SSD-backed `/var/tmp`; no external inference or held-out payloads. Focused tests ran under the local SUITE claim. Exact-head equipped-host CI and independent review are required before integration. No RC, human acceptance, or release readiness is established here.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md:7:On 2026-10-18 the owner instructed: “The claude agent has hit a rate-limit. Review where it left off and take over it's duties.” The `RELEASE_PUBLISHER` claim was transferred from `claude-code` to `codex-api-root` under that instruction. The old record is preserved in the shared Git metadata and the append-only claims log. If Claude resumes, it must coordinate a new handoff before publishing; there is one active publisher.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/REPOSITORY-QUALITY-REVIEW/independent-review.md:13:Governance correctly distinguishes shared GitHub identity from independent agent review. Support/security documentation avoids claiming a released v1. Frozen contest sources and their dependency trees are untouched.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/REPOSITORY-QUALITY-REVIEW/independent-review.md:19:Isolated HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME; atomic SUITE claim acquired for these short offline checks and released afterward. No production state, credentials, inference, or GitHub setting mutations were used.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_LEGACY_POLICY/README.md:7:Fresh GitHub release-list inspection found only alpha.1 and alpha.2, each publishing a Linux x86_64 archive and SHA256SUMS. Public archives downloaded and published archive hashes verified; selected file identities retained in public-release-identities.json. Both contain leading-v VERSION values, no compatibility.json and no MANIFEST.sha256. Local historical tags declare CURRENT_STATE_SCHEMA_VERSION1 and Cargo package version1.2.1; declaration is not an executed binary observation. No legacy executable was run during this inspection. Legacy runtime verification must recognize only verified historical file identities, not a general component-version exception. Config/state schema1 is a bounded eligibility policy, not a claim that the legacy artifacts are v1-qualified.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_LEGACY_POLICY/focused-tests.tap:172:# Subtest: legacy release cannot claim an unpublished platform\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_LEGACY_POLICY/focused-tests.tap:173:ok 35 - legacy release cannot claim an unpublished platform\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12a/independent-review.md:10:1. **Slice Claim:** Claim `PLAN-12_PR-12a` was atomically created in `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` by agent `antigravity` and recorded in `nexus-claims.log`.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12a/independent-review.md:12:3. **Hot-File Handling:** Required hot-file claims (`FILE_cli_src_index.ts`, `FILE_cli_src_sidecar.ts`, `FILE_cli_src_repl.ts`, `FILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md`, `FILE_quickstart.md`) were claimed prior to modification and released immediately upon verification.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_PERSISTENCE_COST_BASELINE/README.md:7:This is source performance evidence, not installed-RC qualification, durability/crash acceptance or a broad product-readiness pass. Raw logs, source/benchmark hashes, Node/kernel identity and exact command are retained. No inference or held-out data were used, and no load was applied to mike-dev. The local SUITE claim was held and released. Final implementation and exact-source measurement, migration/continuity regression coverage and independent acceptance remain outstanding.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RETENTION_JSON_METADATA/README.md:13:This is a source correction. Upgrade restore interruption remains a separate open blocker; final current-base review and exact-head CI are still required. No installed-RC, human, product or release acceptance is claimed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-08_PR-8a/verification.md:13:- Evidence limits: automated HOME isolation and real-sidecar tests only. No human terminal interaction or release qualification is claimed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_POST_REVIEW_TRANSACTION_FIXES/focused-tests.tap:172:# Subtest: legacy release cannot claim an unpublished platform\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_POST_REVIEW_TRANSACTION_FIXES/focused-tests.tap:173:ok 35 - legacy release cannot claim an unpublished platform\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_PR-10d/validation.md:11:- Qualification boundary: no RC-installed 40-task run, provider-matched comparison, or release qualification is claimed. Thresholds and task counts were not changed.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/context_stage7/RESULT_run_25208c1_r3_deep120.md:104:| TS CLI launches the Rust core | tools.ts:14–17 resolves `core/target/{release,debug}/harness-core`; tools.ts:209 `spawn(...)` | **no claim** (neither stated nor contradicted) |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:42:Every task was validated by the custodian in a bounded, atomically claimed `SUITE` window (claim log lines `CLAIM SUITE opencode v7/v8/v9/v10/v11`, each released with `RELEASE SUITE`). Rounds: batches 1–7 one round each (windows v7, v8); batches 8–9 and the repaired task two rounds each (v9–v11). Per-task logs: `reference/<id>.validation.log` in the store. Claim-log evidence: one `VALIDATED <id> rounds=N (<window>)` line per task; latest line governs.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/HELDOUT_CUSTODY/custody-report-2026-10-18.md:89:`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log`, 2026-10-18: `TRANSFER HELDOUT authorship` 02:25:21Z; `BROKEN CLAIM HELDOUT_AUTHORING_B8` 02:33:14Z; `ABORT … author-b8r` 02:35Z; `REJECT HELDOUT batch 9` 02:37Z; `CLAIM/RELEASE SUITE opencode v9` 02:4xZ–02:54:09Z, `v10` 02:5xZ–03:01:22Z, `v11` 03:0xZ–03:05Z; `CUSTODY NOTE v9`, `CUSTODY HOLD` 02:54:09Z; `VALIDATED` lines per task; `BOUNDARY REQUEST (QUALIFICATION BLOCKER)` 03:05:08Z.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12b/independent-review.md:18:1. **Slice Claim:** Claim `PLAN-12_PR-12b` was atomically acquired under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/PLAN-12_PR-12b` and logged to `nexus-claims.log`.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-12_PR-12b/independent-review.md:20:3. **Hot-File Handling:** Short-lived hot-file claims were taken for `FILE_install.sh`, `FILE_scripts_package-linux.sh`, `FILE_cli_src_index.ts`, and `FILE_docs_USER_MANUAL.md`, held only while modifying, tested, and released immediately.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/custody-report-2026-10-17.md:59:- The on-disk corpus is **authored under the `HELDOUT_AUTHORING` claim**, whose `owner.json` names `claude-lead (delegated to an isolated author subagent)`. It is **not** the implementing agent (codex). Whether `claude-lead` is independent of the implementation session (no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history) is **not evidenced** in the store and must be confirmed (see `heldout-authorship-handoff-2026-10-17.md`).\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:7:| Claim protocol | `SUITE` taken atomically (`mkdir`), **ownership recheck before every phase** (owner.json agent+pid must match the watcher's own), released **only if still owned** at exit (claim log 18:56:33Z CLAIM → 19:24:21Z RELEASE; codex re-took at 19:24:39Z — no overlap) |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:37:`make build` **exit 0** (2m18s; `build-info.json`: commit `8cf3e820668a`, commitTime `2026-10-17T18:38:11+00:00`, `dirty:false`, branch null — detached worktree) → `make test` exit 2: **1103 tests / 1098 pass / 5 fail / 0 cancelled** (`full2.log`). The 5 failures all throw from `eval/isolate.mjs:149` (`mountProblem` in the bubblewrap sandbox setup): A1 deliverable verification, standalone server-profile discovery, both T4 smokes, task-path traversal. The identical suite passes **1149/1149** (plus Rust 281/281, evaluator rerun 21/21) on this machine from codex's `/home/mike/nexus-wt/p10g-oracle` worktree (claim-log release line 20:38:32Z). Working hypothesis: the harness sandbox's runtime-mount check rejects snapshots located under `/tmp/opencode`; product code is not implicated (my diff touches `cli/src/tokens.ts` comments + `cli/test/tokens*` only).\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:43:Watcher v3 aborted fail-closed immediately after taking the claim (20:38:51Z) and left its own dead-pid claim in place: its `owns_claim` pid pattern was corrupted by a quoted heredoc (`\\$` escaped the dollar → the pattern never matched). The stale claim was logged and released by the owner-of-record at 20:51:47Z; v4/v5 use a `printf`-built fixed-string pattern. codex's 20:44:48Z \"REQUEST SUITE release … codex will wait\" was honoured. No suites overlapped at any point.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:37:SUITE windows rotated codex ↔ opencode (v4, v5, v6, v7, v8) with zero overlaps; every opencode window took the claim atomically, rechecked ownership before executing, and released only its own claim. One protocol incident (v3 quoting bug, fail-closed) is documented in `test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md`.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:9:| Method | Full `git diff e1759ca..HEAD` review; standalone re-implementation of the estimator (`node`, scratch at `/tmp/opencode/dec17-arith.mjs`, logic transcribed from `cli/src/tokens.ts` — repo test infra NOT imported, suite NOT run); claim-store inspection (`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`); repo-wide greps for stale references |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:61:- `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:189` — \"8 fault classes\" while listing nine (:191-199). **Known outstanding**: file claimed by codex (`nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_ACCEPTANCE.md/owner.json`), handoff recorded in-branch (handoff-codex-t4-acceptance-2026-10-17.md). As represented by the slice. ✓\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:62:- `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:17,39,49` — **not covered by any handoff** and not mentioned in verification.md's \"Not in this slice\" list, yet still asserts the T4 denominator conflict and the CJK/Hangul acceptance conflict \"remain unresolved owner/spec decisions\" and advises \"Decide a compatible acceptance contract … do not call ACC-VER-07 passed\" — both now decided by this PR. File is claimed by codex (`nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json`), so the slice correctly did not edit it — but it also did not hand it off. Issue 1 below.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:67:REQUIREMENTS.md:153 keeps REQ-AGT-118 `partial` with \"Changed-test execution and independent review are **pending**\". Reality matches: docs + test/fixture changed; the SUITE claim is held by codex (verified: `nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json`, pid 532551, since 2026-10-17T17:24:09Z); verification.md:29,32 explicitly defers execution, states a ledger pass \"is not behavioural acceptance\", and lists the re-run steps. This reviewer likewise did not run the suite. REQ-QUAL-105 staying `tested` is defensible: the injector/smoke tests (EVL-001) are unchanged and the 8→9 correction is docs-only. ✓\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/heldout-authorship-handoff-2026-10-17.md:12:- The `HELDOUT_AUTHORING` claim (`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/HELDOUT_AUTHORING`) is held by `claude-lead (delegated to an isolated author subagent)` for store `~/nexus-heldout`, recorded as **\"batch 1 of 4: 10 T2 tasks\"**.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/heldout-authorship-handoff-2026-10-17.md:21:2. **Request transfer at the next safe boundary** — i.e. when the current authoring session pauses or completes a batch. The transfer is recorded in `nexus-claims.log`; the receiving session takes a fresh `HELDOUT_AUTHORING` claim.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.14/scripted-pty/attempt-20261030T2350Z/attempt-status.json:10:  \"reason\": \"This duplicate diagnostic run used the current checkout's legacy D_pty driver, whose assumptions do not match the installed RC14 prompt flow in the REPL cases and whose s4/s6 scripts cancel immediately after queuing steering. Earlier targeted RC14 reruns and an independent review are already recorded in nexus-claims.log; this capture does not supersede or invalidate that accepted evidence and is not counted toward §5.2.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RMW_TRANSACTION_RECOVERY/README.md:17:Prior green hosted CI run39351903121 and scoped review belong to base bbfe9c0 and do not close this new full-diff finding. This patch requires independent re-review and new exact-head CI before integration. No RC, human, product or release acceptance is claimed.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":346686137}},"started_at_ms":1793620876550,"completed_at_ms":1793620876898}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:01:24.902Z","ordinal":41017,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19c22-bda5-7fc2-b9e5-0dc8d047862f","call_id":"call_452cccaea9e849ee8733f1273865129e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 10.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 15069)\nTotal output lines: 224\n\n# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\nThese files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n\n| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately befor…12669 tokens truncated…orking hypothesis: the harness sandbox's runtime-mount check rejects snapshots located under `/tmp/opencode`; product code is not implicated (my diff touches `cli/src/tokens.ts` comments + `cli/test/tokens*` only).\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md:43:Watcher v3 aborted fail-closed immediately after taking the claim (20:38:51Z) and left its own dead-pid claim in place: its `owns_claim` pid pattern was corrupted by a quoted heredoc (`\\$` escaped the dollar → the pattern never matched). The stale claim was logged and released by the owner-of-record at 20:51:47Z; v4/v5 use a `printf`-built fixed-string pattern. codex's 20:44:48Z \"REQUEST SUITE release … codex will wait\" was honoured. No suites overlapped at any point.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/post-integration-2026-10-18.md:37:SUITE windows rotated codex ↔ opencode (v4, v5, v6, v7, v8) with zero overlaps; every opencode window took the claim atomically, rechecked ownership before executing, and released only its own claim. One protocol incident (v3 quoting bug, fail-closed) is documented in `test-evidence-snapshot-8cf3e82.md`.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:9:| Method | Full `git diff e1759ca..HEAD` review; standalone re-implementation of the estimator (`node`, scratch at `/tmp/opencode/dec17-arith.mjs`, logic transcribed from `cli/src/tokens.ts` — repo test infra NOT imported, suite NOT run); claim-store inspection (`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`); repo-wide greps for stale references |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:61:- `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:189` — \"8 fault classes\" while listing nine (:191-199). **Known outstanding**: file claimed by codex (`nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_ACCEPTANCE.md/owner.json`), handoff recorded in-branch (handoff-codex-t4-acceptance-2026-10-17.md). As represented by the slice. ✓\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:62:- `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:17,39,49` — **not covered by any handoff** and not mentioned in verification.md's \"Not in this slice\" list, yet still asserts the T4 denominator conflict and the CJK/Hangul acceptance conflict \"remain unresolved owner/spec decisions\" and advises \"Decide a compatible acceptance contract … do not call ACC-VER-07 passed\" — both now decided by this PR. File is claimed by codex (`nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json`), so the slice correctly did not edit it — but it also did not hand it off. Issue 1 below.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/independent-review-dec17.md:67:REQUIREMENTS.md:153 keeps REQ-AGT-118 `partial` with \"Changed-test execution and independent review are **pending**\". Reality matches: docs + test/fixture changed; the SUITE claim is held by codex (verified: `nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json`, pid 532551, since 2026-10-17T17:24:09Z); verification.md:29,32 explicitly defers execution, states a ledger pass \"is not behavioural acceptance\", and lists the re-run steps. This reviewer likewise did not run the suite. REQ-QUAL-105 staying `tested` is defensible: the injector/smoke tests (EVL-001) are unchanged and the 8→9 correction is docs-only. ✓\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/heldout-authorship-handoff-2026-10-17.md:12:- The `HELDOUT_AUTHORING` claim (`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/HELDOUT_AUTHORING`) is held by `claude-lead (delegated to an isolated author subagent)` for store `~/nexus-heldout`, recorded as **\"batch 1 of 4: 10 T2 tasks\"**.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/GOV_DEC_AMENDMENTS/heldout-authorship-handoff-2026-10-17.md:21:2. **Request transfer at the next safe boundary** — i.e. when the current authoring session pauses or completes a batch. The transfer is recorded in `nexus-claims.log`; the receiving session takes a fresh `HELDOUT_AUTHORING` claim.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.14/scripted-pty/attempt-20261030T2350Z/attempt-status.json:10:  \"reason\": \"This duplicate diagnostic run used the current checkout's legacy D_pty driver, whose assumptions do not match the installed RC14 prompt flow in the REPL cases and whose s4/s6 scripts cancel immediately after queuing steering. Earlier targeted RC14 reruns and an independent review are already recorded in nexus-claims.log; this capture does not supersede or invalidate that accepted evidence and is not counted toward §5.2.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-04_RMW_TRANSACTION_RECOVERY/README.md:17:Prior green hosted CI run39351903121 and scoped review belong to base bbfe9c0 and do not close this new full-diff finding. This patch requires independent re-review and new exact-head CI before integration. No RC, human, product or release acceptance is claimed.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","create_time":1793620884.9017808}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
