{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:09:28.129Z","ordinal":41468,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6c9ad6e3-4bd9-4d9e-b439-316fc8d7f937","process_id":"21487","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","find /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf '%f\\n' | sort | tail -n 80 && sed -n '1,220p' docs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md && sed -n '1,180p' docs/v1.1.0/COLLABORATION.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"list_files","cmd":"find /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf \"%f\\\\n\"","path":"nexus-claims"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' docs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md","name":"STATUS.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,180p' docs/v1.1.0/COLLABORATION.md","name":"COLLABORATION.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/COLLABORATION.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":".claims.lock\nnexus-claims.lock\nnexus-claims.log\nnexus-claims.log.lock\n# v1.1.0 programme status\n\nDurable state of the v1.1.0 programme. A new lead agent can resume from this file alone. Update it at every\ncheckpoint; never record a state the evidence does not support.\n\nLast updated: 2026-10-31T23:33Z\nBranch: `v1/v11-release` · Worktree: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v11-release`\nBaseline: `origin/main` `bed30a90` (PRs #372, #373, #374 merged) ·\n`v1.0.0` tag `501eab68` (published 2026-10-31T11:22Z)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Current gate\n\n**Gates 1–3 complete. All work packages WP-1 through WP-7 and V11-QUALITY-04 are fully implemented, verified,\nindependently reviewed, and merged into `origin/main` across PR #372 (`9a8fe2d5`), PR #373 (`d10ef418`), and\nPR #374 (`bed30a90`). CI matrices (Node 22, 24), dual container packaging (`package-linux.sh`), bit-for-bit\nreproducibility comparison (`cmp`), CycloneDX SBOM validation, and package/installer smoke tests passed.**\n\nRemote annotated tags `v1.1.0-rc.1` and `v1.1.0` exist prematurely at `ba9764bc` and `4789bb7c`. Both Release\nworkflows failed the main-ancestry gate (runs 41234889855 and 41234889861), and no GitHub release was created.\nThey are unqualified and must not be published.\nAll quality fixes are now safely committed to `origin/main`. Tagging and publishing the qualified release candidate\nand stable release is reserved for the owner per project guidelines.\n\n| Gate | State |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Repository baseline and roadmap reconciliation | complete (`ROADMAP-REVIEW.md`) |\n| 2. Specification, xerj research, collaboration plan | complete (`SPEC.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `COLLABORATION.md`) |\n| 3. Implementation in reviewable increments | complete (WP-1..7 and V11-QUALITY-04 merged on `main`) |\n| 4. Full regression and RC qualification | complete on `origin/main` (CI run 41249622550, 41245766686, 41241366953 green) |\n| 5. Release preparation and publication | candidate ready on `origin/main` `bed30a90`; handover to owner for tag/push/publication |\n\n## 2. Documents\n\n| Document | Purpose | State |\n|---|---|---|\n| [`ROADMAP-REVIEW.md`](ROADMAP-REVIEW.md) | Baseline, merged-vs-proposed reconciliation, defect register, traceability | Complete |\n| [`SPEC.md`](SPEC.md) | Normative specification and acceptance criteria | Complete; updated for every shipped shape |\n| [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](REQUIREMENTS.md) | Enforced acceptance ledger (`check_requirements.mjs --ledger`) | 10 required rows, all `tested` |\n| [`COLLABORATION.md`](COLLABORATION.md) | Work packages, frozen contracts, boundaries, integration order | Complete |\n| [`VALIDATION.md`](VALIDATION.md) | Gate definitions, E2E scenarios, migration checks, execution record | Gate definitions complete; record below |\n| [`DECISIONS.md`](DECISIONS.md) | xerj configuration and research log, decisions, open questions | Complete |\n| [`STATUS.md`](STATUS.md) | This file | Living |\n\n## 3. Commits and work packages\n\nBranch `v1/v11-release`, based on `v1/v11-lead-program` at `853c6333`.\n\n| Commit | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `acc48688` | Planning: roadmap review, spec, collaboration plan, validation plan, decisions, status |\n| `d2de3941` | WP-1..WP-3: schema v2 + migration + strict specs + terminal safety; deterministic parallel due-sets; batch runner, integration queue, evidenced receipts |\n| `844854cc` | WP-4..WP-7: typed message channel; replay; estimate provenance; v1.1 ledger; documentation reconciliation |\n| `e22ed4c9` | Independent-review fixes (slot validation, per-recipient delivery, WORK_INTEGRATED, save guard, quarantine, tests) |\n| `ade106b4` | Real v1.0.0 migration fixture; defect dispositions |\n| `fa63a482` | Merge of `origin/main` `7b49e6ff`; README conflict resolved; competing scope recorded |\n| `003d5f7e` | §2.5 dispositions for the parallel post-v1 roadmap; Q6 |\n| `853c6333` | lead-programme execution record; independent reviews subsequently requested changes |\n| `d44e7a87`..`3c727547` | release acceptance tests and real crash evidence; generalized RC repro; persistence and runner review fixes; premature RC1/stable metadata preserved without qualification; acceptance ledger bound to evidence |\n| `76a6b1ca` | PR #373: V11-QUALITY-04 cancellation idempotency, durability-positive acknowledgment, replay future envelope guard |\n| `34f63119`..`c7bb2270` | PR #374: V11-QUALITY-04 genuine prompt submission provenance, tool-result non-suppression, non-vacuous recovery hook assertion, no-ID replay propagation |\n| `9a8fe2d5`, `d10ef418`, `bed30a90` | Merged to `origin/main` with 100% green CI matrix (Node 22, 24, CodeQL, linux-x86_64 dual packaging, cmp, cyclonedx, smoke tests) |\n\n| WP | Title | State | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| WP-1 | Schema v2, migration, spec validation, terminal safety | **complete** | `cli/test/operation_schema.test.ts` (13) |\n| WP-2 | Scheduler due-set, determinism, reservation | **complete** | `cli/test/operation_concurrency.test.ts` (scheduler cases) |\n| WP-3 | Runner batch, integration queue, cancellation, recovery, receipts | **complete** | same file (runner/git cases), `cli/test/operation_git.test.ts` |\n| WP-4 | Inter-agent channel | **complete** | `cli/test/operation_messages.test.ts` (8) |\n| WP-5 | Replay | **complete** | `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts` (34) |\n| WP-6 | Requirements ledger | **complete** | `check_requirements.mjs --ledger … --enforce` |\n| WP-7 | Documentation and release-process fixes | **complete** | corrected proposals, CHANGELOG, release notes, PROTECTIONS |\n| WP-8 | PR publication | **deferred to v1.2** (DEC-V11-12); rejected fail-closed in v1.1 | — |\n| WP-9 | TUI pane, semantic retrieval | **deferred to v1.2** (DEC-V11-13/14) | — |\n\n## 4. Verification actually executed\n\nOnly what is listed here was run. Anything else is planned (`VALIDATION.md` §2–§8).\n\n| Date (UTC) | Commit | Check | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline requirements | `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` | PASS — 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals |\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline release | `gh release list`, `gh release view v1.0.0` | `v1.0.0` published, not draft; body still says acceptance `IN_PROGRESS` |\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline version sync | inspection of the five version-bearing files | all `1.0.0` |\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline divergence | `git rev-list --count main..origin/main` | local `main` carries 2 unpushed user commits, preserved untouched |\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline suite failures | `npm --prefix cli test` on a clean snapshot | **not green**: 7 failures in `team_convergence.test.ts`, reproduced identically on unmodified `origin/main` before the core binary was built (environmental: `Rust core RPC daemon disconnected`). Re-run after `cargo build --release` — see the row below. |\n| 2026-10-31 | various | TypeScript | `npx tsc --noEmit -p cli` | PASS after every increment |\n| 2026-10-31 | various | focused suites | `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs <files>` | operation_schema 13/13, operation_concurrency 15/15, operation_messages 8/8, operation_view 34/34, context_management 22/22, operation_git + convergence_scheduling + convergence_scheduler_properties + check_requirements — **193/193 across the nine affected suites** |\n| 2026-10-31 | `e22ed4c9` | v1.1 ledger | `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --ledger docs/v1.1.0/REQUIREMENTS.md --enforce` | PASS — 10 rows, 10 tested |\n| 2026-10-31 | working tree | v1.0 ledger | `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` | rows unchanged (123 / 108 / 6 / 2 / 7; 12 deferrals); the clean-worktree precondition fails while the branch is dirty, as designed |\n| 2026-10-31 | `d2de3941` | full CLI suite on a snapshot | `npm --prefix cli test` in `/tmp/opencode/v11-suite` | **result recorded in §4.1** |\n\n### 4.1 Full-suite result\n\nSee the entry appended at the end of this section after the run completed. A full suite is executed on a **snapshot\nworktree**, never on the tree being edited (CONCURRENCY §3).\n\n- `d2de3941` (WP-1..3, before WP-4..7 and the review fixes): see `SUITE-d2de3941` below.\n- `e22ed4c9` (final candidate for this session): see `SUITE-e22ed4c9` below.\n\n<!-- SUITE-RESULTS-START -->\n_Not yet appended._ The d2de3941 snapshot run was started at 17:5xZ and had not terminated when this file was\nwritten; its log is `/tmp/opencode/suite-d2de3941.log` (this path is local to the operator host and is not durable\nevidence — the numbers must be copied here when it finishes).\n<!-- SUITE-RESULTS-END -->\n\n### 4.2 Not executed\n\n| Check | Why |\n|---|---|\n| Rust suite (`cargo test --locked`) | not run in this session; the release build succeeded (`cargo build --release --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui`, exit 0) and was required for the CLI tests to reach the core handshake |\n| `bash scripts/security_gates.sh` | not run |\n| Packaging (`package-linux.sh` ×2), SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, `installer-smoke.sh` | not run |\n| Installed-RC qualification (`VALIDATION.md` §8 stages 3–6) | no RC tag, no artifact, no authorization |\n| Cross-runner reproducibility | `repro.yml` is pinned to the v1.0.0 RC regex; not dispatched |\n| Independent acceptance of an RC | no RC exists |\n| Inference/provider checks | none required by this scope; no GATEWAY claim taken |\n\n## 5. Known risks and owed work\n\n| Risk / gap | Impact | State |\n|---|---|---|\n| A real process kill during a live two-unit batch is not demonstrated | `ACC-V11-MAO-07` is demonstrated from a persisted two-`RUNNING` state through a real store, not by killing a process | open |\n| Crash between integration enqueue and merge | `ACC-V11-GIT-02` not demonstrated | open |\n| Cancel between enqueue and drain | `ACC-V11-GIT-04` not demonstrated | open |\n| Checkpoint restore → resume verification consequence | `ACC-V11-CTX-04` not demonstrated (inherited from v1.0.0 prose-only claim) | open |\n| `repro.yml` pinned to `^v1\\.0\\.0-rc\\.\\d+$` | a v1.1.0 RC cannot run cross-runner reproducibility until edited | open (Q5) |\n| v1.0.0 qualification gaps inherited | stable v1.1.0 publication is gated on an owner decision | open (Q1) |\n| v1.0.0 release notes/CHANGELOG were stale at publication | operators read a published release that says it is unreleased; CHANGELOG now correct for v1.0.0, release body still stale on GitHub | open (Q2) |\n| `git diff --exit-code -- cli/dist` in CI is a no-op (dist is untracked) | the step proves nothing | open, documented (`ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` D-V11-07); changing CI needs owner approval |\n| v1.0 ledger `--enforce` requires a clean worktree | the gate cannot pass mid-branch; expected, and it is why the v1.1 ledger uses `--ledger` | by design |\n| Two documents on `main` claim \"v1.1.0\" (the four implemented proposals and the merged WP-11xx roadmap) | release naming and notes are blocked until the owner decides | open (Q6) |\n| `origin/main` moved during the review and now carries a TypeScript 7 dependency bump | verified: `tsc --noEmit` clean, `cli` build clean, 195/195 focused after `npm ci` on TS 7.0.2 | resolved, but the final suite must run on the merged commit |\n\n## 6. Claims held\n\n`$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`: `V11_RELEASE_20261031`, `DOCS_V11_RELEASE`, and `FILE_`\nclaims for `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts`, `operation_runner_execution.ts`, `operation_runner_persistence.ts`,\n`operation_messages.ts`, and `cli/src/operation_cli.ts`. The v11-lead program claims were released before this lane\nstarted. Completed state/repro/v1.0-notes claims were released and logged.\n\n**Not claimed and not used:** `GATEWAY` (no inference run). The repaired full suite must run alone on a snapshot;\nthe two earlier concurrent runs are not accepted evidence.\n\n## 7. Next action\n\n1. Obtain V11-QUALITY-04 plan approval, retrieve the four runtime contracts with XERJ, complete RED/GREEN, and get\n   independent spec and quality approval on the exact repaired head.\n2. Run the full CLI suite alone on a snapshot of that head, plus TypeScript, the v1.1 ledger, Rust and security gates.\n3. Prepare `1.1.0-rc.2` metadata and notes without tagging; run pinned packaging, SBOM, package and installer smoke.\n4. Merge the reviewed RC through draft PR #372, tag the exact main commit, and run installed-RC and cross-runner\n   qualification with independent acceptance.\n5. Resolve the premature stable-tag collision through the documented owner-safe repair path. Do not publish the\n   existing unqualified tag and do not create a replacement tag without that resolution.\n\n## 8. Resumption checklist\n\n1. Read this file, then `ROADMAP-REVIEW.md` §1 and §4, then `SPEC.md` §1 (scope) and §10 (acceptance).\n2. `git log --oneline -10`; compare with §3. A foreign commit means reconcile before editing.\n3. Check `nexus-claims/` for the claims in §6.\n4. Re-run `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --ledger docs/v1.1.0/REQUIREMENTS.md --enforce`; if it fails, the ledger\n   and the tests disagree and the ledger's evidence column is wrong.\n5. Continue at §7.\n# v1.1.0 multi-agent collaboration plan\n\nStatus: normative for how v1.1.0 work is partitioned and integrated. Rules of engagement remain\n`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`; this document adds the v1.1 work packages, contracts, and integration order.\n\nLead: `v11-lead` (branch `v1/v11-lead-program`, worktree `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v11-lead`).\nSpec: [`SPEC.md`](SPEC.md). Traceability: [`ROADMAP-REVIEW.md`](ROADMAP-REVIEW.md) §4.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Ownership model\n\n- **One lead agent** is accountable for architecture, contracts, integration, traceability and release readiness.\n  The lead owns this plan and `SPEC.md`; a behaviour change without a spec update is incomplete.\n- **Work packages (WPs)** are the unit of delegation. A WP is bounded, independently useful, and has one owner.\n- **File boundaries** are exclusive. Two agents never edit the same file in parallel; a shared file is serialised\n  through a hot-file claim (CONCURRENCY §4) and the lead schedules it.\n- **Contracts** (§3) are frozen before implementation. An agent that needs a contract change stops and requests it\n  from the lead; it does not improvise a second shape.\n\n## 2. Work packages\n\n| WP | Title | Owner (role) | Depends on | Parallel-safe with | Files owned |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| WP-1 | Schema v2, migration, spec validation, terminal safety | Agent A | — | WP-5, WP-7 | `cli/src/core/operation.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts` (new), `cli/src/operation_cli.ts`, `cli/src/operation_view.ts`, `cli/test/operation_schema.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts`, `docs/v1.1.0/operation-view.schema.json` |\n| WP-2 | Scheduler due-set, determinism, resource reservation | Agent B | WP-1 contract only | WP-5, WP-7 | `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation.ts` (types section only, after WP-1 lands), `cli/test/v11_scheduler_concurrency.test.ts` (new) |\n| WP-3 | Runner batch execution, integration queue, cancellation, recovery, receipts | Agent C | WP-1, WP-2 | WP-7 | `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_git.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts`, `cli/test/v11_runner_concurrency.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/operation_git.test.ts` |\n| WP-4 | Inter-agent channel: model, delivery, CLI, summary publication | Agent D | WP-1 (types), WP-3 (delivery hook) | WP-5, WP-7 | `cli/src/core/operation_messages.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` (delivery only), `cli/src/operation_cli.ts` (message command only), `cli/test/v11_messages.test.ts` (new) |\n| WP-5 | Operation replay | Agent E | WP-1 (view schema) | WP-2, WP-4, WP-7 | `cli/src/operation_view.ts` (replay section only), `cli/src/operation_cli.ts` (`--replay` only), `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts` (replay cases) |\n| WP-6 | Requirements ledger and traceability enforcement | Agent F | WP-1..WP-5 acceptance IDs | none | `docs/v1.1.0/REQUIREMENTS.md` (new), `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` (v1.1 ledger support only) |\n| WP-7 | Documentation, release notes, changelog, release-process fixes | Agent G | WP-1..WP-5 | WP-2..WP-5 | `docs/v1.1.0/*.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/releases/v1.1.0*.md`, `docs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md`, `README.md` |\n| WP-8 | PR publication (deferred) | unassigned | — | — | `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md` §5.5 only until v1.2 |\n| WP-9 | TUI pane / semantic retrieval (deferred) | unassigned | — | — | — |\n\n### 2.1 Why this order\n\n1. **WP-1 first.** Everything else reads `DurableOperationState`. If the schema gate and migration land after the\n   scheduler, the scheduler's tests would encode a shape that later changes, and the migration test would have to be\n   rewritten. WP-1 also repairs two defects (D-V11-01, D-V11-02) that are independent of concurrency and would\n   otherwise be buried in a large diff.\n2. **WP-2 before WP-3.** The scheduler is pure and cheap to test exhaustively; the runner is I/O and expensive. A\n   due-set bug found in WP-2 costs minutes; the same bug inside the runner costs a flaky suite.\n3. **WP-3 before WP-4.** Message delivery happens at the same `save()` as the `RUNNING` transition. That hook lives\n   in the runner, so the runner must be stable first.\n4. **WP-5 is independent** of concurrency and can run in parallel from the moment WP-1's view schema bumps.\n5. **WP-6 and WP-7 last** so they record what actually shipped, not what was planned.\n\n## 3. Frozen contracts\n\nThese are the only shapes agents share. Changing one requires a lead decision recorded in\n[`DECISIONS.md`](DECISIONS.md).\n\n### 3.1 `Decision.run` batch form\n\n```ts\nexport interface Assignment { unit: WorkUnit; resource: ResourceDescriptor; reroutedFrom?: Reroute }\nexport type Decision =\n  | { kind: \"run\"; assignments: Assignment[] }     // length >= 1, deterministic order, no shared single-slot resource\n  | { kind: \"wait\"; wakeAt: number; reason: string; parked: string[] }\n  | { kind: \"complete\" }\n  | { kind: \"blocked\"; decisions: EscalationDecision[] };\n```\n\nOwner: WP-2. Consumer: WP-3. WP-3 MUST accept a batch of length 1 and MUST NOT special-case `length === 1`.\n\n### 3.2 Operation schema version\n\n```ts\nexport const CURRENT_OPERATION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2;\nexport function migrateOperationState(raw: unknown): DurableOperationState;  // throws UnsupportedOperationSchemaError\nexport function effectiveConcurrency(state: DurableOperationState): number;  // policy.maxConcurrentUnits ?? 1\n```\n\nOwner: WP-1. Consumers: WP-2 (`effectiveConcurrency`), WP-3, WP-4, WP-5, the view.\n\n### 3.3 Message model\n\n```ts\nexport type OperationMessageKind = \"request\" | \"observation\" | \"artifact\" | \"verdict\";\nexport interface OperationMessage { id; at; from; to; kind; body; refs?; deliveredAt?; deliveredTo? }\nexport function publishMessage(state, msg: Omit<OperationMessage,\"id\"|\"at\">, now: number): OperationMessage;\nexport function undeliveredFor(state, unitId: string): OperationMessage[];   // <= 20, oldest first\nexport function markDelivered(state, ids: string[], unitId: string, at: string): void;\n```\n\nOwner: WP-4. Consumer: WP-3 (calls `undeliveredFor`/`markDelivered` in the save that starts a unit).\n\n### 3.4 Receipt extension\n\n```ts\ncandidate?: { digest: string; scope: \"tree\" | \"commit\" };\ntests?: { command: string; status: string; hasExecutedTests: boolean };\nsequence: number;\n```\n\nOwner: WP-3. Consumer: WP-4 (`refs` to a receipt), WP-5 (nothing — replay reads events only).\n\n### 3.5 View document\n\n`schemaVersion` becomes `2`; adds `replay?: { schemaVersion: 1; entries: ReplayEntry[] }`; `additionalProperties:\nfalse` everywhere. Owner: WP-1 (bump) and WP-5 (contents). Any other agent adding a view field must coordinate with\nboth.\n\n## 4. File and hot-file discipline\n\nPer CONCURRENCY §2, claims are directories under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`.\n\n| File | WPs | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/core/operation.ts` | WP-1, WP-2, WP-4 | Serialised. WP-1 first (schema/version), then WP-2 (Decision/Assignment), then WP-4 (message fields). Each change is a separate commit. |\n| `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts` | WP-2 only | Exclusive claim. |\n| `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts` | WP-3 only | Exclusive claim. |\n| `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` | WP-3, WP-4 | WP-3 lands first; WP-4 adds only the message-delivery block and the prompt heading, in a separate commit. |\n| `cli/src/operation_cli.ts` | WP-1, WP-4, WP-5 | One agent at a time; each adds a distinct command/flag block. |\n| `cli/src/operation_view.ts` | WP-1, WP-5 | WP-1 (sanitisation + schema bump), then WP-5 (replay). |\n| `docs/v1.1.0/operation-view.schema.json` | WP-1, WP-5 | WP-1 bumps the version; WP-5 adds `replay`. |\n| `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts` | WP-1, WP-5 | Serialised; append-only per WP. |\n| `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/releases/*` | WP-7 only | Exclusive. |\n\nEvery agent runs `git rev-parse HEAD` and `git log <mine>..HEAD` before each commit and stops on a foreign commit\n(CONCURRENCY §5.1).\n\n## 5. Integration order and checkpoints\n\n| Checkpoint | Entry | Exit criteria | Review |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| CP-0 | Baseline recorded | `origin/main` sha, v1.0 gate status, claims reconciled (this document + ROADMAP-REVIEW §1) | Lead |\n| CP-1 | WP-1 merged into `v1/v11-lead-program` | Schema/migration/spec/safety tests green; no other test changed behaviour | Lead + independent reviewer |\n| CP-2 | WP-2 merged | Scheduler property tests green (1,000 shuffles); concurrency 1 byte-identical outcomes | Lead + independent reviewer |\n| CP-3 | WP-3 merged | Batch execution, queue, cancellation, crash-resume tests green; full CLI suite green | Lead + independent reviewer |\n| CP-4 | WP-4 merged | Channel tests green; dependent-unit prompt exactness | Lead |\n| CP-5 | WP-5 merged | Replay tests green; view schema v2 validates | Lead |\n| CP-6 | WP-6 + WP-7 merged | `check_requirements --enforce` green with v1.1 rows; docs accurate | Lead + independent reviewer |\n| CP-7 | RC qualification | `VALIDATION.md` gates G1–G4 executed on the exact commit | Independent acceptance |\n\nA checkpoint is not \"tests passed\". It is \"the WP's acceptance IDs are demonstrated with named evidence, the diff\nwas reviewed by someone other than its author, and no other WP's acceptance regressed\".\n\n## 6. Assignment briefs\n\nEach brief below is complete enough to hand to a fresh agent with no conversation history. The lead fills in\n`<commit>` and `<WP>` when delegating.\n\n### 6.1 WP-1 — Schema v2, migration, spec validation, terminal safety\n\n**Objective.** Make `DurableOperationState` versioned and fail closed, reject unknown spec keys, and complete\nterminal safety in the operation view.\n\n**In scope.** `CURRENT_OPERATION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`; `migrateOperationState`; `UnsupportedOperationSchemaError`;\nload-time invariants; `.pre-migration-v1` backup of the whole record before the first v2 write; strict spec\nvalidation for top level, `policy`, `git`, and each unit; `safeTerminal` on `view.status`/`unit.status`; the view\nschema validator keyword completion.\n\n**Explicitly out of scope.** Any scheduler or runner change; the `Decision` type; message fields; replay; the\n`git.publish` implementation (it must be rejected, not built).\n\n**Spec.** §4.1–§4.5, §7.6, §12.2. **Acceptance.** ACC-V11-SCHEMA-01..04, ACC-V11-SPEC-01/02, ACC-V11-SAFE-01/02.\n\n**Owned files.** As in §2 WP-1. **Do not touch** `scheduler.ts`, `operation_runner*.ts`, `docs/v1.0.0/**`.\n\n**Deliverables.**\n1. `cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts` with the constant, the migration, the invariant checker and the error class.\n2. `cli/test/operation_schema.test.ts` with a checked-in v1.0.0 fixture (`cli/test/fixtures/operation-v1.json`) that\n   is a real record captured from a v1.0.0 run, not hand-written to fit the migration.\n3. Spec-validation tests using a temporary JSON file and the real CLI entry point.\n4. A hostile-record test injecting `\\x1b]52;…\\x07` into `unit.status` and asserting no ESC in `--dag` output.\n5. `operation-view.schema.json` version 2 with a validator that fails on an unimplemented keyword.\n\n**Checks.**\n```\nnode scripts/run_tests.mjs test/operation_schema.test.ts test/operation_view.test.ts\nnode scripts/run_tests.mjs test/operation_git.test.ts test/convergence_scheduling.test.ts   # non-regression\nnpx tsc --noEmit -p cli\n```\n\n**Handoff format.** A commit on a `v1/wp1-*` branch, a report listing changed files, the commands run and their\nexit codes, acceptance IDs demonstrated with the test name that proves each, and any acceptance ID not demonstrated\nwith the reason. Open risks go in the report, not in a comment.\n\n**Blockers.** If the v1.0.0 fixture cannot be produced without running an inference provider, stop and ask the lead;\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":762177912}},"started_at_ms":1793621367366,"completed_at_ms":1793621368129}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:09:29.602Z","ordinal":41469,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19c2a-2302-76f0-99a5-ae1cf4a92512","call_id":"call_8c25686dab344753bdaeb12ab66bfb18","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 6159)\nTotal output lines: 348\n\n.claims.lock\nnexus-claims.lock\nnexus-claims.log\nnexus-claims.log.lock\n# v1.1.0 programme status\n\nDurable state of the v1.1.0 programme. A new lead agent can resume from this file alone. Update it at every\ncheckpoint; never record a state the evidence does not support.\n\nLast updated: 2026-10-31T23:33Z\nBranch: `v1/v11-release` · Worktree: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v11-release`\nBaseline: `origin/main` `bed30a90` (PRs #372, #373, #374 merged) ·\n`v1.0.0` tag `501eab68` (published 2026-10-31T11:22Z)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Current gate\n\n**Gates 1–3 complete. All work packages WP-1 through WP-7 and V11-QUALITY-04 are fully implemented, verified,\nindependently reviewed, and merged into `origin/main` across PR #372 (`9a8fe2d5`), PR #373 (`d10ef418`), and\nPR #374 (`bed30a90`). CI matrices (Node 22, 24), dual container packaging (`package-linux.sh`), bit-for-bit\nreproducibility comparison (`cmp`), CycloneDX SBOM validation, and package/installer smoke tests passed.**\n\nRemote annotated tags `v1.1.0-rc.1` and `v1.1.0` exist prematurely at `ba9764bc` and `4789bb7c`. Both Release\nworkflows failed the main-ancestry gate (runs 41234889855 and 41234889861), and no GitHub release was created.\nThey are unqualified and must not be published.\nAll quality fixes are now safely committed to `origin/main`. Tagging and publishing the qualified release candidate\nand stable release is reserved for the owner per project guidelines.\n\n| Gate | State |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Repository baseline and roadmap reconciliation | complete (`ROADMAP-REVIEW.md`) |\n| 2. Specification, xerj research, collaboration plan | complete (`SPEC.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `COLLABORATION.md`) |\n| 3. Implementation in reviewable increments | complete (WP-1..7 and V11-QUALITY-04 merged on `main`) |\n| 4. Full regression and RC qualification | complete on `origin/main` (CI run 41249622550, 41245766686, 41241366953 green) |\n| 5. Release preparation and publication | candidate ready on `origin/main` `bed30a90`; handover to owner for tag/push/publication |\n\n## 2. Documents\n\n| Document | Purpose | State |\n|---|---|---|\n| [`ROADMAP-REVIEW.md`](ROADMAP-REVIEW.md) | Baseline, merged-vs-proposed reconciliation, defect register, traceability | Complete |\n| [`SPEC.md`](SPEC.md) | Normative specification and acceptance criteria | Complete; updated for every shipped shape |\n| [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](REQUIREMENTS.md) | Enforced acceptance ledger (`check_requirements.mjs --ledger`) | 10 required rows, all `tested` |\n| [`COLLABORATION.md`](COLLABORATION.md) | Work packages, frozen contracts, boundaries, integration order | Complete |\n| [`VALIDATION.md`](VALIDATION.md) | Gate definitions, E2E scenarios, migration checks, execution record | Gate definitions complete; record below |\n| [`DECISIONS.md`](DECISIONS.md) | xerj configuration and research log, decisions, open questions | Complete |\n| [`STATUS.md`](STATUS.md) | This file | Living |\n\n## 3. Commits and work packages\n\nBranch `v1/v11-release`, based on `v1/v11-lead-program` at `853c6333`.\n\n| Commit | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `acc48688` | Planning: roadmap review, spec, collaboration plan, validation plan, decisions, status |\n| `d2de3941` | WP-1..WP-3: schema v2 + migration + strict specs + terminal safety; deterministic parallel due-sets; batch runner, integration queue, evidenced receipts |\n| `844854cc` | WP-4..WP-7: typed message channel; replay; estimate provenance; v1.1 ledger; documentation reconciliation |\n| `e22ed4c9` | Independent-review fixes (slot validation, per-recipient delivery, WORK_INTEGRATED, save guard, quarantine, tests) |\n| `ade106b4` | Real v1.0.0 migration fixture; defect dispositions |\n| `fa63a482` | Merge of `origin/main` `7b49e6ff`; README conflict resolved; competing scope recorded |\n| `003d5f7e` | §2.5 dispositions for the parallel post-v1 roadmap; Q6 |\n| `853c6333` | lead-programme execution record; independent reviews subsequently requested changes |\n| `d44e7a87`..`3c727547` | release acceptance tests and real crash evidence; generalized RC repro; persistence and runner review fixes; premature RC1/stable metadata preserved without qualification; acceptance ledger bound to evidence |\n| `76a6b1ca` | PR #373: V11-QUALITY-04 cancellation idempotency, durability-positive acknowledgment, replay future envelope guard |\n| `34f63119`..`c7bb2270` | PR #374: V11-QUALITY-04 genuine prompt submission provenance, tool-result non-suppression, non-vacuous recovery hook assertion, no-ID replay propagation |\n| `9a8fe2d5`, `d10ef418`, `bed30a90` | Merged to `origin/main` with 100% green CI matrix (Node 22, 24, CodeQL, linux-x86_64 dual packaging, cmp, cyclonedx, smoke tests) |\n\n| WP | Title | State | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| WP-1 | Schema v2, migration, spec validation, terminal safety | **complete** | `cli/test/operation_schema.test.ts` (13) |\n| WP-2 | Scheduler due-set, determinism, reservation | **complete** | `cli/test/operation_concurrency.test.ts` (scheduler cases) |\n| WP-3 | Runner batch, integration queue, cancellation, recovery, receipts | **complete** | same file (runner/git cases), `cli/test/operation_git.test.ts` |\n| WP-4 | Inter-agent channel | **complete** | `cli/test/operation_messages.test.ts` (8) |\n| WP-5 | Replay | **complete** | `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts` (34) |\n| WP-6 | Requirements ledger | **complete** | `check_requirements.mjs --ledger … --enforce` |\n| WP-7 | Documentation and release-process fixes | **complete** | corrected proposals, CHANGELOG, release notes, PROTECTIONS |\n| WP-8 | PR publication | **deferred to v1.2** (DEC-V11-12); rejected fail-closed in v1.1 | — |\n| WP-9 | TUI pane, semantic retrieval | **deferred to v1.2** (DEC-V11-13/14) | — |\n\n## 4. Verification actually executed\n\nOnly what is listed here was run. Anything else is planned (`VALIDATION.md` §2–§8).\n\n| Date (UTC) | Commit | Check | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline requirements | `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` | PASS — 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals |\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline release | `gh release list`, `gh release view v1.0.0` | `v1.0.0` published, not draft; body still says acceptance `IN_PROGRESS` |\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline version sync | inspection of the five version-bearing files | all `1.0.0` |\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline divergence | `git rev-list --count main..origin/main` | local `main` carries 2 unpushed user commits, preserved untouched |\n| 2026-10-31 | `c7d0b003` | baseline suite failures | `npm --prefix cli test` on a clean snapshot | **not green**: 7 failures in `team_convergence.test.ts`, reproduced identically on unmodified `origin/main` before the core binary was built (environmental: `Rust core RPC daemon disconnected`). Re-run after `cargo build --release` — see the row below. |\n| 2026-10-31 | various | TypeScript | `npx tsc --noEmit -p cli` | PASS after every increment |\n| 2026-10-31 | various | focused suites | `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs <files>` | operation_schema 13/13, operation_concurrency 15/15, operation_messages 8/8, operation_view 34/34, context_management 22/22, operation_git + convergence_scheduling + convergence_scheduler_properties + check_requirements — **193/193 across the nine affected suites** |\n| 2026-10-31 | `e22ed4c9` | v1.1 ledger | `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --ledger docs/v1.1.0/REQUIREMENTS.md --enforce` | PASS — 10 rows, 10 tested |\n| 2026-10-31 | working tree | v1.0 ledger | `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` | rows unchanged (123 / 108 / 6 / 2 / 7; 12 deferrals); the clean-worktree precondition fails while the branch is dirty, as designed |\n| 2026-10-31 | `d2de3941` | full CLI suite on a snapshot | `npm --prefix cli test` in `/tmp/opencode/v11-suite` | **result recorded in §4.1** |\n\n### 4.1 Full-suite result\n\nSee the entry appended at the end of this section after the run completed. A full suite is executed on a **snapshot\nworktree**, never on the tree being edited (CONCURRENCY §3).\n\n- `d2de3941` (WP-1..3, before WP-4..7 and the review fixes): see `SUITE-d2de3941` below.\n- `e22ed4c9` (final candidate for this session): see `SUITE-e22ed4c9` below.\n\n<!-- SUITE-RESULTS-START -->\n_Not yet appended._ The d2de3941 snapshot run was started at 17:5xZ and had not terminated when this file was\nwritten; its log is `/tmp/opencode/suite-d2de3941.log` (this path is local to the operator host and is not durable\nevidence — the numbers must be copied here when it finishes).\n<!-- SUITE-RESULTS-END -->\n\n### 4.2 Not executed\n\n| Check | Why |\n|---|---|\n| Rust suite (`cargo test --locked`) | not run in this session; the release build succeeded (`cargo build --release --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui`, exit 0) and was required for the CLI tests to reach the core handshake |\n| `bash scripts/security_gates.sh` | not run |\n| Packaging (`package-linux.sh` ×2), SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, `installer-smoke.sh` | not run |\n| Installed-RC qualification (`VALIDATION.md` §8 stages 3–6) | no RC tag, no artifact, no authorization |\n| Cross-runner reproducibility | `repro.yml` is pinned to the v1.0.0 RC regex; not dispatched |\n| Independent acceptance of an RC | no RC exists |\n| Inference/provider checks | none required by this scope; no GATEWAY claim taken |\n\n## 5. Known risks and owed work\n\n| Risk / gap | Impact | State |\n|---|---|---|\n| A real process kill during a live two-unit batch is not demonstrated | `ACC-V11-MAO-07` is demonstrated from a persisted two-`RUNNING` state through a real store, not by killing a process | open |\n| Crash between integration enqueue and merge | `ACC-V11-GIT-02` not demonstrated | open |\n| Cancel between enqueue and drain | `ACC-V11-GIT-04` not demonstrated | open |\n| Checkpoint restore → resume verification consequence | `ACC-V11-CTX-04` not demonstrated (inherited from v1.0.0 prose-only claim) | open |\n| `repro.yml` pinned to `^v1\\.0\\.0-rc\\.\\d+$` | a v1.1.0 RC cannot run cross-runner reprodu…1159 tokens truncated…heduler due-set, determinism, resource reservation | Agent B | WP-1 contract only | WP-5, WP-7 | `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation.ts` (types section only, after WP-1 lands), `cli/test/v11_scheduler_concurrency.test.ts` (new) |\n| WP-3 | Runner batch execution, integration queue, cancellation, recovery, receipts | Agent C | WP-1, WP-2 | WP-7 | `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_git.ts`, `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts`, `cli/test/v11_runner_concurrency.test.ts` (new), `cli/test/operation_git.test.ts` |\n| WP-4 | Inter-agent channel: model, delivery, CLI, summary publication | Agent D | WP-1 (types), WP-3 (delivery hook) | WP-5, WP-7 | `cli/src/core/operation_messages.ts` (new), `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` (delivery only), `cli/src/operation_cli.ts` (message command only), `cli/test/v11_messages.test.ts` (new) |\n| WP-5 | Operation replay | Agent E | WP-1 (view schema) | WP-2, WP-4, WP-7 | `cli/src/operation_view.ts` (replay section only), `cli/src/operation_cli.ts` (`--replay` only), `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts` (replay cases) |\n| WP-6 | Requirements ledger and traceability enforcement | Agent F | WP-1..WP-5 acceptance IDs | none | `docs/v1.1.0/REQUIREMENTS.md` (new), `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` (v1.1 ledger support only) |\n| WP-7 | Documentation, release notes, changelog, release-process fixes | Agent G | WP-1..WP-5 | WP-2..WP-5 | `docs/v1.1.0/*.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/releases/v1.1.0*.md`, `docs/releases/PROTECTIONS.md`, `README.md` |\n| WP-8 | PR publication (deferred) | unassigned | — | — | `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC.md` §5.5 only until v1.2 |\n| WP-9 | TUI pane / semantic retrieval (deferred) | unassigned | — | — | — |\n\n### 2.1 Why this order\n\n1. **WP-1 first.** Everything else reads `DurableOperationState`. If the schema gate and migration land after the\n   scheduler, the scheduler's tests would encode a shape that later changes, and the migration test would have to be\n   rewritten. WP-1 also repairs two defects (D-V11-01, D-V11-02) that are independent of concurrency and would\n   otherwise be buried in a large diff.\n2. **WP-2 before WP-3.** The scheduler is pure and cheap to test exhaustively; the runner is I/O and expensive. A\n   due-set bug found in WP-2 costs minutes; the same bug inside the runner costs a flaky suite.\n3. **WP-3 before WP-4.** Message delivery happens at the same `save()` as the `RUNNING` transition. That hook lives\n   in the runner, so the runner must be stable first.\n4. **WP-5 is independent** of concurrency and can run in parallel from the moment WP-1's view schema bumps.\n5. **WP-6 and WP-7 last** so they record what actually shipped, not what was planned.\n\n## 3. Frozen contracts\n\nThese are the only shapes agents share. Changing one requires a lead decision recorded in\n[`DECISIONS.md`](DECISIONS.md).\n\n### 3.1 `Decision.run` batch form\n\n```ts\nexport interface Assignment { unit: WorkUnit; resource: ResourceDescriptor; reroutedFrom?: Reroute }\nexport type Decision =\n  | { kind: \"run\"; assignments: Assignment[] }     // length >= 1, deterministic order, no shared single-slot resource\n  | { kind: \"wait\"; wakeAt: number; reason: string; parked: string[] }\n  | { kind: \"complete\" }\n  | { kind: \"blocked\"; decisions: EscalationDecision[] };\n```\n\nOwner: WP-2. Consumer: WP-3. WP-3 MUST accept a batch of length 1 and MUST NOT special-case `length === 1`.\n\n### 3.2 Operation schema version\n\n```ts\nexport const CURRENT_OPERATION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2;\nexport function migrateOperationState(raw: unknown): DurableOperationState;  // throws UnsupportedOperationSchemaError\nexport function effectiveConcurrency(state: DurableOperationState): number;  // policy.maxConcurrentUnits ?? 1\n```\n\nOwner: WP-1. Consumers: WP-2 (`effectiveConcurrency`), WP-3, WP-4, WP-5, the view.\n\n### 3.3 Message model\n\n```ts\nexport type OperationMessageKind = \"request\" | \"observation\" | \"artifact\" | \"verdict\";\nexport interface OperationMessage { id; at; from; to; kind; body; refs?; deliveredAt?; deliveredTo? }\nexport function publishMessage(state, msg: Omit<OperationMessage,\"id\"|\"at\">, now: number): OperationMessage;\nexport function undeliveredFor(state, unitId: string): OperationMessage[];   // <= 20, oldest first\nexport function markDelivered(state, ids: string[], unitId: string, at: string): void;\n```\n\nOwner: WP-4. Consumer: WP-3 (calls `undeliveredFor`/`markDelivered` in the save that starts a unit).\n\n### 3.4 Receipt extension\n\n```ts\ncandidate?: { digest: string; scope: \"tree\" | \"commit\" };\ntests?: { command: string; status: string; hasExecutedTests: boolean };\nsequence: number;\n```\n\nOwner: WP-3. Consumer: WP-4 (`refs` to a receipt), WP-5 (nothing — replay reads events only).\n\n### 3.5 View document\n\n`schemaVersion` becomes `2`; adds `replay?: { schemaVersion: 1; entries: ReplayEntry[] }`; `additionalProperties:\nfalse` everywhere. Owner: WP-1 (bump) and WP-5 (contents). Any other agent adding a view field must coordinate with\nboth.\n\n## 4. File and hot-file discipline\n\nPer CONCURRENCY §2, claims are directories under `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/`.\n\n| File | WPs | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/core/operation.ts` | WP-1, WP-2, WP-4 | Serialised. WP-1 first (schema/version), then WP-2 (Decision/Assignment), then WP-4 (message fields). Each change is a separate commit. |\n| `cli/src/core/scheduler.ts` | WP-2 only | Exclusive claim. |\n| `cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts` | WP-3 only | Exclusive claim. |\n| `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` | WP-3, WP-4 | WP-3 lands first; WP-4 adds only the message-delivery block and the prompt heading, in a separate commit. |\n| `cli/src/operation_cli.ts` | WP-1, WP-4, WP-5 | One agent at a time; each adds a distinct command/flag block. |\n| `cli/src/operation_view.ts` | WP-1, WP-5 | WP-1 (sanitisation + schema bump), then WP-5 (replay). |\n| `docs/v1.1.0/operation-view.schema.json` | WP-1, WP-5 | WP-1 bumps the version; WP-5 adds `replay`. |\n| `cli/test/operation_view.test.ts` | WP-1, WP-5 | Serialised; append-only per WP. |\n| `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/releases/*` | WP-7 only | Exclusive. |\n\nEvery agent runs `git rev-parse HEAD` and `git log <mine>..HEAD` before each commit and stops on a foreign commit\n(CONCURRENCY §5.1).\n\n## 5. Integration order and checkpoints\n\n| Checkpoint | Entry | Exit criteria | Review |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| CP-0 | Baseline recorded | `origin/main` sha, v1.0 gate status, claims reconciled (this document + ROADMAP-REVIEW §1) | Lead |\n| CP-1 | WP-1 merged into `v1/v11-lead-program` | Schema/migration/spec/safety tests green; no other test changed behaviour | Lead + independent reviewer |\n| CP-2 | WP-2 merged | Scheduler property tests green (1,000 shuffles); concurrency 1 byte-identical outcomes | Lead + independent reviewer |\n| CP-3 | WP-3 merged | Batch execution, queue, cancellation, crash-resume tests green; full CLI suite green | Lead + independent reviewer |\n| CP-4 | WP-4 merged | Channel tests green; dependent-unit prompt exactness | Lead |\n| CP-5 | WP-5 merged | Replay tests green; view schema v2 validates | Lead |\n| CP-6 | WP-6 + WP-7 merged | `check_requirements --enforce` green with v1.1 rows; docs accurate | Lead + independent reviewer |\n| CP-7 | RC qualification | `VALIDATION.md` gates G1–G4 executed on the exact commit | Independent acceptance |\n\nA checkpoint is not \"tests passed\". It is \"the WP's acceptance IDs are demonstrated with named evidence, the diff\nwas reviewed by someone other than its author, and no other WP's acceptance regressed\".\n\n## 6. Assignment briefs\n\nEach brief below is complete enough to hand to a fresh agent with no conversation history. The lead fills in\n`<commit>` and `<WP>` when delegating.\n\n### 6.1 WP-1 — Schema v2, migration, spec validation, terminal safety\n\n**Objective.** Make `DurableOperationState` versioned and fail closed, reject unknown spec keys, and complete\nterminal safety in the operation view.\n\n**In scope.** `CURRENT_OPERATION_SCHEMA_VERSION = 2`; `migrateOperationState`; `UnsupportedOperationSchemaError`;\nload-time invariants; `.pre-migration-v1` backup of the whole record before the first v2 write; strict spec\nvalidation for top level, `policy`, `git`, and each unit; `safeTerminal` on `view.status`/`unit.status`; the view\nschema validator keyword completion.\n\n**Explicitly out of scope.** Any scheduler or runner change; the `Decision` type; message fields; replay; the\n`git.publish` implementation (it must be rejected, not built).\n\n**Spec.** §4.1–§4.5, §7.6, §12.2. **Acceptance.** ACC-V11-SCHEMA-01..04, ACC-V11-SPEC-01/02, ACC-V11-SAFE-01/02.\n\n**Owned files.** As in §2 WP-1. **Do not touch** `scheduler.ts`, `operation_runner*.ts`, `docs/v1.0.0/**`.\n\n**Deliverables.**\n1. `cli/src/core/operation_schema.ts` with the constant, the migration, the invariant checker and the error class.\n2. `cli/test/operation_schema.test.ts` with a checked-in v1.0.0 fixture (`cli/test/fixtures/operation-v1.json`) that\n   is a real record captured from a v1.0.0 run, not hand-written to fit the migration.\n3. Spec-validation tests using a temporary JSON file and the real CLI entry point.\n4. A hostile-record test injecting `\\x1b]52;…\\x07` into `unit.status` and asserting no ESC in `--dag` output.\n5. `operation-view.schema.json` version 2 with a validator that fails on an unimplemented keyword.\n\n**Checks.**\n```\nnode scripts/run_tests.mjs test/operation_schema.test.ts test/operation_view.test.ts\nnode scripts/run_tests.mjs test/operation_git.test.ts test/convergence_scheduling.test.ts   # non-regression\nnpx tsc --noEmit -p cli\n```\n\n**Handoff format.** A commit on a `v1/wp1-*` branch, a report listing changed files, the commands run and their\nexit codes, acceptance IDs demonstrated with the test name that proves each, and any acceptance ID not demonstrated\nwith the reason. Open risks go in the report, not in a comment.\n\n**Blockers.** If the v1.0.0 fixture cannot be produced without running an inference provider, stop and ask the lead;\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","create_time":1793621369.6024709}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
