2.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.1.2.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,12 @@\n # Nexus Code v1.1.2\n \n-**Nexus Code v1.1.2** is a patch release on the v1.1.1 line with one operation message-delivery fix.\n+**Nexus Code v1.1.2** targets the full WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap that was originally planned for v1.1.0. The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files; v1.1.1 is the published predecessor. Version numbers are immutable, so the roadmap work is assigned to v1.1.2.\n+\n+## Release scope and status\n+\n+The intended scope is the complete [WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md), together with any already-approved corrective changes needed for the candidate. The operation message-delivery correction described below remains relevant context for the v1.1.1 predecessor.\n+\n+This document records the target scope; it does not claim that the roadmap is implemented or qualified. Work-package completion, exact-head test and type gates, independent review, release-candidate qualification, and publication are still required before v1.1.2 can be called released. Track implementation and evidence in the work-package plans and release qualification record.\n \n ## Fixed\n \n@@ -27,4 +33,4 @@ Operation records are unchanged: operation schema version 2, as in v1.1.1. No mi\n \n ## Qualification\n \n-This release inherits the v1.1.1 qualification record and is the version-only promotion of `v1.1.2-rc.1`. The source change is limited to `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` (`unsubmittedMessages` and a new `promptCarriesMessage` helper) and its test. Its qualification is the release workflow's gates (version, notes, provenance), plus independent review of the fix (PR #377) and of the candidate.\n+The multi-message resume correction is present in the candidate branch (`c0afc44c`). It is one corrective change within the larger roadmap scope, not the definition of this release. Qualification must cover the complete WP-1101–WP-1108 scope on the exact final candidate, including its full 