{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:14:56.645Z","ordinal":41789,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c21-eae7-7351-8f59-ab15f352b0bf","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-18493508-5d3f-4101-9c53-941e831660c3","process_id":"37894","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '642,656p'; nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md | sed -n '1,55p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md","name":"MEMORY.md","path":"/home/mike/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba /home/mike/.codex/memories/skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md","name":"SKILL.md","path":"/home/mike/.codex/memories/skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"   642\t\n   643\t## Reusable knowledge\n   644\t\n   645\t- PR #10 exact head `bdc705e593def11ee5e44a6ebd0703b57e5953a0` passed CI `39085388798` and merged to `v1/integration` as `2c70d39ad4f9c29cff04c909eef9de6d2a29bdb2`; this was source/CI acceptance, not release qualification. Its claimed readiness artifacts and held-out payload remained out of bounds. [Task 1]\n   646\t- Recovery concurrency procedure: first read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`, work state, claims, PRs, and worktrees; use one claimed slice/worktree, isolated HOME/XDG, snapshot-based full suites, `GATEWAY` claims for inference, no `pkill -f`/`killall`, and owner-only push/tag/publish. [Task 2][Task 3]\n   647\t- Boot evidence proves reboot only, not application power-loss recovery. Verify durable post-reboot state directly; a WSL path in a claim and a newly recreated tmpfs do not prove retained state. [Task 2]\n   648\t- RC14 artifact verification established signed tag object `03770c12a30af830f392eb916122b864c12cf322`, source commit `16eeb6eeffe7fc0bae234aa34dcb671a6ba5ff99`, and Linux archive SHA-256 `52d1c855158c63dbc7cac2e9d87e2f64b1feffb193de97660e92276a2bd46eb7`. Evidence packet `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.14/` has a `SHA256SUMS` index; preserve the GitHub API release-body terminal LF. [Task 3]\n   649\t- ACC-SUP-08 workflow `41038503854` passed on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04; the outputs matched one another and six public RC14 assets byte-for-byte. Serialize full suites: PR #345 duplicate run `41039328573` was canceled while PR #344’s suite was active. [Task 3]\n   650\t- `DEC-20` waives only the manual terminal matrix. Fresh exact-artifact automated CI and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios are still required; older `/tmp/nexus-rc14-pty-20261030` notes are not current qualification. [Task 3]\n   651\t- The Sidecar cancellation regression must verify child liveness before cancel, `INTERRUPTED` and `outstandingToolSettled`, no post-cancel mutation, and shell/child exit. Build the exact archived RC core when comparing release behavior; current helpers can yield `Engine version mismatch`. [Task 4]\n   652\t- Related skill: skills/nexus-release-qualification/SKILL.md. [Task 2][Task 3][Task 4]\n   653\t\n   654\t## Failures and how to do differently\n   655\t\n   656\t- Do not take PR #56, PR #60, PR #61, evaluator, or qualification-host claims without explicit handoff. Green checks on a stale remote head do not validate an independently reviewed replacement; reconcile the exact reviewed head and rerun exact-head CI. [Task 2]\n     1\t---\n     2\tname: nexus-release-qualification\n     3\tdescription: Coordinate or verify a Nexus RC/release lane when claims, exact-head CI, artifact integrity, reproducibility, or installed-PTY qualification are in scope.\n     4\targument-hint: \"[rc-version or release lane]\"\n     5\tuser-invocable: false\n     6\tallowed-tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash\n     7\t---\n     8\t\n     9\t# Nexus Release Qualification\n    10\t\n    11\t## When to use\n    12\t\n    13\t- The task concerns a Nexus v1 RC/release lane, recovery after an interrupted run, or an exact-artifact qualification claim.\n    14\t- The task needs to distinguish source/CI acceptance, artifact evidence, installed-RC qualification, and publication.\n    15\t- Do not use this to bypass another owner's claim, access held-out material, or publish/tag/push without explicit ownership.\n    16\t\n    17\t## Inputs / context to gather\n    18\t\n    19\t1. Read `/home/mike/nexus-code/AGENTS.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`, `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md`, current work state, `.git/nexus-claims`, worktrees, and relevant PR/CI exact heads.\n    20\t2. Snapshot the shared checkout's branch, HEAD, porcelain state, and ownership before any mutation. Treat a dirty shared checkout as read-only.\n    21\t3. For `$ARGUMENTS`, identify the exact tag, source commit, archive digest, installed artifact path, claims, and gate(s) requested.\n    22\t\n    23\t## Procedure\n    24\t\n    25\t1. Establish ownership. Verify host identity, boot identity if recovery is involved, process start time, command, working directory, and claim age. Obtain explicit handoff before touching another lane.\n    26\t2. Work only in a claimed isolated worktree with isolated `HOME`/XDG state. Claim `SUITE` before a full matrix and `GATEWAY` before synthetic gateway work. Never use `pkill -f` or `killall`.\n    27\t3. Separate status: source test/CI, independent review, artifact integrity, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC scripted PTY, held-out/provider/standalone acceptance, and publication. Report each gate separately.\n    28\t4. For artifact integrity, verify tag object -> source commit -> archive digest; compare release metadata, `SHA256SUMS`, provenance/SBOM/manifests, installer/version/help, and evidence packet checksum index. Preserve byte-faithful API captures.\n    29\t5. For reproducibility, build the exact RC on distinct runners, compare runner outputs to each other and public assets byte-for-byte, then retain checksum evidence. Avoid overlapping full CI matrices.\n    30\t6. For installed PTY qualification, rerun every required scripted scenario against the freshly installed exact artifact using isolated HOME/workspace and process-cleanup evidence. Do not substitute historic notes or source-level tests.\n    31\t7. For cancellation remediation, confirm child liveness before cancel; assert `INTERRUPTED`, settled outstanding tool state, no post-cancel mutation, and shell/child exit. Compare only with an exact archived RC core.\n    32\t\n    33\t## Efficiency plan\n    34\t\n    35\t- Read claims/topology once and cache exact head/tag/digest plus gate status in the work-state update.\n    36\t- Run focused gate-specific checks before any serialized full suite. Cancel only an identified duplicate suite, never a different owner’s run.\n    37\t- Stop a readiness claim immediately when an exact-artifact or ownership invariant is missing; record the unresolved gate rather than broadening scope.\n    38\t\n    39\t## Pitfalls and fixes\n    40\t\n    41\t- Green CI or an accepted source review is not RC/product qualification -> require the exact installed artifact and documented acceptance gates.\n    42\t- Reboot, tmpfs recreation, or an inaccessible WSL path is not durable recovery evidence -> inspect durable state on the actual host/filesystem.\n    43\t- `release-assets.json` is an object -> enumerate `.assets`.\n    44\t- A dirty checkout can make `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` fail on cleanliness -> use a clean committed snapshot for that gate.\n    45\t- Sidecar tests do not prove TUI Escape behavior -> rerun the exact-artifact scripted PTY scenario.\n    46\t\n    47\t## Verification checklist\n    48\t\n    49\t- Shared checkout was preserved; worktree, claims, and isolated HOME/XDG are recorded.\n    50\t- Exact head/tag/artifact digest and CI state are recorded.\n    51\t- Every stated gate has a separate pass/fail/unverified disposition.\n    52\t- Artifact and reproducibility evidence includes retained checksums.\n    53\t- Installed-RC PTY evidence is fresh, exact-artifact, and includes process cleanup.\n    54\t- Held-out, owner-only, and publication boundaries were preserved.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":51406}},"started_at_ms":1793621696645,"completed_at_ms":1793621696645}}
