{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:16:22.472Z","ordinal":41861,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c2f-dea4-71b3-98ee-cb4f44bcaab4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8f4abc94-5038-426c-aefd-7d150fe0c90f","process_id":"87902","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -C 4 'WP-110[1-8]' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/wp-1105-evaluators log -5 --oneline --decorate; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/wp-1105-evaluators diff --stat; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/wp-1105-evaluators ls-files --others --exclude-standard eval/evaluators | wc -l"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-scope-reconciliation","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n -C 4 'WP-110[1-8]' docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/wp-1105-evaluators log -5 --oneline --decorate; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/wp-1105-evaluators diff --stat; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/wp-1105-evaluators ls-files --others --exclude-standard eval/evaluators | wc -l"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"19-- Ratatui TUI & Token Accounting    - Flight Recorder Redaction         - TUI Trace Inspector\n20-- Deterministic Packages & Provenance - Standalone `nexus eval` CLI      - Human Annotation Queue\n21-                                    - Deterministic Code Evaluators     - Failure Clustering\n22-                                    - GBNF Tool Grammar Engine          - Composio Dev Bridge (WP-1207)\n23:                                    - Dependabot Modernization (WP-1108)│\n24-                                                                        ▼\n25-                                                                        v1.3.0\n26-                                                                        - Standard OTLP Exporter\n27-                                                                        - Full Context Provenance (CTX-1)\n--\n40-### Work Packages\n41-\n42-| ID | Title | Summary & Deliverables | Backlog / Audit Source |\n43-| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n44:| **WP-1101** | **OpenTelemetry Local Tracing** | Implement `cli/src/core/trace.ts` providing hierarchical tracing conforming to OpenTelemetry GenAI semantics. Captures agent turn roots, model request spans, tool execution spans, and context compactions into local `trace.jsonl` files. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.1 |\n45:| **WP-1102** | **Flight Recorder Credential Redaction** | Implement automated zero-leak credential sanitization across all recorded spans, CLI error dumps, and debug journals, validating against the test fixtures in `docs/CRED003_FLIGHTRECORDER_SANITIZATION_EVIDENCE.md`. | `REQ-DX-105`, `CRED003` |\n46:| **WP-1103** | **Versioned Evaluation Datasets** | Migrate `eval/tasks/` into structured datasets under `eval/datasets/`. Decouple task input specifications (`examples.jsonl`) from evaluation assertions (`oracles.jsonl`). Add versioning and dataset splits (`regression`, `benchmark`). | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §2.3 |\n47:| **WP-1104** | **Standalone `nexus eval` Command** | Implement `nexus eval` subcommand in launcher grammar, supporting `--dataset <path>`, `--runs <count>`, `--isolated-home`, and structured JSON score outputs. | `REQ-EVL-101`, `ROADMAP.md` |\n48:| **WP-1105** | **Deterministic Code Evaluators** | Implement modular evaluator library in `eval/evaluators/code/`: AST syntax validation, build pass/fail, typecheck exit codes, diff boundary compliance, and JSON repair rates. | `LANGSMITH_REVIEW` §4.1 |\n49:| **WP-1106** | **Single Step Loop Mode** | Implement `--step` flag in `nexus run` and `/step` REPL command to execute one agent turn and pause deterministically for operator confirmation. | `REQ-AGT-111` |\n50:| **WP-1107** | **Constrained Decoding & GBNF Tool Grammar Engine** | Implement dynamic Context-Free Grammar (GBNF) generation from registered tool schemas (`read_file`, `write_file`, `edit_file`, `run_command`). Interfaces with `llama.cpp` (`grammar`), `vLLM` (`guided_json`), and `Ollama` (`format`). Supports hybrid grammars (`<think>...</think>` + tool call) for reasoning models (DeepSeek R1). Targets near-zero JSON argument parse errors and enables reliable agentic execution on 7B/14B Q4_K_M local models. | `POSITIONING.md` §3.6, `SPEC-EVALUATION.md` §6 |\n51:| **WP-1108** | **Zero Technical Debt & Dependency Modernization** | Triage, validate, and integrate the 27 post-v1.0.0 Dependabot PRs (#103–#129) under an absolute zero-deprecation policy for third-party libraries. Categorized across 5 staged batches: Core Rust runtime (#105, #107, #110, #113), GitHub Actions CI workflows (#103, #104, #106, #108, #112), Cloudflare micro-workers (#109, #115–#118, #121–#123, #125–#128), TypeScript compiler (#119, #124, #129), and CLI runtime migrations (#111, #114, #120 including Commander 12→15 compatibility audit). Enforces continuous zero-technical-debt invariants. | PRs #103–#129, `ROADMAP.md` §2.1 |\n52-\n53-### v1.1.0 Release Gates\n54-\n55-- **Gate G1.1-1 (Zero-Leak Tracing):** Local trace engine produces valid OTel GenAI spans for all turn steps without leaking environment credentials or writing outside `~/.local/share/nexus/traces/`.\n--\n57-- **Gate G1.1-3 (CLI Parity):** `nexus eval` executes cleanly from packaged binary installations without developer dependencies.\n58-- **Gate G1.1-4 (Constrained Decoding Reliability):** GBNF-constrained execution achieves >=99.5% valid JSON tool call syntax (minimizing syntax repair retries) across supported local inference endpoints (llama.cpp, vLLM, Ollama).\n59-- **Gate G1.1-5 (Zero Technical Debt & Zero Deprecated Packages):** Strictly 0 deprecated packages, 0 unmaintained dependencies, 0 CodeQL alerts, and 0 compiler warnings repository-wide. All 27 Dependabot PR upgrades pass unit/PTY suites, `cargo deny check`, automated npm registry deprecation scans, package reproducibility (`cmp`), and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants.\n60-\n61:### 2.1 Dependabot Triage & Integration Matrix (WP-1108)\n62-\n63-Following the PR #8 integration merge to `main`, Dependabot opened 27 automated dependency update pull requests (PRs #103–#129). These are triaged into 5 distinct integration batches scheduled for the v1.1.0 development cycle (deferred from v1.0.0):\n64-\n65-#### Batch 1: Core Rust Engine Runtime (Low Risk / Initial v1.1.0 Release Cycle)\n--\n134-| **WP-1302** | **Full Context Provenance Graph** | Implement complete graph metadata for all context admissions (tracking origin file, trust classification, transformation history, and compaction survival). | `CTX-001`, `REQ-AGT-010` |\n135-| **WP-1303** | **macOS & arm64 Build Pipelines** | Add native GitHub Actions packaging runners and platform sandboxing (macOS `sandbox-exec` / Linux `arm64`). | `DEC-12`, `REQUIREMENTS.md` §5 |\n136-| **WP-1304** | **Knowledge Freshness & Lifecycle** | Implement automated staleness detection, contradiction resolution, and operator prompts for expiring project knowledge. | `CTX-002`, `REQUIREMENTS.md` §5 |\n137-| **WP-1305** | **cgroup v2 Fine-Grained Limits** | Add direct per-command CPU throttling and memory caps via systemd/cgroup-v2 scopes. | `REQUIREMENTS.md` §5 |\n138:| **WP-1306** | **Composio Enterprise Multi-App MCP Mesh** | Enable dynamic discovery and tool execution across 250+ enterprise SaaS applications (Salesforce, Google Workspace, AWS, Notion, Datadog, Sentry, Asana) using Composio's Model Context Protocol (MCP) toolsets. Compiles enterprise action schemas into logit-constrained GBNF grammars via `WP-1107` to enforce JSON schema syntactic compliance on local models. Enforces egress domain filtering, tmpfs execution isolation, and sovereign zero-telemetry defaults. | Composio Startup Program, `SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md` §7 |\n139-\n140----\n141-\n142-## 5. Architectural Invariants Across All Post-v1 Releases\n7b49e6ff (HEAD -> v1/wp-1105-evaluators) Merge pull request #129 from mikeholownych/dependabot/npm_and_yarn/cli/typescript-7.0.2\nd4f72adc Merge pull request #371 from mikeholownych/v1/merge-pr-131-v2\nc7d0b003 Merge pull request #103 from mikeholownych/dependabot/github_actions/actions/REDACTED\nbfa7f352 Merge pull request #108 from mikeholownych/dependabot/github_actions/softprops/action-gh-release-3.0.3\n684487dd Merge pull request #218 from mikeholownych/dependabot/github_actions/actions/upload-artifact-7.0.2\n10\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":686805645}},"started_at_ms":1793621781785,"completed_at_ms":1793621782472}}
