{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:23:53.806Z","ordinal":42230,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0caaafcd-2149-499e-95df-60aafa2b78ab","process_id":"76311","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","node -e 'const fs=require(\"node:fs\");const s=fs.readFileSync(\"docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md\",\"utf8\");if(!/Superseded draft/.test(s)||!/not tagged, published, or qualified/.test(s))throw new Error(\"v112_rc_superseded_status\");if(!/WP-1101[\\s\\S]*WP-1108/.test(s)||!/v1\\.1\\.0 release failed and published no release files/.test(s)||!/v1\\.1\\.1 is the published predecessor/.test(s))throw new Error(\"v112_rc_full_scope\");if(/inherits the v1\\.1\\.1 qualification|Release qualification for this RC is/.test(s)||!/Qualification status: none/.test(s)||!/qualification remains open/i.test(s))throw new Error(\"v112_rc_no_inherited_qualification\");' && git diff --check && git diff --stat && git diff -- docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-rc-scope","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"node -e 'const fs=require(\"node:fs\");const s=fs.readFileSync(\"docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md\",\"utf8\");if(!/Superseded draft/.test(s)||!/not tagged, published, or qualified/.test(s))throw new Error(\"v112_rc_superseded_status\");if(!/WP-1101[\\s\\S]*WP-1108/.test(s)||!/v1\\.1\\.0 release failed and published no release files/.test(s)||!/v1\\.1\\.1 is the published predecessor/.test(s))throw new Error(\"v112_rc_full_scope\");if(/inherits the v1\\.1\\.1 qualification|Release qualification for this RC is/.test(s)||!/Qualification status: none/.test(s)||!/qualification remains open/i.test(s))throw new Error(\"v112_rc_no_inherited_qualification\");' && git diff --check && git diff --stat && git diff -- docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":" docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md | 14 +++++++++-----\n 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md\nindex 272033d0..0bf778d0 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md\n@@ -1,21 +1,25 @@\n # Nexus Code v1.1.2-rc.1\n \n-**Release Candidate 1 for Nexus Code v1.1.2**: a patch release on the v1.1.1 line with one operation message-delivery fix.\n+**Superseded draft — not tagged, published, or qualified.** This file described an earlier patch-only PR #377 candidate. The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files; v1.1.1 is the published predecessor. The approved v1.1.2 target is now the full [WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md). This draft's patch-only scope and qualification statements do not qualify or define v1.1.2.\n \n-## Fixed\n+## Historical patch-only draft contents\n+\n+The sections below preserve the earlier PR #377 draft for reference. They are not the complete v1.1.2 release notes or qualification record.\n+\n+### Proposed correction\n \n ### A crash-resumed unit no longer receives a multi-message prompt's later messages twice\n \n When a work unit's prompt carried two or more operator or inter-unit messages, and Nexus stopped after submitting that prompt but before the unit's result was saved, resume recognised only the **first** message as already submitted. Every later message from that prompt was injected into the unit's conversation again.\n \n-Resume now recognises each message in a submitted prompt's messages block, whatever its position. Matching is still limited to prompts that Nexus issued (`isSubmittedUnitPrompt`, from v1.1.1), so marker text in model output, tool output, or files cannot suppress a message.\n+The proposed change made resume recognise each message in a submitted prompt's messages block, whatever its position. Matching remained limited to prompts that Nexus issued (`isSubmittedUnitPrompt`, from v1.1.1), so marker text in model output, tool output, or files could not suppress a message.\n \n - Impact in v1.1.1: the duplicated message was advisory context only. No message was lost, and no `TurnResult`, verification, or acceptance outcome was affected.\n - Regression coverage: the post-prompt crash test in `cli/test/operation_release_review.test.ts` now carries two messages. It asserts that each message appears once in the durable history and is acknowledged once.\n \n ## Correction to the v1.1.1 notes\n \n-The v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \"at most once\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash, as described above. v1.1.2 makes the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\n+The v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \"at most once\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash, as described above. The proposed fix was intended to make the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\n \n ## Runtime requirements\n \n@@ -27,4 +31,4 @@ Operation records are unchanged: operation schema version 2, as in v1.1.1. No mi\n \n ## Qualification\n \n-This candidate inherits the v1.1.1 qualification record. The source change is limited to `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` (`unsubmittedMessages` and a new `promptCarriesMessage` helper) and its test. Release qualification for this RC is the release workflow's gates (version, notes, provenance), plus independent review of the fix (PR #377) and of this candidate.\n+**Qualification status: none.** This draft does not inherit v1.1.1 qualification and is not an accepted v1.1.2 release candidate. Qualification remains open and must cover the full WP-1101–WP-1108 scope on the exact final candidate, including the required release gates, independent review, and release acceptance. The PR #377 change described above is historical candidate context only.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":732966782}},"started_at_ms":1793622233072,"completed_at_ms":1793622233805}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:23:55.049Z","ordinal":42231,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19c37-57a9-7d82-9119-273b7162d179","call_id":"call_19f5ca27359a4ea0ad021befa71e0349","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":" docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md | 14 +++++++++-----\n 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md\nindex 272033d0..0bf778d0 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md\n@@ -1,21 +1,25 @@\n # Nexus Code v1.1.2-rc.1\n \n-**Release Candidate 1 for Nexus Code v1.1.2**: a patch release on the v1.1.1 line with one operation message-delivery fix.\n+**Superseded draft — not tagged, published, or qualified.** This file described an earlier patch-only PR #377 candidate. The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files; v1.1.1 is the published predecessor. The approved v1.1.2 target is now the full [WP-1101–WP-1108 roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md). This draft's patch-only scope and qualification statements do not qualify or define v1.1.2.\n \n-## Fixed\n+## Historical patch-only draft contents\n+\n+The sections below preserve the earlier PR #377 draft for reference. They are not the complete v1.1.2 release notes or qualification record.\n+\n+### Proposed correction\n \n ### A crash-resumed unit no longer receives a multi-message prompt's later messages twice\n \n When a work unit's prompt carried two or more operator or inter-unit messages, and Nexus stopped after submitting that prompt but before the unit's result was saved, resume recognised only the **first** message as already submitted. Every later message from that prompt was injected into the unit's conversation again.\n \n-Resume now recognises each message in a submitted prompt's messages block, whatever its position. Matching is still limited to prompts that Nexus issued (`isSubmittedUnitPrompt`, from v1.1.1), so marker text in model output, tool output, or files cannot suppress a message.\n+The proposed change made resume recognise each message in a submitted prompt's messages block, whatever its position. Matching remained limited to prompts that Nexus issued (`isSubmittedUnitPrompt`, from v1.1.1), so marker text in model output, tool output, or files could not suppress a message.\n \n - Impact in v1.1.1: the duplicated message was advisory context only. No message was lost, and no `TurnResult`, verification, or acceptance outcome was affected.\n - Regression coverage: the post-prompt crash test in `cli/test/operation_release_review.test.ts` now carries two messages. It asserts that each message appears once in the durable history and is acknowledged once.\n \n ## Correction to the v1.1.1 notes\n \n-The v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \"at most once\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash, as described above. v1.1.2 makes the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\n+The v1.1.1 notes say that a recipient receives undelivered messages \"at most once\". That holds for prompts carrying a single message. For prompts carrying several messages, v1.1.1 could re-inject the second and later messages after a post-submission crash, as described above. The proposed fix was intended to make the statement hold in both cases. `docs/releases/v1.1.1.md` carries a matching addendum.\n \n ## Runtime requirements\n \n@@ -27,4 +31,4 @@ Operation records are unchanged: operation schema version 2, as in v1.1.1. No mi\n \n ## Qualification\n \n-This candidate inherits the v1.1.1 qualification record. The source change is limited to `cli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts` (`unsubmittedMessages` and a new `promptCarriesMessage` helper) and its test. Release qualification for this RC is the release workflow's gates (version, notes, provenance), plus independent review of the fix (PR #377) and of this candidate.\n+**Qualification status: none.** This draft does not inherit v1.1.1 qualification and is not an accepted v1.1.2 release candidate. Qualification remains open and must cover the full WP-1101–WP-1108 scope on the exact final candidate, including the required release gates, independent review, and release acceptance. The PR #377 change described above is historical candidate context only.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","create_time":1793622235.049593}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
