{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:25:45.475Z","ordinal":42340,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a19c39-0702-7030-bd1c-a2f9be528909","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**APPROVED.** The two tables can cover all eight work packages and five release gates; the as-of date, exact candidate/evidence locators, and explicit open status make partial implementation distinguishable from qualification. The one-file change is atomic, and both claims cover the workstream and file on the same worktree.\n\nWhen filling the matrix, use the latest gate updates and current evidence. For example, WP-1104’s plan contains earlier audit notes that are explicitly superseded by later gate updates; don’t treat those interim notes as the current disposition. Clearly mark missing authoritative evidence as open or unverified."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c35-8dbf-7b72-9a43-c0e91b05ed32","create_time":1793622345.4749453,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":1717}}
