{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T12:57:04.930Z","ordinal":43297,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19c55-b4a2-74b3-92a6-b341183e18d1","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- v1.1.2-release: state=12:52 UTC verified wait: PR396 full suite process tree 2050464/2050484 still active; test worker 2578019 has been in D state jbd2_log_wait_commit since 12:49:35, and full.log has not advanced since then. Another independent test/nonprogress_recovery.test.ts process tree 2583602/2583884 started 12:50:21/22 in /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr396-review-bbcf7cc1; child 2583884 is also in D state. I/O PSI full avg10 11.13%, avg60 12.04%. Conflict log updated. No processes signaled or tests run here. Claim heartbeats refreshed for WP-1103. Docs commits 4b63cee0, ae225c9d, eb6884df are approved and local; no release., phase=ORIENT, gate=WP-1103 gate pending; shared test host blocked in journal waits, next=Re-poll both live test process trees and log; after all external test processes exit, claim SUITE and execute exact-source WP-1103 gate., friction=Concurrent external test runs are stalled in jbd2 journal commit waits and high I/O pressure., updated=2026-11-02T12:00:00Z, reviewer=/root/review_delta, verdict=APPROVED for 05c49df2 and 2a94f62e, retrieval=nexus-test eval_integrity.test.ts:1729 SSE tool-call stream; eval_harness.test.ts:43 deterministic reply pattern; provider_connect.test.ts:31 local provider harness, updated 5 minutes ago\n- ...783 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-02 12:57pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 25 obs (7,342t read) | 32,238t work | 77% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\n27498 12:13p ✓ docs/releases/v1.1.2.md Status Sentence Added — Roadmap and Qualification Explicitly Marked Incomplete\n27499 \" ✓ docs/releases/v1.1.2.md Postcheck Passed — All Three Assertions Green\n27500 \" ○ docs/releases/v1.1.2.md Commit Failed — File Not Staged\n27501 \" ✓ docs/releases/v1.1.2.md Scope Reconciliation Committed — Commit 4b63cee0\n27502 \" ✓ V112_SCOPE_RECONCILIATION Claims Released — Scope Docs Work Logged to nexus-claims.log\n27504 12:15p ○ WP-1103 Claims Still Held — WP-1103_RUNNER_API and eval_dataset.test.ts Claims Active\n27506 \" ○ WP-1103 Integration Worktree Has Untracked Acceptance Evidence File\n27507 12:16p ○ WP-1105 Claimed by Codex-GPT-6 Agent Since Oct 31 — Evaluators Worktree Has Untracked eval/evaluators/\n27509 \" ○ WP-1105 Evaluators Work-in-Progress — eval/evaluators/code/ Has 11 Untracked Files, Agent PID Dead\n27510 \" ✓ wp1105_handoff_audit Subagent Spawned to Investigate Orphaned WP-1105 Claim\n27511 \" ○ Full WP-1101–WP-1108 Roadmap Scope Confirmed from ROADMAP.md\n27513 12:18p ○ PR396-Takeover Suite Parent Process (PID 2050436) Exited — Only Grandchild PID 2050464 Remains\n27519 \" ○ WP-1105 Handoff Audit: Not Eligible to Pick Up — WP-1103 Dependency Unqualified, Claim Preserved\n27531 \" ○ GitHub Release Tags State — v1.1.1 Published, v1.1.0 Tag Only, v1.1.2 Absent\n27532 \" ○ PR396-Takeover Suite Process (PID 2050464) Still Running at 12:18 UTC — 42+ Minutes Elapsed\n27543 12:19p ○ PR396-Takeover Suite Still Running at 43+ Minutes — Provider Recovery Retries and Checkpoint Save Failing\n27548 12:20p ○ WP-1108 Worktree Clean — 8 Commits Ahead of Main, No Active Agent Process\n27549 \" ◆ wp1108_acceptance_audit Subagent Spawned to Evaluate WP-1108 Gate Status\n27550 \" ○ WP-1108 Branch Never Pushed to GitHub — No PRs or CI Runs Exist\n27552 \" ○ WP-1108 Claims History — GPT-6 Handed Off Alert Remediation Files to claude-code DarkFox on Nov 1\n27553 12:21p ○ WP-1108 Alert Remediation PR #v1/alerts-51-23-24 Already Opened — Merged as PR #394 on Nov 1\n27554 \" ✓ Work State Updated — ORIENT Phase Blockers and Next Action Documented for v1.1.2-release\n27556 12:22p ○ WP-1103 Integration Worktree Has Untracked AC2 Suite Acceptance Evidence File\n27557 \" ◆ v112_gate_matrix Subagent Spawned to Produce Full v1.1.2 Release Gate Status Matrix\n27559 \" ○ v1.1.2-rc.1 Release Notes Confirm Narrow Patch Scope — Operation Message Deduplication Fix Only\n\nAccess 32k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19c45-79f8-74d0-bea2-bdff6a04336d","create_time":1793624224.9306588,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
