{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:10:48.703Z","ordinal":44847,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-45fc144d-96ef-4761-bf9d-7b43550db7bc","process_id":"21358","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md | rg -n '^## |^### Item|^### Workstream|^\\*\\*Item|Implementation Status|not yet connected|Release gate|^## 3|^## 4|^## 5|AC[1-9]|Required'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '150,260p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.1.2/PLAN.md | rg -n '^## |^### |Milestone|not yet|requires|Verification'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md | rg -n '^## |^### Item|^### Workstream|^\\*\\*Item|Implementation Status|not yet connected|Release gate|^## 3|^## 4|^## 5|AC[1-9]|Required'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md | sed -n '150,260p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.1.2/PLAN.md | rg -n '^## |^### |Milestone|not yet|requires|Verification'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"11:## 1. Roadmap Overview & Commitments\n33:- **Item 5 and the CERI and comparative harness entry points are not yet connected.** The throttle needs request latency from `cli/src/client.ts`. CERI needs a `nexus eval` command in `cli/src/index.ts`. Both files are claimed by other open work.\n37:## 2. Workstream Roadmap Specifications\n39:### Item 1: Bounded Specialist Agent Profiles (Workstream A)\n57:### Item 2: Objective Independent Review Boundary (Workstream B)\n86:### Item 3: Deterministic Micro-Routing Engine (Workstream C) — cut from PR #396\n104:### Item 4: Multi-Stage Escalation State Machine (Workstream E) — cut from PR #396; superseded by PR #398 non-progress recovery\n121:### Item 5: Telemetry-Informed Concurrency Throttle (Workstream F)\n137:### Item 6: Comparative Evaluation Benchmark Harness (Workstream G)\n149:- **Implementation Status:** Complete in `cli/src/eval/comparative_harness.ts` (Commit `ad8ea909`).\n153:### Item 7: Continuous Evaluation and Regression Intelligence (CERI)\n178:- **Implementation Status:** Foundational primitives and libraries implemented in PR #396 as standalone modules, covered by unit tests only and not yet used by the agent runtime (contracts, tamper-evident evidence store, baseline comparator, epistemological investigation, non-self-approving remediation, operational reporting, and comparative evaluation framework). Interactive agent loop integration and live dual-worker GPU scheduling are scheduled for subsequent integration PRs.\n182:## 3. Deferred Scope (Targeted for v1.2)\n\n---\n\n### Item 7: Continuous Evaluation and Regression Intelligence (CERI)\n- **Objective:** Establish a continuous, evidence-based mechanism for detecting, investigating, classifying, and reporting degradation in Nexus's end-to-end engineering capabilities, enforcing that internal evaluations may veto releases but never certify correctness without independent validation.\n- **Existing Capability / Gap:** `eval/run.mjs` and `cli/src/evaluator.ts` execute tasks and capture candidate receipts, but lack versioned evaluation definitions, run manifests with full model/hardware provenance, designated baseline comparison, 12-state comparative classification, regression intelligence with epistemological distinction, and non-self-approving remediation pathways.\n- **Planned Implementation:**\n  - Workstream A: Versioned evaluation definitions and run manifests capturing immutable commit, dirty status, model identity, toolchain, and host environment.\n  - Workstream B: Append-only evidence persistence with atomic writes, secret redaction, and strict separation between tamper-evidence and independent validation receipts.\n  - Workstream C: Baseline comparator with eligibility validation and 12-state classification (`PASS`, `FAIL`, `REGRESSION_CANDIDATE`, `CONFIRMED_REGRESSION`, `IMPROVEMENT_CANDIDATE`, `FLAKY`, `INFRASTRUCTURE_FAILURE`, `EVALUATOR_DEFECT`, `INCONCLUSIVE`, `NOT_EXECUTED`, `CANCELLED`, `INCOMPARABLE`).\n  - Workstream D: Repeatability and flakiness analysis with bounded rerun policies.\n  - Workstream E: Capacity-aware scheduling for local dual-worker Intel Arc Pro environments.\n  - Workstream F: Representative end-to-end engineering evaluation benchmarks.\n  - Workstream G: Regression intelligence structuring findings into observation, inference, hypothesis, confirmed finding, and unresolved uncertainty.\n  - Workstream H: Reviewable remediation proposals with non-self-approval boundary.\n  - Workstream I: Structured machine-readable operational reporting with measurement limitations and blockers.\n- **Dependencies:** Items 1-6, `CandidateTracker`, `ValidationReceipt`, `isolate.mjs`.\n- **Priority:** High (P1) — Release qualification gate.\n- **Acceptance Criteria:**\n  - Full provenance captured in run manifests without fabricating missing metadata.\n  - Incomparable baselines rejected explicitly rather than silently compared.\n  - Binary pass/fail forcing eliminated in favor of 12-state classification.\n  - Internal evaluations cannot mark candidates as verified without deterministic verifier receipts.\n  - Remediation proposals enforce `approvalStatus: \"PENDING_REVIEW\"`.\n- **Verification Method:** Unit and integration test suites in `cli/test/ceri_*.test.ts`.\n- **Operational Risks:** False regression alarms on non-comparable environments; benchmark overfitting; token consumption during reruns.\n- **Rollback Approach:** Purely additive modules in `cli/src/ceri/`; gated by config flag `ceri.enabled`.\n- **Complexity:** High (5 days).\n- **Implementation Status:** Foundational primitives and libraries implemented in PR #396 as standalone modules, covered by unit tests only and not yet used by the agent runtime (contracts, tamper-evident evidence store, baseline comparator, epistemological investigation, non-self-approving remediation, operational reporting, and comparative evaluation framework). Interactive agent loop integration and live dual-worker GPU scheduling are scheduled for subsequent integration PRs.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Deferred Scope (Targeted for v1.2)\n\nThe following items are explicitly **deferred** to release v1.2:\n1. **Hosted / Multi-Tenant Concurrency:** Nexus trust boundary remains local single-operator.\n2. **Autonomous Tool Generation:** Dynamic creation of new tool definitions by models without human oversight.\n3. **Automatic PR Publication (`git.publish`):** Requires operation-level egress and policy controls.\n4. **Interactive TUI Multi-Agent Pane:** Requires terminal PTY driver redesign.\n10:## 1. Architectural Strategy & Phasing\n26:│ - Verification gating rules                                 │\n50:## 2. Slice 1: Specialist Agent Contracts & Profiles\n52:### 2.1 Modules & Files Changed\n57:### 2.2 Data Contracts & Interfaces\n86:### 2.3 Invariants & Security\n92:## 3. Slice 2: Objective Independent Review Boundary\n94:### 3.1 Modules & Files Changed\n99:### 3.2 Data Contracts & Interfaces\n122:### 3.3 Confirmation Bias Mitigation\n130:## 4. Slice 3: Deterministic Micro-Routing Engine (cut from PR #396)\n134:### 4.1 Modules & Files Changed\n138:### 4.2 Interfaces\n154:## 5. Persistence, State, & Migration Implications\n162:## 6. Verification Milestones\n164:1. **Milestone 1 (Specialist Profiles):** `specialist_profiles.test.ts` passes with 100% test coverage; tool whitelist rejections validated.\n165:2. **Milestone 2 (Review Boundary):** `independent_review.test.ts` passes; implementer narrative redaction verified; structured verdict parsing verified.\n166:3. **Milestone 3 (Micro-Router, cut from PR #396):** `micro_router.test.ts` passes; rule-based queries execute without LLM round-trips.\n167:4. **Milestone 4 (Full Regression):** Complete existing test suite (`npm --prefix cli test`) runs without regressions.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":811312829}},"started_at_ms":1793650247891,"completed_at_ms":1793650248703}}
