{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:11:52.049Z","ordinal":44887,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016ae8ee82dd4481a389b0c489961a7ca9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_d3c522634f18448a9df1222ece3379f8","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\\n@@\\n The v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the published predecessor. GitHub currently has no v1.1.2 release and the remote has no v1.1.2 tag. The v1.1.2 release notes and the former rc.1 draft describe the approved scope and the superseded narrow draft respectively.\\n+\\n+## Current v1.1.2 roadmap alignment\\n+\\n+`origin/main` at `a0d374e8` adds the repository's [Specialist Orchestration and Independent Review roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). This record retains the user-approved WP-1101–WP-1108 scope above and tracks that current roadmap's remaining release commitments as well; neither scope is treated as a substitute for the other.\\n+\\n+| Roadmap item | Current source state | v1.1.2 qualification still required |\\n+|---|---|---|\\n+| Item 1 — Specialist contracts | Runtime roles, contracts, and tool permissions are connected in `origin/main`; PR #396 review fixes are present. | Run the exact-head specialist profile and runtime tests; review the integrated candidate. |\\n+| Item 2 — Independent review boundary | Reviewer evidence packaging and verdict gating are connected in `origin/main`. | Run exact-head boundary, verifier, and operation tests; independently review the integrated behavior. |\\n+| Item 3 — Deterministic micro-routing | Explicitly cut from PR #396 by the current roadmap. | No delivery claim; keep deferred as specified. |\\n+| Item 4 — Multi-stage escalation | Explicitly cut from PR #396 and superseded by merged PR #398 recovery behavior. | Qualify the superseding recovery behavior through the exact-head suite; do not reintroduce the cut state machine. |\\n+| Item 5 — Telemetry-informed throttle | Adaptive throttle code is present, but the roadmap says request-latency wiring and the CERI/CLI integration points remain unconnected. | Connect request latency to throttling, prove overload reduction and recovery, and test the runtime integration. |\\n+| Item 6 — Comparative evaluation harness | Comparative harness source is present in `origin/main`. | Verify its benchmark output and provenance on the integrated exact head. |\\n+| Item 7 — CERI | PR #396 supplies foundational modules, but the roadmap says they are not yet connected to the agent runtime and `nexus eval` entry point. | Complete the required CERI evaluation, provenance, classification, non-self-approval, and operational reporting integrations; meet the roadmap's release-qualification acceptance criteria. |\\n@@\\n - All WP-1101–WP-1108 acceptance evidence and independent reviews are complete.\\n+- Current v1.1.2 roadmap items 1, 2, 5, 6, and 7 are qualified on the exact candidate; cut items 3 and 4 remain deferred as documented.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793650306.8664377}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:11:52.078Z","ordinal":44888,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-46e7e18b-0cdd-47f6-8db7-f57c61db1c22","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -6,2 +6,16 @@\n \n+## Current v1.1.2 roadmap alignment\n+\n+`origin/main` at `a0d374e8` adds the repository's [Specialist Orchestration and Independent Review roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). This record retains the user-approved WP-1101–WP-1108 scope above and tracks that current roadmap's remaining release commitments as well; neither scope is treated as a substitute for the other.\n+\n+| Roadmap item | Current source state | v1.1.2 qualification still required |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| Item 1 — Specialist contracts | Runtime roles, contracts, and tool permissions are connected in `origin/main`; PR #396 review fixes are present. | Run the exact-head specialist profile and runtime tests; review the integrated candidate. |\n+| Item 2 — Independent review boundary | Reviewer evidence packaging and verdict gating are connected in `origin/main`. | Run exact-head boundary, verifier, and operation tests; independently review the integrated behavior. |\n+| Item 3 — Deterministic micro-routing | Explicitly cut from PR #396 by the current roadmap. | No delivery claim; keep deferred as specified. |\n+| Item 4 — Multi-stage escalation | Explicitly cut from PR #396 and superseded by merged PR #398 recovery behavior. | Qualify the superseding recovery behavior through the exact-head suite; do not reintroduce the cut state machine. |\n+| Item 5 — Telemetry-informed throttle | Adaptive throttle code is present, but the roadmap says request-latency wiring and the CERI/CLI integration points remain unconnected. | Connect request latency to throttling, prove overload reduction and recovery, and test the runtime integration. |\n+| Item 6 — Comparative evaluation harness | Comparative harness source is present in `origin/main`. | Verify its benchmark output and provenance on the integrated exact head. |\n+| Item 7 — CERI | PR #396 supplies foundational modules, but the roadmap says they are not yet connected to the agent runtime and `nexus eval` entry point. | Complete the required CERI evaluation, provenance, classification, non-self-approval, and operational reporting integrations; meet the roadmap's release-qualification acceptance criteria. |\n+\n ## Work-package status\n@@ -34,2 +48,3 @@\n - All WP-1101–WP-1108 acceptance evidence and independent reviews are complete.\n+- Current v1.1.2 roadmap items 1, 2, 5, 6, and 7 are qualified on the exact candidate; cut items 3 and 4 remain deferred as documented.\n - The full test suite, type checks, lint/security gates, migration and compatibility checks pass on the exact head.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-integration/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1793650312077,"completed_at_ms":1793650312078}}
