{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:26:50.964Z","ordinal":45307,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19df1-7ad4-7562-8f73-98a3d371837f","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- v1.1.2-release: state=20:26 UTC: full npm test remains active on candidate snapshot a0d374e8; isolated HOME and log unchanged. Process tree 518706/518807/518808/518815 live for 13m; log advanced to 222,935 bytes at 20:26:15 and is in eval qualification/comparative tests. Multiple earlier assertions remain red; final summary pending. SUITE held and heartbeat refreshed. Qualification scope doc now has independent APPROVED review across both the user-approved WP-1101–1108 roadmap and current v1.1.2 roadmap; Item 3 remains OPEN., phase=GREEN, gate=Exact npm test active with failures observed; type/build/process-scope final statuses pending, next=Wait for full npm test and process-scope postcheck to complete; diagnose failures and rerun after fixing prerequisites/defects., friction=Exact-source npm test has not completed; early failing test groups remain unclassified., updated=2026-11-02T20:26:22Z, reviewer=/root/review_delta, verdict=APPROVED release-scope alignment; WP-1103 source diff previously approved; exact gate pending., retrieval=nexus-test eval_integrity.test.ts:1729 SSE tool-call stream; eval_harness.test.ts:43 deterministic reply pattern; provider_connect.test.ts:31 local provider harness, active_agents=Read-only audit delegated to /root/v112_unblocked_work to identify safe progress that does not load the shared test host., updated 1 minute ago\n- ...784 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-02 8:26pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 25 obs (9,274t read) | 36,595t work | 75% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\n27839 8:12p ◆ WP-1103 Exact-Source Qualification Snapshot Worktree Created at origin/main a0d374e8\n27840 \" ✓ SUITE Claim Acquired for WP-1103 Exact-Source Full Test Run\n27841 8:13p ○ WP-1103 Exact-Source Full Suite Started — adaptive_throttle Tests Running at ~11 Minutes\n27842 \" ✓ Qualification Doc Corrected — Item 3 (Micro-Routing) Reclassified as OPEN, Not Deferred\n27843 \" ○ WP-1103 Suite at ~37 Minutes — AgentObserver Failure Traced to ECONNREFUSED on Port 1234\n27844 8:14p ○ WP-1103 Suite at ~78 Minutes — 8 Failures Identified, All Infrastructure/Sandbox Type\n27845 8:15p ○ WP-1103 Suite at ~125 Minutes — write_file Tool Errors and Two Substantive Test Failures\n27846 \" ○ write_file Failures Caused by \"Rust Core RPC Daemon Disconnected\" — Not Sandbox Permission Block\n27847 \" ○ Rust Core Binary Missing from Snapshot Worktree — write_file Failures Confirmed as Build Artifact Absence\n27848 \" ○ Rust Core Binary Name is \"harness-core\" — Multiple Tests Require core/target/release/harness-core\n27849 \" ○ Tests Auto-Skip When harness-core Absent — resolveCoreBinary() Used as Skip Guard\n27850 8:16p ○ Full Test File List Confirmed — Suite Running 80+ Test Files Including TUI E2E and Eval Tests\n27851 \" ✓ v1.1.2 Work State Updated — Scope Alignment Approved, Exact-Candidate Suite Running\n27852 \" ○ WP-1103 Suite at ~4 Hours — Three Named Compaction/Non-Progress Failures, All Rust-Core-Dependent\n27853 8:17p ○ WP-1103 Suite at ~4:43 — Seven Named Failures, Now Including Dual-Model Routing and Compaction Tests\n27854 8:18p ○ New Failure \"D: findings checkpoint before shown output leaves the context\" — 63.9 Second Test Duration\n27855 8:19p ○ New Failure \"E: operator-configured verifier gates every completion\" — 36.2 Seconds\n27856 \" ○ WP-1103 Suite at ~6:47 — Named Failures Now A Through G in Compaction/Verifier Group\n27861 8:20p ○ Suite at ~7:33 — task_completed Tool Also Failing via Rust Core RPC\n27866 8:21p ○ Suite at ~8:27 — HTTP 429 Rate Limit Error and New Behavioral Failures Including \"convergence scheduling\" (43.8s)\n27874 8:22p ○ Suite at ~9:50 — New Named Failures: doctor findings, entry points engine, SPEC-06, ACC-CONT-03 SIGKILL Compaction\n27877 8:24p ○ Suite at ~11:13 — V2 Group Failures: \"unverified changes survive\" (62s) and \"tool still running when host ends\" (15.5s)\n27878 \" ○ V1 Group Failing — \"durable history missing or inconsistent\" (43.6s); Process Death Mid-Turn Sub-test Also Failing\n27879 \" ○ Detailed Failure Analysis — I1 and V1/V2 Failures Partly Rust-Core, Partly Genuine Behavioral Regressions\n27880 8:25p ○ V1 Process Death Group Result — Two Sub-tests Fail, One Passes; Log Growth Stalled\n\nAccess 37k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793651210.9642062,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
