vior. |\n-| Item 3 — Deterministic micro-routing | Explicitly cut from PR #396 by the current roadmap. | No delivery claim; keep deferred as specified. |\n+| Item 3 — Deterministic micro-routing | Explicitly cut from PR #396; no runtime implementation is present in `origin/main`. The roadmap does not explicitly defer this item from the v1.1.2 release. | **OPEN.** Under the user-approved full-roadmap scope, implement and test deterministic query fast paths plus model fallback and provenance for ambiguous requests. |\n | Item 4 — Multi-stage escalation | Explicitly cut from PR #396 and superseded by merged PR #398 recovery behavior. | Qualify the superseding recovery behavior through the exact-head suite; do not reintroduce the cut state machine. |\n | Item 5 — Telemetry-informed throttle | Adaptive throttle code is present, but the roadmap says request-latency wiring and the CERI/CLI integration points remain unconnected. | Connect request latency to throttling, prove overload reduction and recovery, and test the runtime integration. |\n | Item 6 — Comparative evaluation harness | Comparative harness source is present in `origin/main`. | Verify its benchmark output and provenance on the integrated exact head. |\n@@ -46,7 +46,7 @@\n The final candidate remains unqualified until each applicable item is recorded against one exact commit and its artifacts:\n \n - All WP-1101–WP-1108 acceptance evidence and independent reviews are complete.\n-- Current v1.1.2 roadmap items 1, 2, 5, 6, and 7 are qualified on the exact candidate; cut items 3 and 4 remain deferred as documented.\n+- Current v1.1.2 roadmap items 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, and 7 are qualified on the exact candidate; item 4 is satisfied only if the superseding PR #398 recovery behavior passes exact-head qualification.\n - The full test suite, type checks, lint/security gates, migration and compatibility checks pass on the exact head.\n - Linux package outputs, checksums, SBOM, installer behavior, and reproducibility are ve