{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:08:10.454Z","ordinal":46611,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19e17-5056-7c73-84a2-56d4cc699d79","call_id":"call_14a15bf47ff9423c89426ebc85470a13","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 10.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7fdd68\",\"wall_time_seconds\":10.001806222,\"session_id\":41588,\"original_token_count\":1528,\"output\":\"  ✔ a project .env that sets HOME cannot send the operator's key to a spec resource's apiKeyEnv origin (V3n) (5454.357577ms)\\n  ✔ a re-homed token file that links to the operator's token reaches no foreign endpoint (i6i), even one the project selects (3409.207286ms)\\n  ✔ positive control: under the same re-homing .env, the operator's gateway still receives the stored token (890.347747ms)\\n  ✔ no credential material in CLI output, logs or durable state from these runs (1.270244ms)\\n✔ I6: only the operator environment and config.env decide where a stored credential goes (24009.085255ms)\\n✔ generated acyclic operations schedule only after dependencies complete and converge (66.477067ms)\\n✔ scheduler event callback failures produce bounded debug diagnostics (2.917071ms)\\n▶ resource eligibility\\n  ✔ 1. a 429 marks the resource that returned it ineligible, at model scope (4.055228ms)\\n  ✔ 2. Retry-After produces eligible_at = observed + delay (authoritative) (0.676105ms)\\n  ✔ 3. rate-limit reset metadata is honoured; with both hints the later window wins (3.220302ms)\\n  ✔ 4. no new work is assigned to a known-ineligible resource (13.701775ms)\\n  ✔ 5. unrelated providers and models stay eligible (0.663589ms)\\n✔ resource eligibility (25.196105ms)\\n▶ capability-aware rerouting\\n  ✔ 6. an equivalent qualified model is selected when the preferred one is rate-limited (4.697238ms)\\n  ✔ 7. an unqualified model is never selected merely because it is available (5.454561ms)\\n  ✔ 8. a reroute records why, from and to (3.182495ms)\\n✔ capability-aware rerouting (14.133549ms)\\n▶ parking and continuing independent work\\n  ✔ 9. work parks with its wake condition when no qualified alternate exists (9.383542ms)\\n  ✔ 10. independent work continues while a unit is parked (7.430498ms)\\n  ✔ 11. dependent work stays non-runnable until its dependencies complete (6.810649ms)\\n  ✔ 12. the operation does not WAIT while productive work exists (7.150545ms)\\n  ✔ 13. the operation WAITS when no productive work remains, and 14. sleeps until the eligibility time (7.425606ms)\\n  ✔ 15. a wake re-evaluates instead of executing the parked work blindly (3.697931ms)\\n  ✔ 16. a recovered resource becomes eligible again (0.667092ms)\\n  ✔ 17. after recovery another resource may still be the better choice (2.438025ms)\\n  ✔ 18. cancellation while waiting preserves the work (1.916989ms)\\n✔ parking and continuing independent work (48.106011ms)\\n▶ durable waiting across process restart\\n  ✔ 19. restart reconstructs the wake condition from durable state (375.208781ms)\\n  ✔ 20. an overdue wake after restart re-evaluates immediately (1035.669696ms)\\n  ✔ 21. a future wake after restart is rescheduled for the remaining time (1782.830738ms)\\n✔ durable waiting across process restart (3194.400322ms)\\n▶ provider outage\\n  ✔ 22. an endpoint outage reroutes to a qualified resource on another endpoint (3.318168ms)\\n  ✔ 23. an outage parks the work when no alternate exists, and it resumes once a probe succeeds (4.237221ms)\\n  ✔ 24. an outage of one endpoint coexists with independent work on another (6.56641ms)\\n✔ provider outage (14.699365ms)\\n▶ replay safety and non-temporary conditions\\n  ✔ 25. UNKNOWN execution is never turned into a submission elsewhere (10.574786ms)\\n  ✔ 26. auth and permanent failures are not temporary windows (2.810004ms)\\n  ✔ 27. simultaneous conditions are tracked independently (0.836201ms)\\n  ✔ 28. provider- and account-scope limits cover exactly that provider or credential (0.679103ms)\\n  ✔ 29. a model-scope limit covers that model on every endpoint of the provider, and nothing else (0.437058ms)\\n  ✔ 30. no busy loop: repeated failures back off and are bounded (4.625979ms)\\n✔ replay safety and non-temporary conditions (20.683312ms)\\n▶ compatibility and convergence\\n  ✔ 31. unit agents are pinned to the resource and never admit more context than it serves (4.868979ms)\\n  ✔ 32. durable state survives park, wait and resume (1108.446016ms)\\n  ✔ 33. completion still requires the original acceptance dependencies (5.968485ms)\\n  ✔ 34. a genuine no-safe-transition blocks with one concrete decision instead of looping (1.868165ms)\\n✔ compatibility and convergence (1121.698955ms)\\n▶ provider catalog enrichment (optional)\\n  ✔ gateway /v1/models metadata adds capabilities, context and pool; no serving capacity parks the model (1.583891ms)\\n  ✔ an expired catalog condition is re-checked before work is sent, not rediscovered with a request (2.081316ms)\\n  ✔ one driver per operation: a live holder excludes a second driver; a dead holder's lock is taken over (4.823379ms)\\n  ✔ dependency cycles and unknown references are rejected up front (0.576484ms)\\n  ✔ scheduler decisions are pure over state (no executor needed) (0.401971ms)\\n✔ provider catalog enrichment (optional) (9.958767ms)\\n▶ provider credential boundary\\n  ✔ the stored gateway credential is still sent to its gateway (92.845186ms)\\n  ✔ a foreign provider configured as the endpoint receives no stored credential, even after a 401 (26.736007ms)\\n  ✔ a planner on a foreign provider does not inherit the primary gateway's key (116.186972ms)\\n  ✔ an explicit foreign credential is used only for its own provider; the gateway keeps its own (15.495698ms)\\n✔ provider credential boundary (253.937774ms)\\n✔ storedCredentialFor and mayBindCredential do not follow a HOME changed after the authority was recorded (17.322257ms)\\n✔ the workspace root and the repository's own data cannot be deleted; ordinary paths can (2.411536ms)\\n▶ doctor findings name the actual failure\\n  ✔ config.project_env_ignored reports operator-only settings a workspace .env tries to set (REQ-SEC-110) (261.08567ms)\\n  ✔ malformed configuration fails config.valid while independent checks still run (77.196955ms)\\n  ✔ an unreachable endpoint fails reachability and skips what depends on it (98.441593ms)\\n  ✔ a hanging endpoint is bounded by the timeout (687.969849ms)\\n  ✔ the model list keeps the endpoint's /v1 path and the configured model is checked (240.757066ms)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793653690.4548273}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
