{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:10:50.659Z","ordinal":46698,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19e19-c223-7e42-a2cb-00f53e47d0e9","call_id":"call_e38bdfdbe7054e2db3a3c0668e17a1b2","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 10.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"61d4f2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":10.001722243,\"session_id\":41588,\"original_token_count\":1535,\"output\":\"▶ V2: process death while a subagent ran\\n  ✔ a subagent that wrote before the kill leaves the unit unverified after continuing (6331.933627ms)\\n✔ V2: process death while a subagent ran (6332.853544ms)\\n▶ durable operation records match their start whatever the provider's call id looks like\\n  ✔ a high-entropy invocation id is redacted on disk, yet the operation is recorded as completed; recorded progress clears it (267.634627ms)\\n✔ durable operation records match their start whatever the provider's call id looks like (268.171836ms)\\n✔ session continuation restores recovery fields without trusting its verifier baseline (408.460579ms)\\n▶ WP-05: Sensitive-Data Egress Interception & Secret Quarantine (INC-06)\\n  ▶ DATA-001, DATA-002, DATA-004: Formal Classification & Detection\\n    ✔ DATA-002: Classifies into formal categories with normative confidence levels (6.61743ms)\\n    ✔ DATA-001: Detects vendor credentials, tokens, bearer headers, and PEM keys (3.473386ms)\\n    ✔ DATA-003: Preserves code identifiers and matches RHS values only (2.26784ms)\\n    ✔ DATA-004: Calculates Shannon entropy and flags high-entropy random secrets (6.744357ms)\\n    ✔ DATA-004: Detects 20-31 character high-entropy tokens (FINDING-WP05-002) (1.569964ms)\\n  ✔ DATA-001, DATA-002, DATA-004: Formal Classification & Detection (22.93793ms)\\n  ▶ DEST-001, DEST-002: Destination Classification & Boundary Crossing\\n    ✔ DEST-001: Correctly classifies destinations into the 4 trust ranks (13.302896ms)\\n    ✔ DEST-002: Transition enforcement detects lower-trust crossing (0.483649ms)\\n    ✔ ACC-TRUST-02: CIDR classification table, reason codes, and operator origins (3.848277ms)\\n  ✔ DEST-001, DEST-002: Destination Classification & Boundary Crossing (18.370912ms)\\n  ▶ DISC-001, DISC-002, DISC-005: Disclosure Invariants & Protection Modes\\n    ✔ DISC-001: Resource authority does not confer disclosure authority (2.460629ms)\\n    ✔ DISC-005: Supports IRREVERSIBLE_REDACTION mode permanently destroying plaintext (1.39728ms)\\n  ✔ DISC-001, DISC-002, DISC-005: Disclosure Invariants & Protection Modes (4.171106ms)\\n  ▶ REHYD-001..005: Unguessable Scoped References & Anti-Forgery\\n    ✔ REHYD-001: Reference tokens are cryptographically unguessable nonces (prohibiting sequential integers) (1.143273ms)\\n    ✔ REHYD-002: Tokens are strictly scoped to owning taskId (cross-task fails closed) (1.556063ms)\\n    ✔ REHYD-003: Possession alone != authority (isAuthorizedSink=false leaves tokens inert) (0.951794ms)\\n    ✔ REHYD-005: Forged, stale, or unknown tokens remain completely inert (0.424609ms)\\n  ✔ REHYD-001..005: Unguessable Scoped References & Anti-Forgery (4.56933ms)\\n  ▶ FAIL-003: Fail-Closed Behavior on Failure\\n    ✔ FAIL-003: Simulated classifier failure fails closed and blocks egress (0.730303ms)\\n    ✔ FAIL-003: LocalLlmClient fails closed and refuses dispatch if egress evaluation fails (7.505592ms)\\n  ✔ FAIL-003: Fail-Closed Behavior on Failure (8.728451ms)\\n⚠️ [Failover] chatCompletion failed on http://127.0.0.1:30563/v1 (Inference error (HTTP 503): {\\\"error\\\":\\\"Local vLLM unavailable\\\"}). Trying backup endpoint http://127.0.0.1:36237/v1...\\n\\n⚡ Failover: Active inference endpoint switched to http://127.0.0.1:36237/v1\\n  ▶ CTX-006: Route Fallback Trust Re-Admission\\n    ✔ CTX-006: Fallback switching from high-trust to low-trust endpoint re-evaluates egress (150.434181ms)\\n  ✔ CTX-006: Route Fallback Trust Re-Admission (151.173277ms)\\n  ▶ TEST-003: Dynamic Transport Capture Verification\\n    ✔ TEST-003: Outbound chatCompletion transmits 0 synthetic secrets in serialized HTTP body (22.220016ms)\\n    ✔ TEST-003: Outbound chatCompletionStream transmits 0 synthetic secrets in serialized HTTP body (17.980451ms)\\n    ✔ TEST-003: Outbound generateEmbedding transmits 0 synthetic secrets in serialized HTTP body (FINDING-WP05-004) (13.450594ms)\\n  ✔ TEST-003: Dynamic Transport Capture Verification (54.510051ms)\\n  ▶ Adversarial Attacks on References and Authority\\n    ✔ Token guessing attack: brute force random tokens find 0 matches (8.532052ms)\\n    ✔ Authority attack: Full-access execution authority does NOT bypass disclosure interception (1.262459ms)\\n  ✔ Adversarial Attacks on References and Authority (10.125389ms)\\n✔ WP-05: Sensitive-Data Egress Interception & Secret Quarantine (INC-06) (277.514246ms)\\n▶ authorization header schemes\\n  ✔ Basic and Token credentials are classified and redacted (2.246888ms)\\n✔ authorization header schemes (2.609653ms)\\n▶ environment-declared secrets\\n  ✔ a redaction pass over many strings reads the environment once, and still redacts its secrets (56.148894ms)\\n✔ environment-declared secrets (56.57034ms)\\n▶ contextual secrets in code\\n  ✔ code that names a credential is left intact; quoted values and env-file values are classified (3.409185ms)\\n  ✔ trailing quote, semicolon and comma delimiters are stripped from a contextual value (1.363968ms)\\n✔ contextual secrets in code (5.367028ms)\\n▶ paths are not secrets\\n  ✔ workspace and worktree paths are not classified as high-entropy tokens (1.553223ms)\\n✔ paths are not secrets (1.847234ms)\\n▶ Nexus identifiers are not secrets\\n  ✔ generated session ids are never classified, while a real high-entropy token still is (2349.905524ms)\\n✔ Nexus identifiers are not secrets (2350.250724ms)\\n✔ invocation-local reuse preserves contextual, key and serialized redaction (19.516369ms)\\n✔ redaction reuse never crosses an environment or policy change (2.009583ms)\\n✔ all contextual key aliases retain classification with case and identifier prefixes (12.46085ms)\\n▶ RustCoreBridge hello handshake (REQ-REL-103)\\n  ✔ handshake succeeds against real core engine and reports correct protocol and version (27.59749ms)\\n  ✔ handshake fails actionably when protocol mismatches (68.296148ms)\\n  ✔ handshake fails actionably when version mismatches (92.685635ms)\\n  ✔ handshake fails when hello RPC returns an error (63.986688ms)\\n  ✔ handshake fails when hello RPC returns non-JSON (76.627423ms)\\n✔ RustCoreBridge hello handshake (REQ-REL-103) (332.913454ms)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793653850.659145}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
