{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:11:26.057Z","ordinal":46716,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19e1a-4c69-74e1-ad59-c2ba150a59cf","call_id":"call_7f6efd91ccda42ff84745041a036ed29","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 10.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"67e50a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":10.001011695,\"session_id\":41588,\"original_token_count\":1694,\"output\":\"✔ resource supervisor preserves SIGTERM grace for descendants after the main payload exits (2817.955679ms)\\n✖ candidate sandbox and resource supervisor compose around a staged repository (471.069197ms)\\n✖ repository workspaces carry no history beyond the pinned baseline commit (584.641738ms)\\n✔ task paths reject traversal, symlink escapes, and unstable task trees (5.769449ms)\\n✔ task-tree digests frame paths, entry types, executable mode, and content lengths (22.823848ms)\\n✖ task setup and validators run with cleared env, no network, confined filesystem, bounded output and timeout (91.603575ms)\\n✖ candidate namespace cannot read host files or bypass pinned compilers with absolute paths (98.82409ms)\\n✔ qualification corpus binding rejects missing, mismatched, and post-seal task content (5.761768ms)\\n✔ run.mjs refuses to start on an invalid task (263.85909ms)\\n✔ the model proxy injects each scheduled fault into the chat request it names, and records it (67.542782ms)\\n✔ executable probes refuse bind sources that overlap protected corpus material (8.97005ms)\\n✔ --pairs escapes control characters in task IDs in mismatch diagnostics (94.755959ms)\\n✔ --pairs escapes control characters in task IDs in missing-budget and missing-run diagnostics (178.090598ms)\\n✔ --pairs escapes control characters in successful human-readable task tables (392.413718ms)\\n✔ T3 task schema requires steering with checkable constraints, a fact sheet, a long budget and Nexus only (29.54194ms)\\n✔ the T3 driver submits the objective, steers after the scripted tool calls, snapshots, probes, then shuts down (3407.784866ms)\\n✔ the noninteractive T3 driver cancels a checkpoint choice request and does not hang (2.718736ms)\\n✔ the probe answer is the last balanced JSON object (1.583617ms)\\n✔ compactions count only ids a session or task record commits that have originals in its own archive (10.730885ms)\\n✔ T3 evaluator rejects candidate symlinks in workspace facts and steering snapshots (10.851968ms)\\n✔ T3 compaction counting rejects symlinks in HOME, .nexus categories, records and archives (10.173213ms)\\n✔ T3 scoring judges the snapshot: steering honoured only when applied, violable and kept; false absence counted (4.687075ms)\\n✖ a T3 run drives the real sidecar through the sandbox: steering applied, probe answered and scored (343.756878ms)\\n✖ the real T3 runner fails closed when a candidate-created fact path symlinks to an external canary (285.520461ms)\\n✔ the T3 gate passes only a full, clean 8 × 5 workload with no false absence or false presence (557.945339ms)\\n✔ a steer counts as violable only if its constraint could fail: path present, or command failing at baseline (2.11661ms)\\n✔ a command baseline that does not exit cleanly is a harness error, never a granted precondition (1.590518ms)\\n✖ the production version-probe workspace uses the configured capped filesystem (3.721667ms)\\n▶ WP-04: Evaluator Candidate Binding (VER-001, VER-005, F-02)\\n  ✔ Evaluator loads dataset cleanly from JSON and JSONL formats (2.589639ms)\\n  ✔ F-02 & CAND-001: Evaluator binds validation receipts directly to candidate identity (69.751064ms)\\n  ✔ evaluator does not issue a passed receipt when candidate identity is unresolved (0.563566ms)\\n  ✔ Evaluator scorecard renders summary metrics (13.576327ms)\\n✔ WP-04: Evaluator Candidate Binding (VER-001, VER-005, F-02) (89.10059ms)\\n▶ evidence ledger\\n  ✔ quoted and escape-split secrets in arguments are redacted (12.820362ms)\\n  ✔ each call gets a new id and a running record that the end fills in (5.065885ms)\\n  ✔ a failed call keeps its output and appends the error (2.342033ms)\\n  ✔ secrets and terminal escapes are removed and long output is capped (5.826792ms)\\n  ✔ only the latest records are kept (4.693539ms)\\n✔ evidence ledger (33.516399ms)\\n▶ receipt projection\\n  ✔ before any turn every section says why it is empty (1.194913ms)\\n  ✔ a verified turn with a receipt lists every field, redacted (6.442127ms)\\n  ✔ a receipt read back from disk with missing fields drops those rows instead of sending null (1.5768ms)\\n✔ receipt projection (10.051169ms)\\n▶ identities\\n  ✔ action identity ignores key order, whitespace and is independent of call ids (3.119733ms)\\n  ✔ outcome identity ignores timestamps, durations, uuids, request ids and temp paths, not content (3.431238ms)\\n  ✔ a command's exit code decides its outcome, and its timing fields are not part of it (4.82127ms)\\n  ✔ transient and deterministic failures are told apart (0.505535ms)\\n  ✔ an unknown part makes a combined state unknown (0.851405ms)\\n✔ identities (16.391208ms)\\n▶ repetition is judged on action, outcome and state\\n  ✔ the same read on an unchanged state is a loop at the threshold; reformatted args and new call ids do not hide it (1.6845ms)\\n  ✔ a retry after a meaningful input change is a new observation, not a repeat (1.361804ms)\\n  ✔ an external command's unchanged success is a poll, not a loop; a transient failure is waited out (3.963202ms)\\n  ✔ a deterministic failure repeated on an unchanged state is a loop and is recorded as a failed approach (1.240174ms)\\n  ✔ re-reading output compaction removed is re-acquisition, not a loop; recurring re-acquisition is context thrash (1.776987ms)\\n  ✔ on an unknown state nothing is called a repeat or a loop (1.114286ms)\\n✔ repetition is judged on action, outcome and state (12.644181ms)\\n▶ progress\\n  ✔ a new workspace state, new information or a new ledger state is progress; plan edits and identical rewrites are not (2.18336ms)\\n  ✔ operator input resets the no-progress run without erasing repetition evidence (1.272735ms)\\n  ✔ ACC-CONT-09 / REQ-AGT-108: distinct workspace mutations on unknown state count as progress; identical writes stagnate (5.150326ms)\\n✔ progress (9.238181ms)\\n▶ bounded storage does not hide a loop\\n  ✔ repetition records showing recurrence survive eviction pressure; an evicted triple still counts when it recurs (123.368037ms)\\n✔ bounded storage does not hide a loop (123.671401ms)\\n▶ compaction thrash evidence\\n  ✔ consecutive low-yield pressure compactions are counted; a useful one resets the run (0.618263ms)\\n✔ compaction thrash evidence (0.929718ms)\\n▶ the ledger carries tracking\\n  ✔ a new ledger has tracking; a restored ledger without it is completed; the pinned block shows loops and failures (3.632563ms)\\n  ✔ every holder shares one tracking record: re-reading it never orphans a running tracker (0.653851ms)\\n  ✔ an unfinished single-request objective continued with 'continue' keeps its ledger; new work starts a new one (1.601852ms)\\n  ✔ AGT-13: recordAttempt counter is monotonic beyond 50 attempts (0.923627ms)\\n✔ the ledger carries tracking (7.246484ms)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793653886.0571246}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
