{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:16:24.141Z","ordinal":46891,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19e1e-d8cd-7431-b0cd-28592a6d31fe","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- v1.1.2-release: state=21:12 UTC: exact artifact-built suite passed all observed continuation/recovery, core RPC, packaged launcher, and most regular CLI groups. It reached evaluator host/isolation scenarios; 21 individual eval tests have failed there so far, likely host isolation/toolchain prerequisites but require exact error details. Harness is continuing through `VERIFIED needs evidence` tests; no aggregate result yet., phase=GREEN, gate=Full suite active with evaluator/isolation failures observed; core/CLI groups pass. Types/build PASS; process-scope pending., next=Let node:test and terminal process-scope gate finish; capture failure stacks, then distinguish environment failures from source defects., friction=Evaluator/black-box sandbox acceptance tests are red on this host; exact causes pending from final failure details., updated=2026-11-02T21:12:00Z, reviewer=/root/review_delta, verdict=APPROVED release-scope alignment; WP-1103 source diff previously approved; exact gate pending., retrieval=nexus-test eval_integrity.test.ts:1729 SSE tool-call stream; eval_harness.test.ts:43 deterministic reply pattern; provider_connect.test.ts:31 local provider harness, active_agents=Read-only audit delegated to /root/v112_unblocked_work to identify safe progress that does not load the shared test host., heartbeat=2026-11-02T21:12:00Z, claim=SUITE held in /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1103-a0d374e8, updated 3 minutes ago\n- ...784 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-02 9:16pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 25 obs (8,599t read) | 46,855t work | 82% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\n27913 8:47p ○ esbuild Subprocess Spawned by Test — Still Running at 4:14, Parent Node Waiting on ep_poll\n27914 8:48p ○ No Active TCP Connections for PIDs 730133/730147 — Local Gateway Already Closed\n27915 8:49p ○ SIGTERM Sent to Stuck Test Process — Suite Resumed, Full Test File List Visible\n27916 8:52p ○ D3 Timeout Lifecycle Group Fails — Two Verifier Timeout/Failure Tests Both Failing\n27917 8:53p ○ WP-1103 Suite Final Failure Catalog — Upgrade, Verifier Trust, and Launcher Groups\n27918 \" ○ verifier_timeout.test.ts Root Cause Confirmed — Verification Returns NOT_REQUIRED Instead of VERIFIER_TIMED_OUT/VERIFIER_FAILED\n27919 \" ○ v112-wp1103-a0d374e8 Worktree Git Status — Multiple Modified and Untracked Files\n27920 \" ○ WP-1103 Suite Complete — Full Failure Catalog Confirmed, Log Finalized\n27921 \" ○ SUITE Claim Now Empty — Test Host Available for New Suite Run\n27922 \" ○ Both Build Artifacts Confirmed Missing in v112-wp1103-a0d374e8 Worktree\n27923 \" ○ 383 Total Named Failures in WP-1103 Suite — Build Command Confirmed as `cargo build --release --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml`\n27924 8:54p ✓ v1.1.2 Work State Updated to RED Phase — Build Prerequisites Required Before Rerun\n27925 \" ✓ CLI TypeScript Build Succeeded in Snapshot Worktree — cli/dist/index.js Now Present\n27926 8:55p ✓ Rust Core Binaries Built Successfully — harness-core and nexus-tui Now Present\n27927 8:56p ○ v1.1.2-qualification.md Differs Between WP-1103 and WP-1104 Worktrees — Item 3 Scope Changed\n27928 \" ✓ Qualification Doc Synced and All Build Artifacts Verified Present in Snapshot Worktree\n27929 \" ✓ v1.1.2 Work State Advanced to GREEN Phase — Second Suite Rerun Active with Built Artifacts\n27930 8:57p ○ Git Symlink Error During Checkpoint Test — \"alias/file is beyond a symbolic link\"\n27931 9:01p ○ Compaction Group A Passes in Second Suite Run — 220 Seconds vs Prior Failure\n27932 9:02p ○ Compaction Groups B and C Both Pass — Second Suite Run Progressing Clean\n27934 \" ○ Active Test Process Loading tsx From WP-1104 Integration Worktree — Cross-Worktree tsx Loader Contamination\n27935 9:03p ○ All Compaction Groups C and D Pass — ComparativeEvaluationHarness Tests Also Pass\n27936 9:07p ○ harness.test.ts Groups I1 and G Pass — Previously Failing Tests Now Clean\n27940 9:11p ○ Second Suite Run — Sandbox and Verifier Trust Group Failures Persist\n27946 9:13p ✓ v1.1.2 Work State Updated — Evaluator/Isolation Failures Noted, Core Groups Pass\n\nAccess 47k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793654184.141644,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
