{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:42:50.265Z","ordinal":47359,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ff16caf4-0e45-4bd8-a0f3-da8c4bca52fd","process_id":"32309","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '15,45p' .github/workflows/ci.yml; sed -n '25,50p' .github/workflows/release.yml; sed -n '80,118p' .github/workflows/ci.yml; sed -n '1,120p' eval/host/README.md; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1103-a0d374e8","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '15,45p' .github/workflows/ci.yml; sed -n '25,50p' .github/workflows/release.yml; sed -n '80,118p' .github/workflows/ci.yml; sed -n '1,120p' eval/host/README.md; git rev-parse --git-common-dir; cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"    strategy:\n      fail-fast: false\n      matrix:\n        node: [22, 24]\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n      - run: sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install --yes acl make bubblewrap build-essential meson ninja-build pkg-config libcap-dev\n      - uses: actions/setup-go@40f1582b2485089dde7abd97c1529aa768e1baff # v5\n        with:\n          go-version: '1.22.12'\n      - name: Install pinned evaluator toolchains\n        run: bash scripts/install-evaluator-toolchains.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh\n      - name: Mount a dedicated capped tmpfs for evaluator resource fixtures\n        run: |\n          root=/mnt/nexus-eval-ci\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$root\"\n          sudo mount -t tmpfs -o size=128m,mode=0711,uid=\"$(id -u)\",gid=\"$(id -g)\" nexus-eval-ci \"$root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n          runtime_root=/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$runtime_root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT=$runtime_root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@949feb2413d6458794dcd2491c4babbbce0c15c1 # v7.1.0\n        with:\n          node-version: ${{ matrix.node }}\n          cache: npm\n          cache-dependency-path: cli/package-lock.json\n      - name: Install selected Node runtime for isolated evaluation commands\n        run: |\n          node_runtime=\"$(readlink -f \"$(command -v node)\")\"\n      - run: sudo apt-get update\n      - run: sudo apt-get install --yes acl make bubblewrap build-essential meson ninja-build pkg-config libcap-dev\n      - uses: actions/setup-go@40f1582b2485089dde7abd97c1529aa768e1baff # v5\n        with:\n          go-version: '1.22.12'\n      - name: Install pinned evaluator toolchains\n        run: bash scripts/install-evaluator-toolchains.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh\n      - name: Mount a dedicated capped tmpfs for evaluator resource fixtures\n        run: |\n          root=/mnt/nexus-eval-release\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$root\"\n          sudo mount -t tmpfs -o size=128m,mode=0711,uid=\"$(id -u)\",gid=\"$(id -g)\" nexus-eval-release \"$root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n          runtime_root=/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$runtime_root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT=$runtime_root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n      - uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@b725eda525362e7cf34af9a7243cac1e3f01a7ec # stable\n      - name: Install cargo tools (audit, deny, about, cyclonedx)\n        run: |\n          CARGO_HOME=\"${CARGO_HOME:-$HOME/.cargo}\"\n          export CARGO_HOME\n          mkdir -p \"$CARGO_HOME/bin\"\n          echo \"$CARGO_HOME/bin\" >> \"$GITHUB_PATH\"\n          export PATH=\"$CARGO_HOME/bin:$PATH\"\n        # Normal runs take 12-20 minutes; a test process that never exits must fail the job, not hold it for 6 hours.\n        timeout-minutes: 45\n        run: npm --prefix cli test\n\n  linux-x86_64:\n    needs: [test-matrix]\n    runs-on: ubuntu-22.04\n    env:\n      NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE: rust:1.95.0-bookworm@sha256:4c2fd73ef19c5ef9d54bee03b06b2839a392604fbfcd578ed948b71b37c1d7fb\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7.0.1\n      - run: sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install --yes acl make bubblewrap build-essential meson ninja-build pkg-config libcap-dev\n      - uses: actions/setup-go@40f1582b2485089dde7abd97c1529aa768e1baff # v5\n        with:\n          go-version: '1.22.12'\n      - name: Install pinned evaluator toolchains\n        run: bash scripts/install-evaluator-toolchains.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh\n      - run: bash scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh\n      - name: Mount a dedicated capped tmpfs for evaluator resource fixtures\n        run: |\n          root=/mnt/nexus-eval-ci\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$root\"\n          sudo mount -t tmpfs -o size=128m,mode=0711,uid=\"$(id -u)\",gid=\"$(id -g)\" nexus-eval-ci \"$root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT=$root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n          runtime_root=/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime\n          sudo install -d -o \"$USER\" -g \"$USER\" -m 0711 \"$runtime_root\"\n          echo \"NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT=$runtime_root\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@949feb2413d6458794dcd2491c4babbbce0c15c1 # v7.1.0\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n          cache: npm\n          cache-dependency-path: cli/package-lock.json\n      - name: Install selected Node runtime for isolated evaluation commands\n        run: |\n          node_runtime=\"$(readlink -f \"$(command -v node)\")\"\n          npm_cli=\"$(readlink -f \"$(command -v npm)\")\"\n          npm_root=\"$(dirname \"$(dirname \"$npm_cli\")\")\"\n          case \"$npm_root\" in */lib/node_modules/npm) ;; *) echo \"Unexpected setup-node npm package path\" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac\n# Qualification host\n\nThis directory is the reviewable procedure for preparing the host that runs `eval/run.mjs` for v1 qualification\n(ACCEPTANCE §6). The host is `mike-dev`: 12 cores (Xeon X5650, no SMT), 46 GiB RAM, 16 GiB swap, kernel 6.8,\nsystemd 255, cgroup v2 with `cpu memory pids` delegated to the operator's user manager. Inference is remote (the\nhomelab-ai gateway, DEC-16), so this host's CPU and memory serve only the agents, their builds and the tests.\n\nNothing here touches the inference appliance, the gateway, the firewall, model workers, credentials or other\nservices. The changes are limited to the following:\n\n| Change | File or object | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Install `acl` | apt package | `setfacl` grants the evaluator uid access to each disposable run directory (`grantRunAsAccess`). |\n| System account `nexus-eval` | `/etc/passwd`, `/var/lib/nexus-eval` (0700), shell `nologin` | The candidate and validators run as a uid that cannot read the operator's files or the held-out store. |\n| One sudoers rule | `/etc/sudoers.d/90-nexus-eval`: `<operator> ALL=(nexus-eval) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/bwrap` | The harness's only privilege. No `env`, no shell, no other command. |\n| Size-capped tmpfs | `srv-nexus\\x2dqual-ws.mount` at `/srv/nexus-qual/ws`, `size=storageBytes,mode=0711,uid=<operator>,nosuid,nodev` | The resource contract's `workspaceRoot`: the hard cap on what a run keeps, across all phases. |\n| Runtime directory | `/opt/nexus-qual` (root, 0755) | `sandboxRuntimeRoots` for the installed RC and the peer agents. It is filled per RC. |\n\n- `/usr/bin/bwrap` must report upstream version 0.12.0 or later (CVE-2026-87766). `validate.mjs` cannot detect distro backports, so it also rejects older vendor-patched builds. Ubuntu 24.04 `0.9.0-1ubuntu0.3` removed the fix. Install a release with the fix before qualification; `scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh` shows the pinned source build that CI uses. `provision.sh` does not replace the binary.\n- `provision.sh` applies these changes and is idempotent. It never remounts an active tmpfs.\n- `rollback.sh` removes them. It keeps `/opt/nexus-qual` unless you pass `--purge-runtime`, and it leaves `acl` installed.\n- `validate.mjs`, run as the operator, proves the result using infrastructure fixtures only.\n\n```sh\nsudo OPERATOR=mike bash eval/host/provision.sh\nnode eval/host/validate.mjs --heldout <sealed task store> --json docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%MZ).json\n# undo: sudo bash eval/host/rollback.sh\n```\n\n`eval/host/container-test/run.sh` exercises provision and rollback as root in a disposable privileged container:\nfresh and repeated runs, rollback, refusal of a foreign account, sudoers file or symlinked root (with no changes),\nrecovery from an interrupted run, and rollback leaving a re-created account alone. Every line must read PASS.\n\n`validate.mjs` uses the operator's own root sudo for two probes of the custodian's root-owned store: that it\nexists, and which file to try reading as the evaluator. The file's name is used but never printed or stored. These\nprobes need the operator's general sudo, not the narrow evaluator rule.\n\nThe harness's `asUser` invokes `/usr/bin/sudo -n -u nexus-eval -- /usr/bin/bwrap …` directly. sudo's `env_reset`\nand Bubblewrap's `--clearenv` clear the environment, so the rule names only `/usr/bin/bwrap`. This host's sudo PAM\nstack (`common-session-noninteractive`) does not load `pam_systemd`, so a process switched to `nexus-eval` stays in the\nrun's cgroup. `validate.mjs` checks this.\n\n## Resource profile\n\n`resource-profile.json` holds the values. The three frozen T2 configs and every T3/T4 config embed them as their\n`resources` object, byte-identical. `score.mjs --pairs` refuses comparisons whose manifests differ.\n\nCustodian calibration across all 40 sealed T2 reference solutions passed 40/40 under this profile:\n`maxMemoryPeakMiB` 1206.5, `maxPidsPeak` 163, `maxWorkspaceMiB` 225.0, `oomKills` 0, and `pidsMaxEvents` 0.\n\n| Key | Frozen | Exact kernel meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cpuPercent` | 800 | `cpu.max = 800000 100000`. The payload's processes may together use at most 8 CPUs' worth of runtime per wall-clock second. This is **rate throttling, not a total budget**. Total CPU time is bounded only by the phase's wall-clock limit times 8, and each phase's `cpuUsageUsec` and `cpuThrottledUsec` are recorded. |\n| `memoryBytes` | 16 GiB | `memory.max`, with `memory.swap.max = 0` and `memory.oom.group = 1`. The charge counts the phase's anonymous memory, the page cache it faults in (reclaimable before OOM), **and the tmpfs pages it writes**. A phase that writes 6 GiB of build output therefore has about 10 GiB left for its processes. Exceeding the limit OOM-kills the whole phase, and this is recorded. |\n| `tasks` | 4096 | `pids.max`. This counts threads, not just processes: Go test binaries, `cargo` with parallel `rustc`, and Node/Bun worker threads all consume tasks. |\n| `storageBytes` | 20 GiB | The size of the dedicated tmpfs. It caps everything a run holds in its workspace and home **across phases**, because when a phase's cgroup is removed, its tmpfs charges move to the unlimited parent. Writes beyond the cap fail with `ENOSPC`. Runs are serial, and each run's directories are removed afterwards. |\n\n### Why these values\n\n- **Fairness.** Nexus, Goose and OpenCode get identical limits. Each agent's own process is small next to them: OpenCode\n  about 1.1 GiB RSS, the others less, as observed on this host. No agent is systematically starved.\n- **CPU.** Eight of the twelve cores leave four for the harness, the model proxy, the OS and the box's other tenants.\n  Then load from those tenants cannot change a run's available CPU. The X5650 is slow, so the throttle is set\n  high enough not to bind on a normal build.\n- **Memory and threads.** Sized for the heaviest language class in the corpus, Rust test builds, where parallel `rustc`\n  plus a multi-GiB target directory on tmpfs both count. The measurement below records this repository's own\n  `core` crate under the contract as a lower-bound reference.\n- **Storage.** The worst-case RAM is a full tmpfs plus a phase at its memory limit: 20 + 16 = 36 GiB. Together with\n  about 7 GiB of other host use (`free` on 2026-10-18 09:40Z: 7 GiB used, 39 GiB available), that stays below the\n  46 GiB of physical memory. The margin is only about 3 GiB, so the other host load is re-measured and recorded in\n  the run record before each qualification window. If that load grows, the box can reach swap.\n\n### Freezing\n\n1. **Calibration (custodian, before freeze).** The custodian validates every sealed task's reference solution under\n   this profile and reports only aggregates: pass count; maximum `memoryPeakBytes`, `pidsPeak` and workspace bytes\n   across phases; any OOM, pids or ENOSPC event; and the longest phase wall time under the 8-CPU throttle, compared\n   with the task's budget. Agents rebuild repeatedly, unlike a single reference build, so the storage headroom is\n   checked against a reference build repeated three times in one workspace. If a reference fails because of a limit, the limit is raised, the\n   change is recorded, and calibration is repeated. No candidate result is involved.\n2. **Freeze.** Set `\"status\": \"frozen\"`, commit, and record the profile's SHA-256 in the frozen run record\n   (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) before the first qualification run.\n3. **After freeze.** Values never change in response to qualification outcomes. A change for any reason after the\n   first scored run invalidates the affected runs. They are kept as evidence and rerun.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git\n{\n  \"agent\": \"codex-root\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/v112-wp1104-integration\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1103-a0d374e8\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-11-02T20:12:45Z\",\n  \"pid\": 516692,\n  \"scope\": \"exact-source full test and build for WP-1103 integration on current origin/main a0d374e8\",\n  \"heartbeat\": \"2026-11-02T20:26:22Z\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":751586851}},"started_at_ms":1793655769513,"completed_at_ms":1793655770265}}
