{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T21:47:54.337Z","ordinal":47578,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016ae90509546881a3bfa8235f15acdf52","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The repeated failures now have two concrete host causes, both outside the source change: the checked-in compiler-scan helper was group-writable due to this host’s shared-worktree umask, so the fail-closed guard rejected it; and CI-specific evaluator roots were not passed to the local runner. The host already has the pinned Go/Rust toolchains, cgroup delegation, a 128 MiB capped tmpfs, and a runtime fixture. I’ve restored the helper to its tracked 0644 mode and am rerunning all evaluator tests with those fixtures configured."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793656073363,"completed_at_ms":1793656074337}}
