{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:49:42.803Z","ordinal":49109,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a19e74-4693-7960-bf00-1393c76f8cfd","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Made something a person can open (PR, deck, page, image, report)? Attach it to that item: fields {\"work_product\": \"https://…\" or \"/absolute/file\"}; several, with titles, as one JSON string: \"[{\\\"title\\\": \\\"<name>\\\", \\\"url\\\": \\\"https://…\\\"}]\"\n- Deliverables: write a deck, report, page or other file the person asked for as a file and attach it as work_product before you finish. When you stop, claude-mem copies each attached file (and any deck, document, page, image or spreadsheet you wrote outside the source tree) into this project's deliverables bucket, ~/.claude-mem/deliverables/<project>/, and links it on the request's card in My Work.\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...785 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-11-02 10:49pm UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 25 obs (8,938t read) | 49,101t work | 82% savings\n\n### Nov 2, 2026\n28037 9:52p ◆ Eval Test Suite 91/91 Pass — All Previously-Failing Evaluator Tests Now Clean\n28038 \" ○ WP-1103 Worktree State: 8 Modified Files, 13 Untracked New Files, HEAD at Merge Commit a0d374e8\n28039 \" ○ v1.1.2 Release Gate Status — All Five Gates Still Open or Partial\n28040 9:58p ○ Full Suite Log Now Contains compaction/restart Tracking Tests — Different Test File Running\n28041 10:04p ○ convergence_invariants.test.ts Running — jbd2 Stall on New Test File, harness-core Binary Active\n28042 10:10p ○ WP-1103 and WP-1104 CLI Tests Passing — Versioned Eval Dataset Options and RustCoreBridge Handshake\n28063 10:31p ○ Host IO Pressure Spiked to avg10=25.73 During Extended jbd2 Stall on PID 1416567\n28064 10:32p ○ jbd2 Stall on PID 1416567 Cleared — Process Exited After 3+ Minutes, Suite Progressed\n28065 10:45p ◆ Full npm Test Suite Completes — 2246/2251 Pass, 0 Fail, 5 Skip in 52.5 Minutes\n28066 \" ○ Full Suite Log SHA-256 Captured — bae2a5b6c347... — WP-1103 Worktree Git Status Confirmed\n28067 10:46p ○ WP-1104 Integration Worktree Has Uncommitted Changes — Qualification Doc and Oracle Isolation Doc Modified\n28068 \" ○ WP-1104 Integration Branch Diverges from WP-1103 Worktree by 111 Files — CERI, Independent Review, and Nonprogress Recovery Added\n28069 \" ○ WP-1103 and WP-1104 Integration Branch Share Merge Base 593d569b — Integration is 7 Ahead, WP-1103 is 28 Ahead\n28070 10:47p ○ WP-1103 and WP-1104 File Claims Still Held by WP-1104 Integration Worktree — Stale Heartbeats at 20:26 UTC\n28071 \" ○ WP-1103 Worktree Has 60+ Uncommitted Files — All WP-1103 Feature Work Untracked in Current Worktree\n28072 10:48p ◆ New Worktree v112-integrated-exact Created at Exact WP-1103 Merge Commit\n28073 \" ✓ v1.1.2 Release Work State Updated to INTEGRATE Phase with Exact Suite Gate PASS\n28074 \" ○ WP-1103 Candidate Patch Scope: 8 Modified Files, 51 Untracked New Files\n28075 \" ○ WP-1104 Integration Branch Holds 59 nexus-claims on WP-1103 Files\n28076 \" ✓ 50 nexus-claims Transferred from Stale Integration Branch to Exact a0d374e8 Worktree\n28077 \" ○ SUITE Claim Held by Dead PID 1164203 — Last Heartbeat 22:05 UTC, All PIDs Gone\n28078 \" ✓ SUITE nexus-claim Released After Exact Candidate Suite PASS\n28079 10:49p ◆ WP-1103 Candidate Patch Applied to Clean v112-integrated-exact Worktree\n28080 \" ○ WP-1103 Candidate Tree Hash Computed: ac52532540209a39e2aad86af84a16ba375dd770\n28081 \" ○ Source-Tree Identity Verified — Both Worktrees Produce Identical Tree SHA ac52532540\n\nAccess 49k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only. Worker runtime: use Smart search by default: follow the mem-search skill in three steps—search({query, project}) for an index, timeline({anchor}) for context around relevant results, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records you choose after reviewing the index and context. Do not use auto or guided modes. Optional Dumb search, dumb_search({query, project}): Doesn’t reason about the results. Fast, but shallow. Use Smart for reliable recall. A hosted read-only connector may expose searches without write tools; do not call a missing write tool.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793659782.8034215,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"],"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"harness","hook":true}}]}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:49:44.155Z","ordinal":49110,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0fd4138577b17921016ae91387b90881a3b1428cd3b1fc88b9","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I’m continuing from the exact-base candidate: first I’m checking the current release work state and peer-review availability, then I’ll close the qualification evidence and keep moving through the remaining v1.1.2 roadmap items."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793659783744,"completed_at_ms":1793659784155}}
