{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:49:50.411Z","ordinal":49129,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016ae9138cfed081a3af0fcd55f829a743","status":"completed","call_id":"call_eb22d27e993e4304854a5b191d57a163","name":"exec","input":"const rr = await Promise.all([\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git status --short && git rev-parse --show-toplevel && git rev-parse HEAD && git status --branch --short\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact\",max_output_tokens:2000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,220p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact\",max_output_tokens:4000}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,200p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact\",max_output_tokens:3500}),\n  tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git diff --stat && git diff --name-only\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact\",max_output_tokens:1500})\n]);\nfor (let i=0;i<rr.length;i++) text(`RESULT ${i+1}\\n${rr[i].output}`);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793659788.9970438}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:49:50.459Z","ordinal":49130,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016ae9138c3e7c81a39822380bfb052b74","usage":{"input_tokens":45429,"cached_input_tokens":44032,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":319,"reasoning_output_tokens":55,"total_tokens":45748},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":95044421,"cached_input_tokens":94219008,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":145499,"reasoning_output_tokens":70102,"total_tokens":95189920},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":957456150,"cached_input_tokens":949381632,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1961687,"reasoning_output_tokens":995273,"total_tokens":959417837}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:49:52.648Z","ordinal":49131,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-01bf3dba-338c-4c51-b139-7394b1999f08","process_id":"76173","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,220p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md","name":"v1.1.2-qualification.md","path":"docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Nexus Code v1.1.2 Qualification Record\n\n**Status as of 2026-11-02: NOT QUALIFIED.** This record tracks the full WP-1101–WP-1108 scope selected for v1.1.2 and the five release gates in the [roadmap](../v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md). Evidence from a focused test, source review, earlier branch, or prior release is not a pass for the exact final candidate.\n\nThe v1.1.0 release failed and published no release files. v1.1.1 is the published predecessor. GitHub currently has no v1.1.2 release and the remote has no v1.1.2 tag. The v1.1.2 release notes and the former rc.1 draft describe the approved scope and the superseded narrow draft respectively.\n\n## Current v1.1.2 roadmap alignment\n\n`origin/main` at `a0d374e8` adds the repository's [Specialist Orchestration and Independent Review roadmap](../v1.1.2/ROADMAP.md). This record retains the user-approved WP-1101–WP-1108 scope above and tracks that current roadmap's remaining release commitments as well; neither scope is treated as a substitute for the other.\n\n| Roadmap item | Current source state | v1.1.2 qualification still required |\n|---|---|---|\n| Item 1 — Specialist contracts | Runtime roles, contracts, and tool permissions are connected in `origin/main`; PR #396 review fixes are present. | Run the exact-head specialist profile and runtime tests; review the integrated candidate. |\n| Item 2 — Independent review boundary | Reviewer evidence packaging and verdict gating are connected in `origin/main`. | Run exact-head boundary, verifier, and operation tests; independently review the integrated behavior. |\n| Item 3 — Deterministic micro-routing | Explicitly cut from PR #396; no runtime implementation is present in `origin/main`. The roadmap does not explicitly defer this item from the v1.1.2 release. | **OPEN.** Under the user-approved full-roadmap scope, implement and test deterministic query fast paths plus model fallback and provenance for ambiguous requests. |\n| Item 4 — Multi-stage escalation | Explicitly cut from PR #396 and superseded by merged PR #398 recovery behavior. | Qualify the superseding recovery behavior through the exact-head suite; do not reintroduce the cut state machine. |\n| Item 5 — Telemetry-informed throttle | Adaptive throttle code is present, but the roadmap says request-latency wiring and the CERI/CLI integration points remain unconnected. | Connect request latency to throttling, prove overload reduction and recovery, and test the runtime integration. |\n| Item 6 — Comparative evaluation harness | Comparative harness source is present in `origin/main`. | Verify its benchmark output and provenance on the integrated exact head. |\n| Item 7 — CERI | PR #396 supplies foundational modules, but the roadmap says they are not yet connected to the agent runtime and `nexus eval` entry point. | Complete the required CERI evaluation, provenance, classification, non-self-approval, and operational reporting integrations; meet the roadmap's release-qualification acceptance criteria. |\n\n## Work-package status\n\n| Package | Required outcome | Observed evidence | Status | Evidence still required for v1.1.2 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| WP-1101 — OpenTelemetry local tracing | Local GenAI spans for turns, model requests, tools, and compactions; credentials protected and trace output confined. | Prototype commit `8a83c9e7` lacks runtime event wiring and exact-head gate evidence. | **OPEN** | Integrated runtime wiring, tracing and redaction regressions, path-confinement proof, exact-head review and gates. |\n| WP-1102 — Flight recorder credential redaction | Zero-leak sanitization across traces, CLI errors, and debug journals. | Commit `ee7c8b1e` contains partial redaction work; operator acceptance remains pending. | **OPEN** | Full sink coverage, adversarial/credential fixtures, operator acceptance, and exact-head review. |\n| WP-1103 — Versioned evaluation datasets | Versioned datasets with separate examples/oracles and regression/benchmark splits; candidate prompts cannot access oracles. | Integration branch `v1/v112-wp1104-integration` is at docs-scope HEAD `eb6884df` with pending AC2 test and plan edits. The mount-view test passed focused 3/3; source-level peer review accepted the diff after removal of a duplicate, misleading evidence file. The full snapshot run at `00a8cb4d` failed (2,133 pass, 3 fail, 2 skipped; log SHA-256 `e6ea08b2b56c3f1ada337290db9ae0601921a23f99fd1ca50e7d95b507f870e9`) during concurrent PR396 test traffic. That snapshot is not the exact integration source and has no process-scope postcheck. | **PARTIAL / UNQUALIFIED** | Clean serialized full suite and process-scope postcheck on the exact integration source; resolve or independently classify all failures; complete fresh full-slice review and candidate-specific evidence. |\n| WP-1104 — Standalone `nexus eval` | Packaged command supports dataset selection, run count, isolated home, and structured score output. | Source commits `05c49df2` and `2a94f62e` were reviewed; `npm run build` passed. Focused six-task installed-candidate acceptance is recorded in `WP-1104-PLAN.md`, but it is not final integrated-candidate qualification. | **SOURCE SLICE CLOSED / RELEASE GATE OPEN** | Re-run applicable checks on the final integrated candidate; prove package parity and installed CLI operation without developer dependencies; fresh independent review. |\n| WP-1105 — Deterministic code evaluators | Modular AST, build, typecheck, diff-boundary, and JSON-repair evaluators. | Worktree `v1/wp-1105-evaluators` has untracked `eval/evaluators/` files and no WP-1105 commit or test evidence. Its documented dependency on WP-1103 remains open. | **OPEN** | Resolve owner handoff while preserving existing files; complete implementation, tests, review, and exact-head gate after WP-1103. |\n| WP-1106 — Single-step loop mode | `--step` and `/step` pause deterministically after one agent turn for operator confirmation. | An independently approved plan exists. Implementation requires `cli/src/agent.ts`, currently claimed by the PR396 agent. | **OPEN** | Obtain file handoff, implement and test the plan, then review and qualify on the integrated head. |\n| WP-1107 — GBNF tool grammar | Generate tool-schema grammars and integrate supported provider paths. | Prototype commit `9cb5f6de` is unintegrated; provider-path integration and validation are missing. | **OPEN** | Integrate providers and demonstrate the roadmap reliability target on supported endpoints; exact-head tests and review. |\n| WP-1108 — Dependency modernization | Triage and integrate the 27 Dependabot updates while meeting the zero-deprecation and compatibility requirements. | Branch `v1/wp-1108-dependency-modernization` is clean at `550112cd`, but has no PR or branch CI. Its triage record still lists integrated CodeQL/dependency scans, runtime compatibility, notice comparisons, package reproducibility, and release artifacts as outstanding. | **PARTIAL / UNQUALIFIED** | Owner/claim alignment; integrated scans and alerts; required test/PTY, `cargo deny`, npm deprecation, CLI compatibility, reproducibility, archive, checksum, SBOM, and installer evidence. |\n\n## Release-gate status\n\n| Gate | Required proof | Current evidence | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G1.1-1 — Zero-leak tracing | Valid OTel GenAI spans for all required turn steps, no credential leakage, and writes confined to the approved trace directory. | WP-1101 prototype lacks runtime wiring and gate evidence. | **OPEN** |\n| G1.1-2 — Dataset decoupling | All benchmark tasks execute and no oracle data reaches candidate prompts; exact candidate and process-scope evidence retained. | Six-task focused acceptance and AC2 focused test exist; the latest full run failed on a non-exact snapshot under concurrent test traffic. | **PARTIAL / UNQUALIFIED** |\n| G1.1-3 — CLI parity | Packaged `nexus eval` works without developer dependencies on the exact release candidate. | Focused installed-candidate evidence exists; final integrated candidate is unverified. | **PARTIAL / UNQUALIFIED** |\n| G1.1-4 — Constrained decoding | At least 99.5% valid tool-call JSON across the supported llama.cpp, vLLM, and Ollama endpoints. | No qualifying cross-endpoint result found. | **OPEN** |\n| G1.1-5 — Zero technical debt | Zero deprecated/unmaintained packages, zero CodeQL alerts and compiler warnings, plus required suite/PTY, cargo-deny, npm scans, reproducibility, and CLI option compatibility without breaking unprivileged sandbox invariants. | WP-1108 branch has no branch CI; integrated scan and qualification evidence remain outstanding. | **OPEN** |\n\n## Exact-candidate release checklist\n\nThe final candidate remains unqualified until each applicable item is recorded against one exact commit and its artifacts:\n\n- All WP-1101–WP-1108 acceptance evidence and independent reviews are complete.\n- Current v1.1.2 roadmap items 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, and 7 are qualified on the exact candidate; item 4 is satisfied only if the superseding PR #398 recovery behavior passes exact-head qualification.\n- The full test suite, type checks, lint/security gates, migration and compatibility checks pass on the exact head.\n- Linux package outputs, checksums, SBOM, installer behavior, and reproducibility are verified for that head.\n- CLI option compatibility is verified without weakening or bypassing unprivileged sandbox invariants.\n- Installed-candidate acceptance covers evaluator isolation, oracle exclusion, provider behavior, and relevant operator scenarios.\n- Independent release acceptance approves the exact candidate and evidence packet.\n- The v1.1.2 tag and public release assets are published only after all prior gates pass.\n\nNo v1.1.2 release, tag, or publication is recorded by this document. Update the status and attach evidence as gates are completed; do not convert a partial or historical result into a release pass.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":895262731}},"started_at_ms":1793659791751,"completed_at_ms":1793659792647}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:49:52.837Z","ordinal":49132,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-281a50fb-0e5e-41f3-bd2c-1874f88dbf7a","process_id":"72482","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,200p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,200p' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md","name":"WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md","path":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# WP-1103: Versioned Dataset Oracle Isolation\n\n## Specification\n\n**User story:** As an evaluation operator, I need versioned datasets to keep task stimulus separate from evaluator assertions, so that benchmark results cannot be inflated by exposing expected answers to the candidate.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **AC1:** For a selected versioned example, the objective reaches the actual candidate prompt/provider-request boundary, while synthetic oracle-only assertion/validator sentinels are absent from the candidate prompt, request, argv, environment, stdin, and other candidate-visible input channels. Tests: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`.\n- **AC2:** The candidate's staged workspace and declared filesystem/mount view expose the task fixture repository but do not expose the dataset task directory or hidden validator files by path or content. Test: `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`.\n- **AC3:** Dataset selection returns exactly the manifest-declared IDs for the requested `regression` or `benchmark` split and rejects unknown/empty splits or task IDs. Tests: `dataset selection returns exactly manifest-declared ids for each split`; `dataset selection refuses unknown ids and invalid splits`.\n- **AC3a:** Loading rejects changes to oracle records or task-tree content after manifest freeze. Tests: `loader rejects oracle data changed after its manifest was frozen`; `loader rejects task data changed after its manifest was frozen`.\n- **AC4:** After the candidate exits, the evaluator can still access the private oracle record and produce the expected score for the synthetic fixture. Test: `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`.\n- **AC5:** Run the exact candidate CLI against a local fake provider that captures the actual request after prompt construction; record one candidate invocation and validator/scorer result for each of the six manifest-declared benchmark task IDs, with zero skipped or missing tasks. Pin the candidate SHA, dataset version/split, and the SHA-256 recomputed from the final integrated `core-v1/manifest.json`; do not reuse the prior branch's `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43` as current evidence. Test/evidence: `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. This establishes execution coverage and request isolation, not model quality.\n\n**Out of scope:** Modifying oracle semantics, held-out corpus data or custody; changing evaluator scoring; packaging the runtime; live inference against a real model/provider. AC5 uses the actual candidate CLI and prompt path with a local deterministic fake provider; the fake provider captures the request and returns a fixture response so the evaluator can score every declared benchmark task.\n\n**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset loader and runner integration; current runner claims are held by root after the prior claim was recorded stale and broken; a test seam for AC1, AC2 and AC4. AC5 requires an integrated exact-candidate benchmark run and is separate from the unit regression suite; packaged installed CLI behavior depends on WP-1104.\n\n**Files claimed/current ownership:** The plan file and `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` are claimed by root on `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. The WP-1103 umbrella claim covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`. Runner claims on the same branch cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and `eval/dataset.test.mjs`; that `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim spans chunks 1 and 2 sequentially. The G1.1-2 evidence is claimed at `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`; write it only after the exact candidate CLI run completes and the final manifest hash is recomputed. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **Reconcile the versioned dataset** — on `origin/main` 593d569b, add tests first for manifest digest/version validation, split selection, task ID rejection, and task/oracle separation; then port the public `core-v1` dataset loader, examples/oracles, task fixtures and docs. Files: `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**`, `eval/dataset.test.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`. Tests: `dataset selection returns exactly manifest-declared ids for each split`; `dataset selection refuses unknown ids and invalid splits`; `loader rejects stimulus data changed after its manifest was frozen`; `loader rejects oracle data changed after its manifest was frozen`; `loader rejects task data changed after its manifest was frozen` in `eval/dataset.test.mjs`.\n2. **Wire and harden the runner** — author failing regressions first for bounded task snapshots, explicit installed executable identity, private config/key files, safe output directory, and post-exit scoring; then implement the runner integrity guard and importable versioned API and integrate it with `eval/run.mjs`. Files: `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, `eval/dataset.test.mjs`. Tests: `per-run versioned snapshot guard preserves the bounded dataset digest`; `importable runner API passes only evaluator config and keeps credentials private`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`. Keep the `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim held across chunks 1 and 2.\n3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\n4. **Run gates on the integrated head** — run evaluator focused tests, TypeScript build/type gate, exact project test suite, process-scope gate, and package/installed qualification on a free `SUITE`; tie every result to the final exact commit and manifest SHA.\n\n**Reference corpora:** `nexus-test` for existing CLI test conventions; `nexus-cli` for subprocess boundary and agent invocation patterns.\n\n**Retrieved references:** `nexus-test` `eval_harness.test.ts:185-211` uses a fake executable on `PATH` and captures spawned arguments/logs without a live provider; `nexus-test` `harness.test.ts:875` exercises refusal before inference. These are test-seam precedents, not proof of the Nexus runner's exact provider request or filesystem mount boundary. XERJ query: `capture spawned child process command arguments in tests without live provider`; second query: `spawnSync mock executable capture process argv and environment in test`.\n\n**Retrieval log (runner API chunk):** `2026-11-02T00:34Z` — corpus `nexus-test`, query `capture spawned child process arguments environment and stdin in tests without live provider`, hit `eval_integrity.test.ts:1220`; contract: test marker paths are passed as argv rather than interpolated into child source, used as a subprocess-test precedent. `2026-11-02T00:34Z` — corpus `nexus-cli`, definition query `agentCommand`, `MISS`; this symbol is local to `eval/run.mjs` and absent from the indexed CLI source, so the adapter was extracted from the current harness implementation and locked by a failing test before the edit.\n\n**Risk / unknown:** The current runner merges example and oracle fields into an evaluator-side task record before launching the candidate. The exact prompt/provider request and candidate filesystem/mount boundary must be observed without a live model; the fake provider/request capture must establish the actual CLI prompt path, and filesystem checks must establish access denial rather than mere omission from the staged copy. The benchmark evidence must identify the exact candidate SHA, dataset version, split, manifest SHA-256, denominator and each task invocation/result.\n\n**Coordination:** The original plan was independently approved by `review_delta` and `release_gate_audit`. The previous runner claim was older than 24 hours, its clean branch was still `c548e53e`, the host had rebooted since the claim, and no process had its worktree as cwd; `.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log` records the stale-claim break at 2026-11-01T21:56Z. Old dataset and runner branches are preserved as read-only reference. Fresh claims now point to `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. Re-review this updated plan before coding. The previous SUITE claim was released after host reboot interrupted its run; claim SUITE before the next suite.\n\n## AC2 plan addendum — actual candidate mount view\n\n**Spec refinement:** AC2 requires evidence from the running dataset candidate's filesystem view, in addition to proving that the staged fixture workspace omits hidden files. The test must show that the candidate can see its declared `/workspace` mount, that the evaluator's dataset staging root is not mounted there, and that the absolute hidden validator path is unreadable.\n\n**Chunk:** Extend the existing `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` subtest in `cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts`. Use the local fake provider to ask the real candidate to execute a read-only `run_command` probe. Capture the command's stdout and assert all three mount/path outcomes, while retaining the existing relative-path and sentinel assertions. No production sandbox change is planned unless the probe exposes a real leak.\n\n**Reference retrieval:** XERJ `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:183` (`probeBwrapSandbox`) demonstrates probing a real Bubblewrap process against an outside canary; `nexus-cli/tools.ts:1523` locates the production `run_command` wrapper, and `nexus-cli/sandbox.ts:219` provides the `wrapSandboxedCommand` signature. `eval/isolate.mjs` is outside the indexed CLI source; local source inspection at `agentSandboxArgv` confirmed the evaluator mounts `/tmp` as tmpfs and binds the candidate workspace at `/workspace`.\n\n**Observed TDD:** The first focused run failed because the assertion matched the literal readable branch in the captured command rather than its stdout. The test was corrected to parse the `run_command` result. The focused dataset test then passed 3/3, with workspace mount present, dataset root mount absent, and the absolute validator path unreadable. This change adds dataset-specific acceptance evidence; it does not change production sandbox code.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":31899152}},"started_at_ms":1793659791801,"completed_at_ms":1793659792834}}
