{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:50:23.903Z","ordinal":49178,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19e74-e71f-7b73-8501-6911e25f9c87","call_id":"call_88a1da2f27294b16beba5146f860ebe8","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 1\n M cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs\n M cli/src/index.ts\n M docs/releases/v1.1.2-rc.1.md\n M docs/releases/v1.1.2.md\n M docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md\n M eval/README.md\n M eval/run.mjs\n M scripts/package-linux.sh\n?? cli/src/eval_cli.ts\n?? cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts\n?? cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts\n?? docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md\n?? docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\n?? docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md\n?? eval/dataset.mjs\n?? eval/dataset.test.mjs\n?? eval/datasets/\n?? eval/package_runtime.test.mjs\n?? eval/runner_api.mjs\n?? eval/runner_integrity.mjs\n?? scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs\nbae2a5b6c3472ab2dbcbb446867adc2c0a2ddc6fe2e25b7753e3be340fa85cb0  /tmp/v112-wp1103-a0d374e8-npm-test-final.log\n5ecdd84e573c2c6ee0c7cda6c038b6a4043ad002ec7a004cceaef3dceb67320e  /tmp/v112-eval-focused.log\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 2\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"RESULT 3\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 5348)\nTotal output lines: 103\n\n# WP-1104: Standalone `nexus eval` command\n\n## Specification\n\n**User story:** As a Nexus operator, I need to run a versioned evaluation dataset through the installed Nexus executable and receive a structured score file, so that I can compare candidate builds reproducibly without depending on the source checkout.\n\n**Acceptance criteria:**\n\n- **AC1:** `nexus eval --help` exposes `--dataset`, `--split`, `--runs`, `--isolated-home`, and `--output`. Test: `eval CLI help exposes versioned dataset options`.\n- **AC2:** A packaged candidate resolves and executes the installed CLI dispatch, runner, and scorer from its package closure when launched outside the source checkout, without inference for an empty benchmark split. Test: `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout`.\n- **AC3:** A versioned dataset run rejects unsupported `--limit` before creating the output directory or starting the runner; help states that `--limit` applies only to legacy runs. Test: `versioned eval rejects limit before runner or output creation`.\n- **AC4:** An exact installed candidate run executes the six unique public benchmark tasks with no skips or missing tasks and records the binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA. Test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`.\n- **AC5:** Existing legacy dataset invocation and `--limit` behavior remain compatible. Test: `legacy eval invocation and limit remain supported`.\n\n**Out of scope:** Adding evaluator kinds, changing the public dataset schema, changing legacy scoring, or publishing/tagging a release.\n\n**Dependencies:** WP-1103 versioned dataset and runner foundation at `6adbeb31` and `00a8cb4d` on this branch. WP-1102 is not a functional dependency. WP-1108 is not imported as a branch; package changes will be based on the selected current package script and separately checked against its ownership and gate state.\n\n**Files claimed:** `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md`, and all paths in the accepted WP-1103 commits being integrated.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. **CLI grammar and compatibility** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`; tests: `eval CLI help exposes versioned dataset options`, `legacy eval invocation and limit remain supported`. Write tests first, verify expected RED, then port the CLI implementation.\n2. **Versioned argument validation** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`; test: `versioned eval rejects limit before runner or output creation`. Preserve existing runner and filesystem behavior outside this acceptance criterion.\n3. **Versioned runtime dispatch and packaged closure** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`; tests: `versioned eval invokes resolved installed runner`, `evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files`, `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout`. First verify resolver/dispatch with a synthetic package; verify the staged allowlist excludes datasets/oracles; then build and stage the actual package and invoke the installed CLI outside the checkout against an empty benchmark split, exercising the real runner and scorer subprocesses without inference. Reconcile package allowlist changes against the current script rather than replaying historical packaging commits.\n4. **Installed candidate acceptance** — files: `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts` and the WP-1103 acceptance evidence path when claimed; test: `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`. Require six unique manifest IDs, an invocation and validator result for each, zero skips/missing, candidate binary SHA, split, and recomputed manifest SHA.\n\n**Reference corpora:** `nexus-cli` for Commander registration and CLI command dispatch; `nexus-test` for CLI command test patterns; `nexus-wp1104-reference` for the prior WP-1104 resolver and runtime behavior; `nexus-docs` for evaluation acceptance and dataset contracts.\n\n**Risk / unknowns:** The current package script must contain the evaluator closure needed by WP-1105. Retrieval query: \"which evaluator modules are copied into the Linux package and how are runtime paths resolved?\" The installed artifact test is the acceptance gate for this boundary.\n\n## Base and claim state at plan review\n\n- Selected source base: `origin/main` = `593d569b5aa2a43d1b31138d37e90b8b65ffcbe7`.\n- Current package script blob at that base: `5f410376b1c167fa6422ea912d8e69e92ccb8972`.\n- `scripts/package-linux.sh` claim was free before this slice took its claim.\n- WP-1108 triage at `v1/wp-1108-dependency-modernization` says its added CI job has not run at that branch head and its policy batch is not accepted; no WP-1108 packaging changes are treated as a qualified prerequisite.\n- Plan review: approved after narrowing dependencies, adding RED-first named tests, and requiring real package execution outside the checkout.\n\n## Retrieval log\n\n- 2026-11-02 08:24 UTC — corpus `nexus-test`; query: `HTTP server listen loopback capture chat completion request SSE tool_calls spawn installed CLI candidate integration test`; hit `eval_integrity.test.ts:1729` and `eval_harness.test.ts:43`; the retrieved passages show the SSE tool-call framing and deterministic task-response pattern used by the local fake provider.\n- 2026-11-02 08:33 UTC — corpus `nexus-test`; query: `runtimeMountProblem rejects protected runtime root /tmp allowedRoots forbidden runtime root`; hit `eval_integrity.test.ts:1532`; contract: runtime allowlist roots must be outside protected roots such as `/tmp`. `xerj def \"runtimeMountProblem\" --prefix nexus-test` returned MISS; verified the current implementation directly in `eval/isolate.mjs` before changing the acceptance harness install location.\n\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-cli`; query: \"Commander CLI command registration subcommand options action parse\"; hit `index.ts:2`; Commander import and command registration context informed the planned integration seam.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-cli`; definition lookup `createCommand`; MISS. No eval-specific API was derived from this lookup.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-cli`; query: \"registerOperationCommands program.command run resume status options action\"; hit `operation_cli.ts:230`; retrieved the `Command` parameter and chained `.command(...).option(...).action(...)` registration pattern.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-test`; query: \"CLI parser help assert spawnSync process execPath test\"; hit `cli_option_scope.test.ts:29`; retrieved the real CLI invocation/help assertion pattern.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"parseEvalRuns and validate versioned dataset options runVersionedEvalCommand\"; hit `eval_cli.ts:254`; the prior runner validates required dataset and rejects versioned `--limit` before resolving the installed runner or creating output.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"resolveInstalledEvalRuntime NEXUS_HOME packageRoot runnerApiPath installed executable path\"; hit `eval_cli.ts:228`; installed resolver uses `NEXUS_HOME`, canonicalizes the launcher/runtime paths, checks package confinement and executable status.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"isolateEvalCommandHome HOME XDG eval command startup before provider config\"; hit `eval_cli.ts:160`; isolated HOME and XDG paths are set before launcher configuration/startup.\n- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-reference`; query: \"resolveInstalledEvalRuntime NEXUS_HOME packageRoot runnerApiPath installed executable path\"; definition hit `eval_cli.ts:22…1348 tokens truncated…310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in candidate-specific `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json`. The earlier generic `acceptance.json` is retained unchanged as superseded evidence; the test writes candidate evidence exclusively and rejects relative `hidden/...` command paths as well as full hidden validator commands in captured requests. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\n- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\n\n## Gate attempt notes\n\n- **Global release-scope guard:** Current `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still defines v1.1.2 as a patch on v1.1.1 containing one operation-message fix and inheriting v1.1.1 qualification. `docs/v1.1.0/README.md` also says WP-11xx is not implemented in its described release. This conflicts with the user's direction to complete the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap in v1.1.2. The release definition, integrated branch, qualification and candidate must be reconciled to the full roadmap before any v1.1.2 publication; this WP slice does not change the release notes or release branch.\n- **Cross-slice audit (2026-11-02, independent read-only agents):** WP-1101 (`8a83c9e7`) has an unintegrated recorder prototype without runtime event wiring or branch-head gate evidence; WP-1102 (`ee7c8b1e`) has partial redaction work with operator acceptance pending; WP-1103 dataset/runner branches (`e430dab5`, `c548e53e`) have no PR, and required actual provider-request isolation, filesystem/mount denial, post-exit oracle scoring, and six-task G1.1-2 evidence are absent. WP-1105 has no implementation delta, WP-1106 has no branch or implementation, WP-1107 (`9cb5f6de`) is an unintegrated grammar generator prototype without provider-path integration, and WP-1108 (`550112cd`) is a partial modernization policy batch without branch-head gate evidence. None is release-qualified. These are audit leads; revalidate on the integrated exact head before marking any tracker item done.\n\n## Gate update — 2026-11-02\n\nThe notes above describe intermediate attempts and are superseded where they conflict with this gate update. After correcting the relative hidden-command checks and making evidence creation exclusive and candidate-specific, independent review by `/root/review_delta` returned **APPROVED** for the WP-1103/1104 source and six-task evidence. The reviewer did not rerun tests.\n\nThe final synchronized full-suite run completed with **2,138 tests, 2,136 passed, 0 failed, and 2 skipped**. The terminal process-scope postcheck reported `scope measurement fixtures passed`. Log: `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot/wp1104-suite-final-ac4.log`; SHA-256: `19aeb576f3be4f45b7507d79a0a1cfda1a46e9caebca59f87de9e60b17bf5a16`. The modified source and test files were byte-for-byte matched against the suite snapshot. `npm run build` passed on the integration worktree. The full-suite and process-scope claim was released after all test processes exited.\n\nInstalled-candidate evidence is recorded in `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e-suite.json` for package archive SHA-256 `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. It records all six benchmark tasks and captured requests, with no missing or skipped task. The loopback deterministic provider does not establish model quality: its task-completion responses are not solutions, and hidden checks are recorded false. This is dataset execution and request-isolation evidence only. Per the 2026-11-02 coordinator ruling, this mock-only acceptance does not consume the GATEWAY claim; any remote/provider-backed inference still requires that claim.\n\nThis gate closes the WP-1103/1104 source slice only. It does not qualify a tagged release artifact or satisfy the full WP-1101..WP-1108 roadmap. `docs/releases/v1.1.2.md` still describes a narrower patch and must be reconciled with the user's full-roadmap scope before publication. The built archive predates the source commit and does not carry an explicit source-commit binding; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\n\n### WP-1104 tracker closeout\n\n- **Status:** done for the standalone CLI, package runtime closure, and six-task dataset execution acceptance delivered by this slice.\n- **Commit:** `05c49df2` (`feat(eval): package and run the versioned evaluator`).\n- **Test evidence:** `npm test` completed with 2,138 tests, 2,136 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped; process-scope postcheck passed. Log SHA-256: `19aeb576f3be4f45b7507d79a0a1cfda1a46e9caebca59f87de9e60b17bf5a16`.\n- **Type/build gate:** `npm run build` passed on the committed source tree.\n- **Independent review:** `/root/review_delta` returned **APPROVED** for commit `05c49df2`, including the gate record and candidate evidence; reviewer did not rerun the suite.\n- **Retrieval log:** XERJ entries above, including `nexus-test/eval_integrity.test.ts:1729` and `nexus-test/eval_harness.test.ts:43`.\n- **Release qualification boundary:** this tracker closeout is not exact-tag or publication approval; retain the full-roadmap and release-scope guards above.\n\n- A first `npm test` run on `/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-wp1104-suite-snapshot` was diagnostic only: the snapshot had no `cli/dist/index.js` or Rust core binaries, and `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` was unset so the actual package smoke was skipped. Its test runner reported 1,981 tests (1,739 pass, 222 fail) and then remained in `turn_semantics.test.ts` with repeated provider-recovery retries; that process was interrupted after about 40 minutes. This is not accepted full-suite evidence.\n- Snapshot prerequisites are now built: `npm run build` and debug `cargo build --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui` passed. Release core binaries were copied from the successful pinned Bookworm package build, whose Rust sources are unchanged by this WP-1104 slice.\n- A separate focused test process in `/home/mike/nexus-wt/pr398-review` remains active. The next full-suite attempt must wait for it to finish, then set `NEXUS_PACKAGE_ROOT` to the freshly extracted development package so the actual outside-checkout runtime test runs instead of skipping.\n- After peer review identified that the former empty-dataset `--limit 0` case did not prove truncation, the legacy compatibility test was strengthened to a non-empty two-task fixture and async local OpenAI-compatible mock. The first mock response format caused an expected transport failure; the second run timed out because the evaluator used the repository as its workspace and discovered the repository test command. Both causes were corrected. Current targeted TypeScript no-emit and `git diff --check` pass, and the updated focused suite passes 7/7.\n- AC4 can use the deterministic local fake provider and payload capture specified in `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md`; no public provider is needed for the dataset-isolation acceptance. The release concurrency plan still requires the serial `GATEWAY` claim for evaluator runs. That claim is held by `codex-root` on `ubuntu-desktop` for RC15 E5 provider verification (since 2026-10-31T09:47Z, no PID). This host is `mike-dev`, has a different boot ID, and has no matching process; the claimed worktree remains with untracked RC15 evidence. A handoff/stale determination is not supportable locally, so a conflict/handoff request was appended to the shared claim log and the claim/worktree remain untouched.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793659823.9032714}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
