{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:50:56.490Z","ordinal":49226,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19e75-666a-7812-b2cb-cd1874516233","call_id":"call_205ba073fb4242c4978a6a7e2883286b","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Your canonical to-do list and working state for this project, kept across sessions: whatever is still open is shown at the start of every session. Each call appends one entry to a list. To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...details}. State on the list itself: any other fields (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list). Returns what is still open in the list. Params: list (required), fields (required). This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__work_state_write(args: {\n  // Keys to set. Include \"task\" to update a to-do item. Values are strings, numbers, booleans, or null to clear a key.\n  fields: { [key: string]: string | number | boolean | null; };\n  // The to-do list or tracked thing this entry belongs to, e.g. \"release\" or \"auth-refactor\"\n  list: string;\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\n```"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793659856.4907978}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
