{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:51:08.465Z","ordinal":49237,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-329a3e9b-3ea7-474a-9003-a34c96717f20","process_id":"4369","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'NEXUS_PACKAGE_ARCHIVE|package-linux.sh|Bookworm|package.*rc.1' docs/v1.1.0 docs/releases scripts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'NEXUS_PACKAGE_ARCHIVE|package-linux.sh|Bookworm|package.*rc.1' docs/v1.1.0 docs/releases scripts","query":"NEXUS_PACKAGE_ARCHIVE|package-linux.sh|Bookworm|package.*rc.1","path":"v1.1.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"scripts/package-linux.sh:16:VERSION=${1:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:17:OUT=${2:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:22:    echo \"NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE must use the approved digest-pinned Rust 1.95 Bookworm builder (set NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1 only for local development)\" >&2\nscripts/package-linux.sh:26:  echo \"NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE must use the approved digest-pinned Rust 1.95 Bookworm builder\" >&2\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md:7:This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It replaces RC12 and RC13, which were tagged but never published: both release workflows failed in the test step, so neither package exists. RC14 ships the same product changes as RC12; everything in the [RC13](v1.0.0-rc.13.md), [RC12](v1.0.0-rc.12.md) and [RC11](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) notes is included.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.13.md:7:This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It replaces RC12, which was tagged but never published: its release workflow failed in the test step, so no RC12 package exists. RC13 ships the same product changes as RC12; everything in the [RC12 notes](v1.0.0-rc.12.md) and the [RC11 notes](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) is included.\nscripts/repro-identity.mjs:23:  if (process.env.NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE !== APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE) fail(\"Rust build image is not the approved digest-pinned Bookworm builder\");\nscripts/repro-identity.mjs:38:  const reviewedPackageScript = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"show\", `${packageToolCommit}:scripts/package-linux.sh`], { encoding: \"utf8\" });\nscripts/repro-identity.mjs:74:  if (buildImages.some((image) => image !== APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE)) fail(\"every builder must use the approved digest-pinned Bookworm Rust build image\");\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:20:# 1. Generate Rust SBOM for the exact platform shipped by package-linux.sh.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.12.md:5:**Not published:** the `v1.0.0-rc.12` release workflow failed in its test step, so no RC12 package exists. [RC13](v1.0.0-rc.13.md) replaces it with the same product changes.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.12.md:9:This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It supersedes RC11 because a power-loss test found that an interrupted upgrade could leave the installation unable to start. Everything in the [RC11 notes](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) is included.\ndocs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md:17:PR #374 (`bed30a90`). CI matrices (Node 22, 24), dual container packaging (`package-linux.sh`), bit-for-bit\ndocs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md:114:| Packaging (`package-linux.sh` ×2), SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, `installer-smoke.sh` | not run |\ndocs/v1.1.0/VALIDATION.md:34:| G1h | Packaging | `bash scripts/package-linux.sh` twice + byte comparison | identical tarball, `SHA256SUMS`, notices, SBOM, installer |\ndocs/v1.1.0/VALIDATION.md:135:| 2 | Version bump to `1.1.0-rc.1` (`package.json` only, then `sync-version.mjs`); `docs/releases/v1.1.0-rc.1.md`; CHANGELOG section | `sync-version --check --tag v1.1.0-rc.1` |\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:19:**Files claimed:** `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md`, and all paths in the accepted WP-1103 commits being integrated.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:25:3. **Versioned runtime dispatch and packaged closure** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`; tests: `versioned eval invokes resolved installed runner`, `evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files`, `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout`. First verify resolver/dispatch with a synthetic package; verify the staged allowlist excludes datasets/oracles; then build and stage the actual package and invoke the installed CLI outside the checkout against an empty benchmark split, exercising the real runner and scorer subprocesses without inference. Reconcile package allowlist changes against the current script rather than replaying historical packaging commits.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:36:- `scripts/package-linux.sh` claim was free before this slice took its claim.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:53:- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-package-reference`; query: \"package-linux.sh evaluator runtime allowlist copy eval run.mjs\"; hit `package-linux.sh:73`; retrieved the explicit runtime closure and exclusions for datasets, tests and held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:66:- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:71:- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in candidate-specific `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json`. The earlier generic `acceptance.json` is retained unchanged as superseded evidence; the test writes candidate evidence exclusively and rejects relative `hidden/...` command paths as well as full hidden validator commands in captured requests. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:100:- Snapshot prerequisites are now built: `npm run build` and debug `cargo build --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui` passed. Release core binaries were copied from the successful pinned Bookworm package build, whose Rust sources are unchanged by this WP-1104 slice.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":646454128}},"started_at_ms":1793659867818,"completed_at_ms":1793659868464}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:51:09.648Z","ordinal":49238,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19e75-99d0-7c33-8a13-e598d8f2989d","call_id":"call_4d2e0ea3912a461286daa894f6a0aa93","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"scripts/package-linux.sh:16:VERSION=${1:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:17:OUT=${2:?usage: package-linux.sh VERSION OUTPUT_DIR}\nscripts/package-linux.sh:22:    echo \"NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE must use the approved digest-pinned Rust 1.95 Bookworm builder (set NEXUS_ALLOW_HOST_RUST_BUILD=1 only for local development)\" >&2\nscripts/package-linux.sh:26:  echo \"NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE must use the approved digest-pinned Rust 1.95 Bookworm builder\" >&2\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.14.md:7:This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It replaces RC12 and RC13, which were tagged but never published: both release workflows failed in the test step, so neither package exists. RC14 ships the same product changes as RC12; everything in the [RC13](v1.0.0-rc.13.md), [RC12](v1.0.0-rc.12.md) and [RC11](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) notes is included.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.13.md:7:This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It replaces RC12, which was tagged but never published: its release workflow failed in the test step, so no RC12 package exists. RC13 ships the same product changes as RC12; everything in the [RC12 notes](v1.0.0-rc.12.md) and the [RC11 notes](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) is included.\nscripts/repro-identity.mjs:23:  if (process.env.NEXUS_BUILD_CONTAINER_IMAGE !== APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE) fail(\"Rust build image is not the approved digest-pinned Bookworm builder\");\nscripts/repro-identity.mjs:38:  const reviewedPackageScript = execFileSync(\"git\", [\"show\", `${packageToolCommit}:scripts/package-linux.sh`], { encoding: \"utf8\" });\nscripts/repro-identity.mjs:74:  if (buildImages.some((image) => image !== APPROVED_RUST_BUILD_IMAGE)) fail(\"every builder must use the approved digest-pinned Bookworm Rust build image\");\nscripts/generate_sbom.sh:20:# 1. Generate Rust SBOM for the exact platform shipped by package-linux.sh.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.12.md:5:**Not published:** the `v1.0.0-rc.12` release workflow failed in its test step, so no RC12 package exists. [RC13](v1.0.0-rc.13.md) replaces it with the same product changes.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.12.md:9:This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It supersedes RC11 because a power-loss test found that an interrupted upgrade could leave the installation unable to start. Everything in the [RC11 notes](v1.0.0-rc.11.md) is included.\ndocs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md:17:PR #374 (`bed30a90`). CI matrices (Node 22, 24), dual container packaging (`package-linux.sh`), bit-for-bit\ndocs/v1.1.0/STATUS.md:114:| Packaging (`package-linux.sh` ×2), SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, `installer-smoke.sh` | not run |\ndocs/v1.1.0/VALIDATION.md:34:| G1h | Packaging | `bash scripts/package-linux.sh` twice + byte comparison | identical tarball, `SHA256SUMS`, notices, SBOM, installer |\ndocs/v1.1.0/VALIDATION.md:135:| 2 | Version bump to `1.1.0-rc.1` (`package.json` only, then `sync-version.mjs`); `docs/releases/v1.1.0-rc.1.md`; CHANGELOG section | `sync-version --check --tag v1.1.0-rc.1` |\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:19:**Files claimed:** `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md`, and all paths in the accepted WP-1103 commits being integrated.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:25:3. **Versioned runtime dispatch and packaged closure** — files: `cli/src/eval_cli.ts`, `cli/src/index.ts`, `cli/test/eval_cli.test.ts`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/README.md`, `eval/package_runtime.test.mjs`, `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs`, `scripts/stage_eval_runtime.mjs`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`; tests: `versioned eval invokes resolved installed runner`, `evaluator runtime allowlist copies only runtime files`, `packaged evaluator runtime executes outside checkout`. First verify resolver/dispatch with a synthetic package; verify the staged allowlist excludes datasets/oracles; then build and stage the actual package and invoke the installed CLI outside the checkout against an empty benchmark split, exercising the real runner and scorer subprocesses without inference. Reconcile package allowlist changes against the current script rather than replaying historical packaging commits.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:36:- `scripts/package-linux.sh` claim was free before this slice took its claim.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:53:- 2026-11-02 — corpus `nexus-wp1104-package-reference`; query: \"package-linux.sh evaluator runtime allowlist copy eval run.mjs\"; hit `package-linux.sh:73`; retrieved the explicit runtime closure and exclusions for datasets, tests and held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:66:- **GREEN:** Pinned Bookworm package build completed; after extraction outside the checkout, `node --test eval/package_runtime.test.mjs` passed 3/3 with the actual installed `nexus eval` CLI, runner, and scorer. The rebuilt development artifact is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.1.2-rc.1.tar.gz`; it is not exact-commit release evidence.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:71:- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in candidate-specific `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json`. The earlier generic `acceptance.json` is retained unchanged as superseded evidence; the test writes candidate evidence exclusively and rejects relative `hidden/...` command paths as well as full hidden validator commands in captured requests. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:100:- Snapshot prerequisites are now built: `npm run build` and debug `cargo build --locked --manifest-path core/Cargo.toml --bin harness-core --bin nexus-tui` passed. Release core binaries were copied from the successful pinned Bookworm package build, whose Rust sources are unchanged by this WP-1104 slice.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793659869.6486921}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
