{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T22:54:16.607Z","ordinal":49315,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a19e78-741d-7eb2-b733-646ce6af408a","author":"/root/review_delta","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/review_delta\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED** for the AC2 evidence assertion; I found no separate WP-1104 runtime or packaging blocker in the source reviewed.\n\nAt [eval_dataset.test.ts:39](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/cli/test/eval_dataset.test.ts:39), the mount probe searches for the exact dataset root followed by a space. A mount sourced from a descendant such as `dataset/tasks/...` can miss that match, while the absolute-path probe checks only the original validator path. That leaves an alias mount exposure untested. The runner’s current protected-path overlap guard appears to reject such mounts, so I found no current leak; please make the probe detect mounts rooted anywhere under the dataset tree.\n\nThe qualification record should also make the latest skipped acceptance unmistakable. At [v1.1.2-qualification.md:27](/home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/releases/v1.1.2-qualification.md:27), “GATE PASS” is broader than the evidence when the six-task installed-package test was skipped; line 39 correctly keeps G1.1-2 **PARTIAL / UNQUALIFIED**. Narrow the WP-1103 label to the source-test gate and state that installed acceptance was skipped. Likewise, identify the prior `b385cd…` acceptance as historical rather than current candidate proof.\n\nI did not run tests. The latest exact-candidate full-suite result is not a release-qualification pass, and installed acceptance remains pending."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793660056.6058288,"content_item_metadata":[{"provenance":{"type":"tool","namespace":"collaboration"}}]}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":2039}}
