{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T23:01:26.420Z","ordinal":49607,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","session_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","root_turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","response_id":"resp_0fd4138577b17921016ae9163db05481a39e55e134e4517388","usage":{"input_tokens":126630,"cached_input_tokens":120576,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1203,"reasoning_output_tokens":1096,"total_tokens":127833},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":101161839,"cached_input_tokens":100243200,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":166947,"reasoning_output_tokens":80092,"total_tokens":101328786},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":963573568,"cached_input_tokens":955405824,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1983135,"reasoning_output_tokens":1005263,"total_tokens":965556703}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T23:01:28.428Z","ordinal":49608,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a192c0-f277-7f60-8574-21ce71edb8c2","turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-68540fb2-bd86-4282-83b2-ed4a579f94cd","process_id":"8995","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'acceptance\\.json|acceptance-b385|candidate-specific|file claim' docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n \"acceptance\\\\.json|acceptance-b385|candidate-specific|file claim\" docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md","query":"acceptance\\.json|acceptance-b385|candidate-specific|file claim","path":"WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:71:- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in candidate-specific `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json`. The earlier generic `acceptance.json` is retained unchanged as superseded evidence; the test writes candidate evidence exclusively and rejects relative `hidden/...` command paths as well as full hidden validator commands in captured requests. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:72:- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:81:The notes above describe intermediate attempts and are superseded where they conflict with this gate update. After correcting the relative hidden-command checks and making evidence creation exclusive and candidate-specific, independent review by `/root/review_delta` returned **APPROVED** for the WP-1103/1104 source and six-task evidence. The reviewer did not rerun tests.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:85:Installed-candidate evidence is recorded in `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e-suite.json` for package archive SHA-256 `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. It records all six benchmark tasks and captured requests, with no missing or skipped task. The loopback deterministic provider does not establish model quality: its task-completion responses are not solutions, and hidden checks are recorded false. This is dataset execution and request-isolation evidence only. Per the 2026-11-02 coordinator ruling, this mock-only acceptance does not consume the GATEWAY claim; any remote/provider-backed inference still requires that claim.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:20:**Files claimed/current ownership:** The plan file and `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` are claimed by root on `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. The WP-1103 umbrella claim covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`. Runner claims on the same branch cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and `eval/dataset.test.mjs`; that `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim spans chunks 1 and 2 sequentially. The G1.1-2 evidence is claimed at `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`; write it only after the exact candidate CLI run completes and the final manifest hash is recomputed. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:26:3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":698068630}},"started_at_ms":1793660487729,"completed_at_ms":1793660488428}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T23:01:29.601Z","ordinal":49609,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19e7f-0f81-7ad3-b928-9e10bf252a24","call_id":"call_eb5ceac995f040d49ef5956beece9321","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:71:- **Six-task installed-candidate acceptance (2026-11-02):** The new `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance` acceptance test first failed with the expected missing-evidence assertion. A diagnostic run also confirmed that extracting an installed runtime below `/tmp` is rejected by the existing runtime root policy, so the test now extracts the archive into a fresh safe worktree path outside `/tmp` and the source checkout. A pinned Bookworm package was built from this integration worktree and its exact installed `bin/nexus` ran the `core-v1` benchmark split through a loopback deterministic fake provider. Focused test passed: 6/6 task invocations, 6 captured requests, no skipped or missing tasks, recomputed manifest SHA `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`; archive SHA `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. Per-task hidden/regression validator and scorer outputs are retained in candidate-specific `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e.json`. The earlier generic `acceptance.json` is retained unchanged as superseded evidence; the test writes candidate evidence exclusively and rejects relative `hidden/...` command paths as well as full hidden validator commands in captured requests. This acceptance establishes execution coverage and request capture only; the deterministic `task_completed` fixture does not establish model quality, and its expected hidden checks are recorded as false.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:72:- **Independent review:** Initial re-review returned `REQUEST_CHANGES` to close WP-1103/1104 because six-task installed-candidate evidence was absent. Review of the first evidence found the relative hidden-command assertion too weak and the evidence write non-exclusive; both findings were addressed and the focused acceptance test passed again with candidate-specific evidence. Fresh full-slice re-review is pending.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:81:The notes above describe intermediate attempts and are superseded where they conflict with this gate update. After correcting the relative hidden-command checks and making evidence creation exclusive and candidate-specific, independent review by `/root/review_delta` returned **APPROVED** for the WP-1103/1104 source and six-task evidence. The reviewer did not rerun tests.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1104-PLAN.md:85:Installed-candidate evidence is recorded in `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-b385cd533f9e-suite.json` for package archive SHA-256 `b385cd533f9e14bb161dba9a352d310acf067d756c8982413970b5999db1432a`. It records all six benchmark tasks and captured requests, with no missing or skipped task. The loopback deterministic provider does not establish model quality: its task-completion responses are not solutions, and hidden checks are recorded false. This is dataset execution and request-isolation evidence only. Per the 2026-11-02 coordinator ruling, this mock-only acceptance does not consume the GATEWAY claim; any remote/provider-backed inference still requires that claim.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:20:**Files claimed/current ownership:** The plan file and `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` are claimed by root on `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. The WP-1103 umbrella claim covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`. Runner claims on the same branch cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and `eval/dataset.test.mjs`; that `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim spans chunks 1 and 2 sequentially. The G1.1-2 evidence is claimed at `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`; write it only after the exact candidate CLI run completes and the final manifest hash is recomputed. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\ndocs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md:26:3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793660489.6013298}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fall