{"timestamp":"2026-11-02T23:01:40.882Z","ordinal":49613,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0fd4138577b17921016ae9164cc17881a3a311e1287be3bb6c","status":"completed","call_id":"call_684481d35df6405fb6a1fc90d2ef177a","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/v112-integrated-exact/docs/v1.1.0/WP-1103-ORACLE-ISOLATION.md\\n@@\\n-**Files claimed/current ownership:** The plan file and `cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs` are claimed by root on `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. The WP-1103 umbrella claim covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`. Runner claims on the same branch cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and `eval/dataset.test.mjs`; that `eval/dataset.test.mjs` claim spans chunks 1 and 2 sequentially. The G1.1-2 evidence is claimed at `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`; write it only after the exact candidate CLI run completes and the final manifest hash is recomputed. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\\n+**Files claimed/current ownership:** The WP-1103 and WP-1104 integration claims are held by root on `v1/v112-integrated-exact`, based on `a0d374e8`. The WP-1103 umbrella covers `eval/dataset.mjs`, `eval/datasets/core-v1/**` (public development tasks only), `eval/README.md`, and `docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-EVALUATION.md`; runner claims cover `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/runner_api.mjs`, `eval/runner_integrity.mjs`, and the dataset tests. The current candidate-specific G1.1-2 evidence is `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-27dbbb8120e7.json`; earlier generic and `b385cd…` records are retained as historical and are not current-candidate proof. Do not edit, index, or expose held-out payloads.\\n@@\\n-3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Then run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips, recording candidate SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, request capture and validator/scorer result in the claimed `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance.json`. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `versioned benchmark acceptance records complete manifest coverage`. Requires the installed candidate and package closure from WP-1104; this is the G1.1-2 evidence run, not a unit-test substitute.\\n+3. **Prove candidate isolation and complete coverage** — use the actual candidate CLI path with a deterministic local fake provider that captures the request after prompt construction. Separately intercept and record the exact `{command, argv, env}` launch payload handed to the sandbox wrapper, and inspect the sandbox payload/stdin at that boundary. Assert the objective appears in the expected argv and captured provider request; the sentinel is absent from serialized argv/environment/stdin; and credentials stay evaluator-side except the intended local proxy token. Keep filesystem/mount checks in the separate `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files` test. Score with evaluator-held oracles after candidate exit. Run every manifest-declared benchmark ID with no skips and record candidate archive SHA, dataset/split, recomputed manifest hash, captured-request digests and validator/scorer results in a new candidate-specific evidence file. Do not overwrite prior evidence. Tests/evidence: `versioned dataset candidate receives stimulus without oracle sentinels`; `candidate launch envelope contains stimulus but no oracle data in argv env or stdin`; `versioned dataset candidate workspace excludes evaluator files`; `versioned dataset oracle scores after candidate exit`; `installed candidate runs all public benchmark tasks with provenance`. This is G1.1-2 execution/isolation evidence, not a model-quality test or release gate substitute.\\n@@\\n **Coordination:** The original plan was independently approved by `review_delta` and `release_gate_audit`. The previous runner claim was older than 24 hours, its clean branch was still `c548e53e`, the host had rebooted since the claim, and no process had its worktree as cwd; `.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log` records the stale-claim break at 2026-11-01T21:56Z. Old dataset and runner branches are preserved as read-only reference. Fresh claims now point to `v1/v112-wp1103-runner-reclaim` at `origin/main` 593d569b. Re-review this updated plan before coding. The previous SUITE claim was released after host reboot interrupted its run; claim SUITE before the next suite.\\n+\\n+## Current candidate update — 2026-11-02\\n+\\n+- The pinned Bookworm package archive SHA-256 `27dbbb8120e755061e92218eaceb5e12b7d9457230b9b0aa82b96d28cc3791ee` passed six-task installed acceptance. The candidate-specific record is `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/wp-1103-g1.1-2/acceptance-27dbbb8120e7.json`; the manifest digest was recomputed as `05ee2fa33ae5f6d6afc35df2e003c913de3f7bf0f817d2f76c709c16fb640d43`. All six declared benchmark IDs were invoked once, six requests were captured, and no task was missing or skipped. Deterministic task-completion responses did not solve the tasks; hidden checks are false, so this evidence is not a quality claim.\\n+- The complete CLI suite passed 2,251 tests with 2,246 pass, 0 fail and 5 skips; the six-task acceptance was among the skips because its explicit package/evidence environment variables were not set. Separate package acceptance above is the six-task evidence. The process-scope fixture postcheck passed.\\n+- Peer review requested that the AC2 mount probe detect nested dataset-source mounts. The probe now checks mountinfo's root field for the exact dataset root and slash-delimited descendants. Focused dataset test passed 3/3 after the change, and `/root/review_delta` approved the updated source diff. Final commit-bound gate evidence remains open.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a19de1-2f43-7663-a2d9-f17adf8cb101","create_time":1793660492.7567606}}}
